/* Generated by tools/build_content.py - original study content, one unit per textbook lesson. */
window.HY_LESSONS = [{"n":1,"zh":"爱的细节","en":"Details of Love","book":1,"theme":"Affection in long relationships shows up as small, repeated habits rather than speeches.","grammar":{"id":"g01","point":"不是……而是……","point_en":"not A, but B","structure":"不是 + A + 而是 + B","explain_en":"This pattern corrects a wrong assumption. The speaker first names what something is not, then supplies what it actually is. Use it when the listener probably has the wrong idea, or when you want to sharpen a contrast you have just suggested. The 不是 half is usually short, and 而是 must come in the same clause with the real answer. The two halves are balanced, so the words either side of the pair normally share the same shape: noun with noun, verb with verb, clause with clause. It differs from 不是……就是……, which offers two genuine options; here one option is rejected and the other is asserted. It also differs from 不但……而且……, which adds information instead of replacing it. Word order is fixed, 不是 first, 而是 second, and the whole pair usually follows the subject: 他 不是 忘了，而是 没听见. If the subject would be long, repeat a short pronoun in the second half instead of stretching one subject across both halves. The pattern often opens a sentence with 真正的 or 真正的问题, because its job is to redraw the definition before giving a conclusion.","common_mistake":"Learners write 不是……但是…… or drop 是 from the second half (不是他，而他不来). Keep 是 in both halves; 但是 cannot replace 而是 here.","examples":[{"zh":"她不是没看见我，而是不想说话。","py":"tā bú shì méi kàn jiàn wǒ ér shì bù xiǎng shuō huà","en":"It is not that she failed to see me; she simply did not want to talk."},{"zh":"我先说明，这不是抱怨，而是提醒。","py":"wǒ xiān shuō míng zhè bú shì bào yuàn ér shì tí xǐng","en":"Let me be clear from the start: this is not a complaint, it is a reminder."},{"zh":"真正的问题不是时间不够，而是顺序不对。","py":"zhēn zhèng de wèn tí bú shì shí jiān bù gòu ér shì shùn xù bú duì","en":"The real problem is not too little time, but the wrong order of steps."}],"drills":[{"q":"他今天迟到，____因为堵车，而是因为闹钟坏了。","options":["不是","不但","虽然","即使"],"answer":0,"explain":"而是 can only pair with 不是. 不但 needs 而且 later, 虽然 needs 但是 later, and 即使 needs 也 later, so none of them can sit in this half."},{"q":"他不是不想帮忙，____。","options":["而是那天实在没有时间","但是那天实在没有时间","而且那天实在没有时间","就是那天实在没有时间"],"answer":0,"explain":"The corrective pair must stay 不是……而是……. 但是 and 而且 would signal a different relation, and 就是 expresses emphasis, not correction."}]},"reading":{"title":"一碗汤的温度","text":"周末我回老家吃饭。奶奶的耳朵越来越不好，跟她说话得大声喊。爷爷嘴上总抱怨她慢，一边催她，一边又把椅子往后拉了一点。\n\n我坐在旁边看这两个人。他们结婚四十多年，也吵架，也会互相不耐烦。可我慢慢发现，真正打动人的，不是好听的话，而是很多很小的细节。爷爷记得她的药放在哪个抽屉，也知道她半夜会咳，就把水杯放在她手边。\n\n吃饭前，爷爷把一碗汤递给她，手指在碗边停了一下，试了试温度。奶奶什么也没说，只把碗往他那边推了推。晚饭后，爷爷打开电台听新闻，她就坐在旁边安静地等待，不时替他加一点热水。\n\n那一刻我忽然明白，他们的婚姻很少说“爱”，可这些动作一直在说。","translation":"At the weekend I went back to my hometown for a meal. My grandmother's hearing is getting worse, so you have to shout when you talk to her. My grandfather complains out loud that she is slow, and he is always urging her along, but at the same time he pulls her chair back a little for her. I sat beside them and watched. They have been married for more than forty years; they quarrel, and they do get impatient with each other. Yet I slowly noticed that what really moves people is not fine words but a great many very small details. My grandfather remembers which drawer her medicine is in, and he knows she coughs in the middle of the night, so he puts a glass of water by her hand. Before dinner he passes her a bowl of soup, pauses his fingers at the rim and tests the temperature. She says nothing, only pushes the bowl slightly back towards him. After dinner he turns on the radio for the news, and she sits beside him waiting quietly, now and then topping up his hot water. In that moment I suddenly understood: their marriage rarely says the word love, but these movements have been saying it all along.","questions":[{"q":"作者写这篇文章，主要是想告诉我们____。","options":["老夫妻的关心藏在很小的动作里","奶奶的耳朵越来越不好","爷爷每天都要听一会儿新闻","老家吃饭时的气氛很安静"],"answer":0,"explain":"The middle two paragraphs are both built from small acts of care, and the closing line says the marriage rarely speaks the word love while the movements keep saying it."},{"q":"根据第一段，爷爷一边催奶奶，一边____。","options":["把她的椅子往后拉了一点","大声喊她快点吃饭","把药悄悄放进抽屉里","顺手打开电台听新闻"],"answer":0,"explain":"The last sentence of paragraph one says 一边催她，一边又把椅子往后拉了一点, so the second action is pulling her chair back for her."},{"q":"作者说他们的婚姻“很少说爱”，是想说明____。","options":["老人不习惯说出这个词","感情主要靠动作表达出来","语言在婚姻里没有用处","作者自己的婚姻也不顺利"],"answer":1,"explain":"The last sentence contrasts 很少说 with 一直在说, and the paragraph before it lists actions such as testing the soup and topping up hot water, so the point is that the feeling lives in the actions."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["奶奶总抱怨爷爷说话太吵。","他们年轻时也常常吵架。","爱的细节往往藏在很小的动作里。","爷爷半夜起来给她倒水。","他每天清晨听一会儿电台新闻。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe one small habit that shows someone cares, at home or at work. Use the words below.","required_words":["细节","抱怨","爱护","等待"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我们办公室有一位同事，每天早上先把饮水机打开。这不算什么大事，可这些细节让加班的人有热水喝。他很少抱怨辛苦，也常常爱护新来的年轻人，愿意等待他们慢慢学会。真正的关心，大概就是这样安静地做下去。","tips":"Open with the habit itself in one sentence, then give one concrete moment that shows its effect on someone. Finish with a short sentence about what the habit means, not a summary of everything."}},{"n":2,"zh":"留串钥匙给父母","en":"Leaving a Bunch of Keys to Our Parents","book":1,"theme":"A spare key lets parents help in the way they know best, while learning to keep a respectful distance.","grammar":{"id":"g02","point":"除了……（以外），还/也……","point_en":"besides A, also B","structure":"除了 + A + （以外），Subject + 还/也 + B","explain_en":"Use this pattern to add one more item to something the listener already knows. The 除了 part names the item that is already on the table; the main clause then adds the new information that the sentence is really about. 以外 is optional, but it is common in written Chinese and often makes the two halves easier to hear. After the second subject comes 还 or 也 before the verb, and never after the verb. With a plural subject, 都 is also possible, as in 除了他，我们也都去了. Compare 除了……都……, which is the exclusion reading: 除了他，别人都来了 means everyone except him came. The additive reading needs 还 or 也; using 都 changes the meaning completely. It also differs from 不但……而且……, which stacks two facts with rising emphasis, while 除了……还 merely adds a second point in a neutral tone. Word order matters: 除了 sits in front of its object, and 以外 closes that phrase. Do not put 除了 after the verb: 除了打扫屋子以外，母亲还…… is right, 母亲打扫了除了屋子以外 is not.","common_mistake":"Learners often place 还 after the verb (除了英语，他说还汉语) or use 都 when they mean addition. Keep 除了 + object + 以外 at the front, then subject, then 还/也, then the verb.","examples":[{"zh":"除了打扫屋子以外，母亲还修好了水龙头。","py":"chú le dǎ sǎo wū zi yǐ wài mǔ qīn hái xiū hǎo le shuǐ lóng tóu","en":"Besides cleaning the room, my mother also fixed the tap."},{"zh":"这份工作除了工资，还能学到不少东西。","py":"zhè fèn gōng zuò chú le gōng zī hái néng xué dào bù shǎo dōng xi","en":"Apart from the salary, this job also lets you learn a lot."},{"zh":"除了我，弟弟也想去县里看看。","py":"chú le wǒ dì di yě xiǎng qù xiàn lǐ kàn kan","en":"Besides me, my younger brother also wants to go and see the county town."}],"drills":[{"q":"____打扫屋子，母亲还修好了水龙头。","options":["除了","因为","即使","虽然"],"answer":0,"explain":"The main clause already has 还, which marks an addition. 因为 would ask for a result, 即使 demands 也, and 虽然 demands 但是, so only 除了 sets up the additive frame."},{"q":"____，这份工作还能让我学到不少东西。","options":["除了工资以外","工资除了以外","除了以外工资","以外除了工资"],"answer":0,"explain":"除了 must come before the noun it introduces, and 以外 follows that noun. The other orders break the fixed 除了 + object + 以外 shape."}]},"reading":{"title":"门边的那串钥匙","text":"我在城里工作了六年，老家在农村。装修完新房那年，我把一串钥匙挂在门边的挂钩上，父母来的时候不用在楼下等我。\n\n母亲第一次来，是趁我上班，悄悄来的。晚上我回家，屋子亮着灯，被子晒过，又软又暖，桌上有汤，厨房的灰尘也不见了。她没留下字条，只把钥匙挂回了原处。\n\n我几乎能想象她干活儿的样子：先把窗户打开，再一间一间地擦。她不说，是怕我不高兴。\n\n后来我发现她来得不多。她说，除了送点吃的以外，她也不愿意多来，怕打扰我。父亲更少说话，只在电话里问一句锁好了没有。\n\n那串钥匙一直挂在门边。除了温暖以外，它还给我一种感受：这间屋子一直有人惦记着我。","translation":"I have worked in the city for six years, and my hometown is in the countryside. The year the new flat was decorated, I hung a bunch of keys on a hook by the door, so my parents would not have to wait for me downstairs. My mother's first visit came while I was at work, and she came quietly. When I got home that evening the room was lit up, the quilt had been aired and was soft and warm, soup was on the table, and the dust in the kitchen was gone. She left no note, only hung the key back where it belonged. I can almost picture how she worked: open the windows first, then wipe one room after another. She says nothing about it because she is afraid I would be annoyed. Later I realised she does not come often. She says that apart from bringing a little food, she does not want to visit too much in case she disturbs me. My father says even less; on the phone he only asks whether the lock is done up. That bunch of keys has stayed by the door. Besides warmth, it gives me a feeling that someone in this flat is always thinking of me.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["作者装修新房的过程","一串钥匙带来的家庭温暖","母亲打扫房间的技巧","城市和农村生活的区别"],"answer":1,"explain":"The key is mentioned in the first and last paragraphs, and everything between describes the mother caring for the flat, so the passage is about the warmth the key brings rather than the decoration itself."},{"q":"母亲第一次来的时候，____。","options":["趁作者上班时悄悄来的","提前打电话告诉了作者","带着父亲一起来的","在楼下等了很久"],"answer":0,"explain":"Paragraph two opens with 母亲第一次来，是趁我上班，悄悄来的, which rules out an announced visit or waiting downstairs."},{"q":"作者把一串钥匙留给父母，主要是因为____。","options":["想让母亲常来帮忙打扫","怕自己把钥匙弄丢","希望父母来了不用在楼下等","想请父母搬来城里长住"],"answer":2,"explain":"The reason is stated directly after the key is mentioned: 父母来的时候不用在楼下等我. Nothing in the passage suggests she was asked to clean or that the parents were moving in."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["母亲悄悄地把被子抱到阳台上晒。","除了打扫屋子，母亲还留了一锅汤。","我在城里工作，老家在农村。","这间屋子不大，可是让人感到温暖。","她想象着母亲擦桌子的样子。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about something a family member quietly does for you. Use the words below.","required_words":["农村","屋子","温暖","感受"],"min_chars":80,"model":"奶奶住在农村，屋子不大，却收拾得很干净。每次回去，她总把被子晒好，说这样睡着更暖。我以前只觉得方便，这几年才慢慢感受到，那些小动作是她表达想念的方式。屋子里的温暖，原来是有人一直在等你，就像小时候一样。","tips":"Start with where the person lives and one habit they repeat, then describe one visit in concrete detail. Close with what you understand now that you did not notice before."}},{"n":3,"zh":"人生有选择，一切可改变","en":"Having Choices in Life Makes Change Possible","book":1,"theme":"A steady job is not the only safe choice, and a deliberate change at midlife can be the more honest one.","grammar":{"id":"g03","point":"无论/不管……都/也……","point_en":"no matter what/whether..., still...","structure":"无论/不管 + unlimited conditions，Subject + 都/也 + main clause","explain_en":"Both 无论 and 不管 open a clause that sweeps over every possible case, and the main clause answers with 都 or 也. 无论 is the more formal choice and appears often in writing; 不管 is common in speech and slightly more casual, but the structure is identical. Inside the opening clause you need a question word such as 什么, 谁, 怎么, 哪, 多少, or a 多么 + adjective, or a 还是……还是…… list, or 多 + adjective. Without one of those signals the clause is not a real sweep and the sentence falls apart. The main clause must carry 都 or 也; 还 and 就 do not work here. Word order: the 无论 clause comes first, then the subject of the main clause, then 都/也 right before the verb: 无论多忙，他都回家吃饭. When one subject serves both clauses, it can sit before 无论 or between the clauses, and both are fine. Do not add 但是 in the main clause. Compare 即使……也……, which concedes one unlikely extreme rather than covering all cases.","common_mistake":"Learners drop 都/也 from the main clause and write 无论天气怎么样，他出去跑步, or put 但是 there instead. The main clause needs 都 or 也, and 但是 is wrong inside this pair.","examples":[{"zh":"无论天气怎么样，他都在六点半到公司。","py":"wú lùn tiān qì zěn me yàng tā dōu zài liù diǎn bàn dào gōng sī","en":"No matter what the weather is like, he reaches the office at half past six."},{"zh":"不管客户提出什么问题，她都能耐心回答。","py":"bù guǎn kè hù tí chū shén me wèn tí tā dōu néng nài xīn huí dá","en":"Whatever question a client raises, she can answer it patiently."},{"zh":"不管是哪个版本，成本都要先算清楚。","py":"bù guǎn shì nǎ ge bǎn běn chéng běn dōu yào xiān suàn qīng chu","en":"Whichever version it is, the cost has to be worked out first."}],"drills":[{"q":"____天气怎么样，他每天早上都跑步。","options":["无论","因为","虽然","只有"],"answer":0,"explain":"The main clause already has 都, which is the partner of 无论/不管. 因为 would introduce a cause, 虽然 would need 但是, and 只有 would need 才, so only 无论 fits."},{"q":"无论工作多忙，他____会抽时间陪家人。","options":["都","但是","因为","所以"],"answer":0,"explain":"The slot between the subject and the verb takes the adverb 都 or 也. 但是, 因为 and 所以 are conjunctions that cannot sit in that adverb position, and none of them pairs with 无论."}]},"reading":{"title":"四十岁那年，他去学开船","text":"老陈在工厂干了二十年，是熟练的工人。工作稳定，待遇也不差，可他每年冬天都发愁一件事：这辈子是不是就到这里了。\n\n四十岁那年，他用积蓄买了一条二手帆船。太太一开始坚决不同意，说这个年纪该安静一点。他还是决定辞职，跟着船队学驾驶。\n\n第一次出海的傍晚，风很小，船几乎不动。他坐在甲板上，忽然觉得心里很平静。后来他常说，海上没有谁催你，只有风和你的手。\n\n如今他在港口干活儿，收入不高，可日子正是他盼望的样子。他每天六点起床，比在工厂时还早。无论别人怎么评价，他都不后悔自己的选择。人生有选择，一切才可能改变。","translation":"Chen had worked in a factory for twenty years and was a skilled worker there. The job was stable and the pay and benefits were not bad, yet every winter he worried about one thing: was this as far as his life would go? In the year he turned forty he used his savings to buy a second-hand sailing boat. His wife was firmly against it at first and said that at this age he ought to settle down. He still decided to resign and learned to steer with a sailing crew. On the evening of his first trip out, the wind was very light and the boat barely moved. Sitting on the deck, he suddenly felt calm inside. Later he often said that at sea nobody hurries you, only the wind and your own hands. These days he works at the harbour and earns little, but his days are exactly what he hoped for. He gets up at six every morning, earlier than he did at the factory. No matter how other people judge it, he does not regret his choice. Life offers choices, and that is what makes change possible.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章想告诉我们____。","options":["海上航行其实非常危险","中年换一种活法也有意义","工厂的工作待遇不好","买帆船应该先问家人"],"answer":1,"explain":"The closing sentence is 人生有选择，一切才可能改变, and the whole middle section shows that Chen's change worked out, so the passage argues that a different way of living in midlife is worthwhile."},{"q":"四十岁那年，老陈做的主要事情是____。","options":["在工厂当上了负责人","带着太太一起去旅行","买了二手帆船，后来辞了职","把积蓄都存进了银行"],"answer":2,"explain":"Paragraph two says he used his savings to buy a second-hand sailing boat, then decided to resign and learn to steer; the wife was against it, so she did not join him."},{"q":"从最后一段可以看出，老陈____。","options":["后悔当初辞掉工作","对现在的日子比较满意","想回工厂继续上班","收入比以前高很多"],"answer":1,"explain":"He says his days are what he hoped for and that he does not regret his choice, and the passage notes his income is not high, so he is content rather than regretful or richer."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["他在这个工厂干了二十年。","这份工作很稳定，待遇也不错。","她辞职以后，每天去学驾驶帆船。","无论多晚回家，他都先做饭。","傍晚的海面平静得像一面镜子。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a change you made that surprised the people around you. Use the words below.","required_words":["稳定","辞职","盼望","未来"],"min_chars":80,"model":"三年前我从一份稳定的工作辞职，去了一家很小的公司。很多同事不理解，我自己也曾经为收入发愁。可是每天做的事都是我盼望的，我愿意从头学新的东西。未来不一定更轻松，但这个选择是我自己的，我不后悔。","tips":"Say what you left and what you moved to in the first two sentences, then add one worry you actually had. End with how you judge the decision now, without claiming it was easy."}},{"n":4,"zh":"子路背米","en":"Zilu Carrying Rice","book":1,"theme":"An old story about carrying rice home shows that care is measured in effort rather than in what money can buy.","grammar":{"id":"g04","point":"即使……也……","point_en":"even if..., still...","structure":"即使 + unlikely condition，Subject + 也 + unchanged result","explain_en":"即使……也…… concedes an extreme or unlikely condition and then insists that the result does not change. The 即使 half is a hypothesis, not a fact, which is what separates it from 虽然……但是……. Compare 虽然下雨了，我们还是出发了, where the rain really happened, with 即使下雨，我们也要出发, where the rain is only a possibility being pushed aside. The main clause needs 也, or 还是 and 仍然 for a stronger tone; 但是 and 所以 cannot sit inside this pair. The concession is usually something the listener would expect to change the outcome, so the sentence sounds resolute: it says my decision survives this too. One subject can serve both halves, and it may stand before 即使 or be repeated in the second clause. Both halves normally use the same verb shape; if the first half has an adjective, the second half should describe a matching consequence. Do not combine 即使 with 而且 or 只有. Keep 也 before the verb, never at the end of the sentence.","common_mistake":"The usual error is answering 即使 with 但是 or 所以, as in 即使下雨，但是我们也要出发. The main clause takes 也 (or 还是, 仍然), but a 但是 clause cannot be grafted onto 即使.","examples":[{"zh":"即使下大雨，比赛也照常进行。","py":"jí shǐ xià dà yǔ bǐ sài yě zhào cháng jìn xíng","en":"Even if it pours with rain, the match will go ahead as usual."},{"zh":"这份资料即使看不完，也要先分清重点。","py":"zhè fèn zī liào jí shǐ kàn bù wán yě yào xiān fēn qīng zhòng diǎn","en":"Even if you cannot finish these materials, you still need to sort out the key points first."},{"zh":"即使你不同意，也应该先把理由说清楚。","py":"jí shǐ nǐ bù tóng yì yě yīng gāi xiān bǎ lǐ yóu shuō qīng chu","en":"Even if you disagree, you should still explain your reasons first."}],"drills":[{"q":"____明天下雨，我们也要按时出发。","options":["即使","因为","只要","不但"],"answer":0,"explain":"也要 in the main clause marks a concession that survives the condition, which is the job of 即使. 因为 needs 所以, 只要 needs 就, and 不但 needs 而且, so none of them can answer 也."},{"q":"即使路很远，他____坚持每天走回家。","options":["也","但是","所以","因为"],"answer":0,"explain":"The slot between the subject and the verb takes the adverb 也 or 都, and 即使 requires 也 in the main clause. 但是, 所以 and 因为 are conjunctions, so they cannot fill an adverb slot or complete this pair."}]},"reading":{"title":"一袋米的路","text":"从前有一个年轻人，家里很穷，父母年纪大了，吃得很少。他听说很远的一个镇上有活干，就背起简单的行李出门了。\n\n他在一户人家做事。主人见他老实、勤奋，愿意多给他一点银子。他把钱都存着，舍不得花一分，只想早点回家。\n\n每年冬天，他都要背一袋米回去，要走三天的路。后背被带子磨得发红，肩膀酸得抬不起来，可他从不说委屈。有人劝他把米卖了换成钱，他摇头：父母年纪大了，能吃到儿子背回来的米，比什么都好。\n\n后来他的父母先后去世，他常常惭愧，觉得陪他们的时间太少。这个故事在民间流传至今，人们用它讲孝顺。即使今天物质丰富、买米一点也不难，这份心意也没有过时。","translation":"Long ago there was a young man whose family was very poor; his parents were old and ate very little. When he heard that there was work in a town far away, he packed a simple bag and set off. He worked for a household there. The head of the house saw that he was honest and hard-working and was willing to pay him a little more silver. He saved every bit of it and begrudged spending any, wanting only to get home sooner. Every winter he carried a bag of rice back, a journey of three days. The strap rubbed his back red and his shoulders ached so much he could hardly lift them, but he never complained of being hard done by. People urged him to sell the rice for money instead, and he shook his head: his parents were old, and being able to eat rice their son had carried home himself was better than anything. After his parents passed away one after the other, he often felt ashamed, thinking he had spent too little time with them. The story has been passed down among ordinary people to this day, and people use it to talk about caring for one's parents. Even now, when goods are plentiful and buying rice is no trouble at all, that feeling has not gone out of date.","questions":[{"q":"这个故事主要讲的是____。","options":["古代农民怎样种米","一个年轻人对父母的孝心","一个镇上做生意的办法","民间故事是怎么记下来的"],"answer":1,"explain":"The young man saves his pay, walks three days with rice on his back, and refuses to sell it; the last paragraph says people use the story to talk about 孝顺, so the theme is care for parents."},{"q":"每年冬天，年轻人回家时都要____。","options":["带一些银子送给邻居","坐船去县里买米","背一袋米走三天的路","在镇上住一个冬天"],"answer":2,"explain":"Paragraph three begins 每年冬天，他都要背一袋米回去，要走三天的路, and the passage never mentions a boat, a county town or a winter stay."},{"q":"父母去世以后，他的心情说明他____。","options":["觉得自己陪父母的时间不够","后悔没有多挣一些银子","从此不想再回家","认为这个故事没有意义"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 他常常惭愧，觉得陪他们的时间太少, so the shame comes from too little time together, not from money or from rejecting the story."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["他把挣来的银子都存了起来。","这个故事在民间流传了很久。","他很惭愧，觉得自己做得不够。","那个人老实又勤奋，值得信任。","即使路很远，他也决定走回去。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about someone in your family who quietly does more than their share. Use the words below.","required_words":["勤奋","惭愧","团圆","满足"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我父亲是个老实人，在工厂做技术工作，一辈子勤奋。他很少说自己累，下班还去照顾爷爷。过年的时候一家人团圆，他话最少，却最早起来准备饭菜。我以前觉得这一切理所当然，现在想起来有点惭愧。他不求出名，只要家人满足，就笑了。","tips":"Introduce the person and one habit in the first sentence, then show it in a single scene such as a holiday meal. Finish by naming what you now feel about it, keeping the change of heart modest."}},{"n":5,"zh":"济南的泉水","en":"Spring Water in Ji'nan","book":1,"theme":"The springs of a city matter less as a sight to tick off than as a daily habit that sets its pace.","grammar":{"id":"g05","point":"与其……不如……","point_en":"rather than A, it would be better to B","structure":"与其 + less good option，不如 + preferred option","explain_en":"与其……不如…… compares two things you could do and comes down on the second one. 与其 introduces the option the speaker is setting aside, and 不如 introduces the one being recommended, so the order of the two clauses carries the advice. This is why the pair is not simply 'rather than': it always ends with a recommendation. Both halves should be actions with matching shape, normally the same verb type and length. The subject usually stands before 与其 and is not repeated in the second clause, and 不如 comes directly after the comma. In speech 不如 is often strengthened to 还不如, and 倒 can be added for a softer, slightly ironic tone. The pattern is close to 与其说……不如说……, but that version corrects a description rather than choosing between actions: 与其说他是领导，不如说他是老师 does not mean you can pick one. It is the opposite of 宁可……也不……, which refuses the second option instead of recommending it. Keep the pair in this order; 不如……与其…… is not used.","common_mistake":"Learners reverse the two halves (不如……与其……) or leave out 不如 after the comma. The fixed order is 与其 first, 不如 second, and both clauses need a full predicate.","examples":[{"zh":"与其在群里反复讨论，不如先把数据核对清楚。","py":"yǔ qí zài qún lǐ fǎn fù tǎo lùn bù rú xiān bǎ shù jù hé duì qīng chu","en":"Rather than going round and round in the group chat, it would be better to check the figures carefully first."},{"zh":"与其换新的，不如把这台修好。","py":"yǔ qí huàn xīn de bù rú bǎ zhè tái xiū hǎo","en":"Rather than replace it, it would be better to get this one repaired."},{"zh":"与其说他是我的领导，不如说他是我的老师。","py":"yǔ qí shuō tā shì wǒ de lǐng dǎo bù rú shuō tā shì wǒ de lǎo shī","en":"He is less my manager than my teacher."}],"drills":[{"q":"与其等别人来帮忙，____自己先试一次。","options":["不如","因为","虽然","即使"],"answer":0,"explain":"与其 must be answered by 不如, the only partner that carries the recommendation. 因为 needs 所以, 虽然 needs 但是, and 即使 needs 也, so the sentence would have no main clause."},{"q":"与其花钱请人修，____。","options":["不如自己动手试试","宁可自己动手试试","只好自己动手试试","才自己动手试试"],"answer":0,"explain":"The second half of 与其 is fixed as 不如. 宁可 needs a rejected 也不 clause, 只好 does not pair with 与其, and 才 needs a preceding condition rather than a comparison."}]},"reading":{"title":"泉水边的十分钟","text":"到济南的第二天，我才明白这里的人为什么爱说泉水。\n\n老城的巷子里，泉眼分布得很密，几乎每走几百步就能碰见一处。水从石头下面出来，一年四季都是温的。冬天清晨，水面上飘着一层白气，像有人在下面生了一盆火。\n\n从前的文字里就记载过这些水。有人写它，说它清得像玉，说它的声音像有人在小声说话。如今来打水的人还是很多，老人提着水壶，排成一条不长的队，一边等一边聊天。\n\n这些泉不是人工挖出来的，而是天然形成的。地势低，水无处可去，就从岩石的缝里出来。水在石头表面流过，留下形状不同的痕迹，所以每一处泉眼看着都不一样。\n\n与其赶着去下一个地方，不如在这里坐十分钟。这份从容，才是泉水真正给人的东西。","translation":"It was only on my second day in Ji'nan that I understood why people here love to talk about the spring water. In the lanes of the old town the springs are spread densely, and you bump into one every few hundred steps. The water comes out from under the stones and is warm all year round. On a winter morning a layer of white vapour drifts over the surface, as if someone had lit a small fire underneath. Written records from long ago already noted this water. Someone wrote that it was as clear as jade, and that its sound was like a person speaking softly. Even today many people come to fetch water: elderly men and women carry kettles and form a short queue, chatting while they wait. These springs were not dug by hand; they formed naturally. The ground lies low, the water has nowhere else to go, so it comes out through cracks in the rock. As it runs over the surface of the stones it leaves marks of different shapes, which is why every spring looks a little different. Rather than rushing off to the next place, it is better to sit here for ten minutes. That unhurried quality is what the springs really give a person.","questions":[{"q":"作者写这篇文章，主要是想____。","options":["介绍泉水形成的原因","表达对这座城市的喜欢","说明打水为什么要排队","介绍济南的历史名人"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage moves from the springs to the people fetching water and ends with sitting by them for ten minutes, so the aim is affection for the city rather than a science or history lesson."},{"q":"根据第四段，泉水是从____出来的。","options":["岩石的缝里","老城的墙根下","人工挖的水井里","河边的新管子里"],"answer":0,"explain":"The fourth paragraph says 水无处可去，就从岩石的缝里出来, and it states plainly that the springs were not dug by hand, which rules out a well or a pipe."},{"q":"作者说“不如在这里坐十分钟”，是因为____。","options":["走累了需要休息","泉水边有免费的茶","想体会这座城市慢慢的节奏","下一班车还没有来"],"answer":2,"explain":"The last two sentences link the ten minutes with 从容 and say that this is what the springs really give, so the reason is the city's pace, not tiredness or a bus."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这些泉水是天然形成的。","老人在泉边排队打水，一边聊天。","这块石头的形状很独特。","这座城市的历史很悠久。","与其坐车，不如走过去看看。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a place in your city you would take a visitor to, and explain why. Use the words below.","required_words":["悠久","独特","充满","优美"],"min_chars":80,"model":"如果朋友来我的城市，我会带他去老河边的那条街。那里的房子很老，历史很悠久，每一家的门都不一样，颜色也很独特，看上去十分优美。傍晚的时候，街上充满饭香，小孩在跑，老人坐在门口聊天。我每次走在那里，都能感受到这座城慢慢的样子。","tips":"Name the place and one detail a visitor would notice first, then add what happens there at a certain time of day. Close with why you keep going back, in one short sentence."}},{"n":6,"zh":"除夕的由来","en":"Origin of Chuxi","book":1,"theme":"A New Year's Eve legend explains why one night of staying up together still carries meaning.","grammar":{"id":"g06","point":"宁可……也不……","point_en":"would rather A than B","structure":"宁可 + accepted cost，Subject + 也不 + refused option","explain_en":"宁可……也不…… states a preference that costs the speaker something. The 宁可 half is what they agree to accept, even though it is inconvenient, tiring or expensive; the 也不 half is what they refuse. The pattern is about principle rather than neutral comparison: two options exist, and one is ruled out on purpose. 也不 is the default second half. 也不愿 and 也不想 appear when the second verb is 愿意 or 想, and 决 can stand in for 也 for a firmer tone, as in 宁可……决不……. One subject covers both halves, and 也不 sits directly after the comma, before the verb. Compare 与其……不如……: that pair also weighs two options, but it recommends one instead of rejecting one, so the tone is practical advice rather than resolve. Compare 宁愿, which is warmer and more common in speech, and 宁可不……也要……, where the second half is something still wanted rather than refused. Word order is fixed, 宁可 first and 也不 second, and the refused clause usually takes no 但是.","common_mistake":"Learners leave out 也 and write 宁可……不愿意……, or add 但是 in the second clause. Keep both halves: 宁可 first, then 也不 before the verb you are refusing.","examples":[{"zh":"宁可多等十分钟，也不挤那趟地铁。","py":"nìng kě duō děng shí fēn zhōng yě bù jǐ nà tàng dì tiě","en":"I would rather wait ten minutes longer than squeeze onto that train."},{"zh":"她宁可自己加班，也不愿把任务推给别人。","py":"tā nìng kě zì jǐ jiā bān yě bù yuàn bǎ rèn wù tuī gěi bié rén","en":"She would rather work late herself than push the task onto someone else."},{"zh":"我们宁可少赚，也不降低质量。","py":"wǒ men nìng kě shǎo zhuàn yě bù jiàng dī zhì liàng","en":"We would rather earn less than lower the quality."}],"drills":[{"q":"我____多走二十分钟，也不坐那趟挤满人的车。","options":["宁可","与其","不但","因为"],"answer":0,"explain":"也不 in the second half marks a refusal, and only 宁可 sets that up. 与其 needs 不如, 不但 needs 而且, and 因为 needs 所以, so none of them can answer 也不."},{"q":"她宁可自己加班，____麻烦别人。","options":["也不愿意","但是不愿意","所以不愿意","因为不愿意"],"answer":0,"explain":"The fixed pair is 宁可……也不……, so the second half must begin with 也不. 但是, 所以 and 因为 would each set up a different relation and break the pattern."}]},"reading":{"title":"外公讲的除夕","text":"小时候，每到农历的最后一天，外公都会给我讲除夕的由来。\n\n他说，很久以前，山里有一种怪物，每到这一天的半夜就出来。谁家的门没关好，它就去吓人。人们恨它，又拿它没办法。后来有人发现，这怪物怕红色，也怕很响的声音。于是大家在家门口贴上红纸，把竹子放在火里烧，噼啪的声音把它赶走了。\n\n外公说，那天晚上没有人敢睡，全家坐在一起，这就叫守岁。宁可熬夜，也不让怪物进门。\n\n我问外公，怪物真的存在吗？他笑着说，说不定这个说法只是编出来骗小孩的。可是第二天，家家门口都是红色的纸，整个村子都是鞭炮的声音。大人们纷纷说，这样过一夜，心里才踏实。这个风俗就这样一年一年地传下来。","translation":"When I was small, my grandfather on my mother's side would tell me the origin of New Year's Eve on the last day of the lunar calendar every year. He said that long ago there was a kind of monster in the mountains, and it came out in the middle of the night on that day. If a household had not shut its door properly, it would go and frighten the people inside. People hated it and could do nothing about it. Then someone discovered that the monster was afraid of red and also afraid of loud noises. So everyone pasted red paper on their doors and burned bamboo in the fire, and the crackling sound drove it away. My grandfather said that nobody dared to sleep that night and the whole family sat up together, which is what people call staying up for the New Year. They would rather lose sleep than let the monster in. I asked him whether the monster really existed. He laughed and said that maybe the story was just made up to frighten children. But the next day every doorway was red and the whole village rang with firecrackers. The grown-ups all said that after a night like that, you finally feel settled. And that is how the custom has been passed down, year after year.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要讲的是____。","options":["除夕和它的习俗是怎么来的","小孩子为什么怕黑","农村的冬天怎么取暖","红纸是怎么做出来的"],"answer":0,"explain":"The first sentence announces 除夕的由来, and the rest explains the monster story, 守岁 and 鞭炮, so the passage is about the origin of the festival and its customs."},{"q":"为了赶走怪物，人们贴红纸，还____。","options":["在门口放了一锅水","全家一起唱老歌","烧竹子弄出很大的响声","把门锁得比平时更紧"],"answer":2,"explain":"Paragraph two says people pasted red paper and 把竹子放在火里烧，噼啪的声音把它赶走了; the water, the singing and the extra locks are not in the text."},{"q":"外公说“说不定这个说法只是编出来骗小孩的”，可以看出外公____。","options":["其实非常害怕怪物","对这个说法并不完全相信","觉得孩子不该过年","希望孩子早点回家睡觉"],"answer":1,"explain":"He is laughing as he says it, and 说不定 marks uncertainty about the legend, so he does not fully believe the story. Nothing in the passage suggests fear or a wish for the child to go to bed."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["除夕的晚上，一家人一起守岁。","我们宁可早到，也不愿意迟到。","过年的时候，孩子们最喜欢放鞭炮。","外婆说，这个风俗很有意义。","他昨天熬夜把工作做完了。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a family custom or a rule you keep, and say what it means to you. Use the words below.","required_words":["除夕","风俗","意义","整个"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我们家有一个小小的风俗：除夕那天，不管多忙，全家都要一起包饺子。母亲和面，父亲剁馅，我负责把饺子摆得整整齐齐。整个厨房都是热气。这个习惯看起来普通，意义却不小，它让我们知道，一年总要有一天是为家人留出来的。","tips":"Start by naming the custom and when it happens, then describe one concrete moment with two or three actions. Finish with the meaning in a single sentence instead of a long moral."}},{"n":7,"zh":"成语故事两则","en":"Two Idiom Stories","book":1,"theme":"Two old idioms about seeing only part of the picture, read as advice for listening carefully and reaching a fair conclusion at work.","grammar":{"id":"g07","point":"只有……才……","point_en":"only if A, and only then B","structure":"只有 + condition + 才 + result","explain_en":"Use 只有……才…… when the result in the second clause depends on one condition and on nothing else: 'only if A, then B'. 只有 introduces that single necessary condition. 才 comes after the subject of the second clause and immediately before its verb or adjective, and it marks the result as something that becomes possible only because the condition has been met. The condition clause normally comes first, though it can be moved to the end for emphasis. The subject usually follows 只有 (只有你把计划说清楚，我们才……), but putting the subject first is also fine (你只有说清楚，我们才……). 才 is the fixed partner; it is not a tense marker and it cannot be replaced by 就. Compare 只要……就……, which presents a sufficient condition and sounds permissive ('as long as A happens, B follows'). 只有……才…… narrows the options and often carries a note of insistence or warning. Compare 除非……否则……, which names the only exception and then states what happens without it.","common_mistake":"The usual slip is pairing the wrong partners, as in 只有努力，就能成功 or 只要你努力，才能成功. Learners also leave 才 out when the second clause ends in an adjective: 只有早睡，身体好 instead of 只有早睡，身体才会好.","examples":[{"zh":"只有先听清楚别人的想法，才能把自己的意见说对。","py":"zhǐ yǒu xiān tīng qīng chu bié rén de xiǎng fǎ cái néng bǎ zì jǐ de yì jiàn shuō duì","en":"Only by hearing other people's thinking first can you put your own view across correctly."},{"zh":"他只有把每个数字都确定下来，才会签字。","py":"tā zhǐ yǒu bǎ měi gè shù zì dōu què dìng xià lái cái huì qiān zì","en":"He signs only after every figure has been confirmed."},{"zh":"只有把两个人的想法放在一起，才看得见问题的全部。","py":"zhǐ yǒu bǎ liǎng gè rén de xiǎng fǎ fàng zài yì qǐ cái kàn de jiàn wèn tí de quán bù","en":"Only by putting both people's ideas side by side can you see the whole of the problem."}],"drills":[{"q":"____你先把材料看完，我们才能开始。","options":["只有","只要","既然","虽然"],"answer":0,"explain":"只有 is the only one of these that can be answered by 才 in the result clause. 只要 would require 就 (只要你把材料看完，我们就可以开始), 既然 pairs with 就 to draw a conclusion from an accepted fact, and 虽然 needs 但是 or 也 to set up a contrast."},{"q":"这种味道，____从小在这里长大的人，____说得清楚。","options":["只有……才……","只要……就……","既然……就……","越……越……"],"answer":0,"explain":"The slot after the first marker holds a noun phrase (从小在这里长大的人), and the sentence says those people and nobody else can explain the taste — the exclusive reading that 只有……才…… gives. 只要 and 既然 need a full clause with its own subject and predicate, and 越……越…… compares two changes in degree, which cannot be built out of a noun phrase."}]},"reading":{"title":"每个人都摸到了什么","text":"公司开周会时，同一个问题常常有好几种说法。有人只看到数据，有人只听到客户的意见。如果大家急着争论，最后拿到的结论往往是片面的。这让我想起盲人摸象的故事：几个人一起去摸大象，一个摸到牙齿，一个摸到尾巴，一个摸到腿，分别说出自己的感觉，谁也不服谁。\n\n其实他们都没有错，只是每个人看到的部分太小。工作上也一样，只有把不同的观察放在一起，才能确定问题到底在哪儿。善于听别人说话的人，往往比急着下结论的人更有智慧。团队讨论的价值，不在于谁的反应最快，而在于大家愿意把话说完整。","translation":"In a weekly office meeting, the same problem often comes out in several versions. One person looks only at the numbers; another has only heard the customer's complaint. If everyone starts arguing straight away, the conclusion we end up with is usually one-sided. This reminds me of the story of the blind men and the elephant: several of them go up to the animal together, one feels its teeth, one its tail, one its leg, and each reports what he feels, and not one of them gives way. In fact none of them is wrong; each has simply seen too small a part. Work is the same. Only by putting the separate observations side by side can we work out where the problem really is. People who are good at listening tend to have more wisdom than people who are quick to announce a conclusion. The value of a team discussion is not who reacts fastest, but whether everyone is willing to finish the sentence.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想说的是____。","options":["开会的时候最好少说话","把片面的看法放在一起才接近事实","盲人比普通人更有智慧","客户的意见比数据更重要"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph states the point directly: only by putting different observations together can the team find the real problem."},{"q":"文中说，他们摸大象的时候____。","options":["一起把大象画了下来","分别说出自己的感觉","找将军来判断对错","把绳子系在大象身上"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage says 一个摸到牙齿，一个摸到尾巴……分别说出自己的感觉，谁也不服谁."},{"q":"从文章看，作者认为团队讨论最重要的是____。","options":["谁的声音最大","谁的反应最快","大家愿意把话说完整","谁手里的数据最多"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing sentence contrasts 反应最快 with 愿意把话说完整 and names the second as the real value."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["盲人用手摸大象，每个人说的都不一样。","你先别急着下结论，事情还没有确定。","他善于听别人说话，所以很少出错。","只看到一部分就下判断，结论常常是片面的。","这次讨论没有结果，大家分别回了办公室。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a meeting or a family discussion where people saw the same situation differently. Show what happened when you slowed down and put the pieces together. Use the words below.","required_words":["结论","片面","确定","善于"],"min_chars":80,"model":"上周我们讨论一个新项目。开始时每个人看到的部分都不一样，有人担心成本，有人担心时间。我们没有急着下结论，而是把意见一条一条写下来，再逐条确定。只看一部分就下判断，结论往往是片面的。讨论结束后我发现，只有把不同的看法放在一起，才会得出完整的答案。善于听别人说话，也是一种智慧。","tips":"Open with the situation in one sentence, then give one concrete disagreement. Show the turn — what you did differently — and close with a short line about what you now believe."}},{"n":8,"zh":"“朝三暮四”的古今义","en":"Three at Dawn and Four at Dusk","book":1,"theme":"How the same facts can be framed two ways, and why the order of a message changes how people feel about it.","grammar":{"id":"g08","point":"只要……就……","point_en":"as long as A, then B","structure":"只要 + sufficient condition + 就 + result","explain_en":"Use 只要……就…… for a sufficient condition: as long as A happens, B follows, and nothing else is required. 只要 opens the first clause, though the subject may stand in front of it (只要你来 / 你只要来). 就 comes after the subject of the second clause, directly before its verb, adjective or a 会/能 phrase. The tone is encouraging or permissive — the speaker is lowering the bar and saying one thing is enough. 只要 takes 就 and never 才. Compare 只有……才……, which marks a necessary, exclusive condition and often carries an implied 'otherwise not'; 只要……就…… says this route is enough and does not rule out other routes. Compare 如果……就……, which is a neutral hypothesis and does not stress sufficiency. 只要 also appears in the frame 只要是……就…… when a whole category is meant (只要是本公司的员工就可以报名). When both clauses share one subject, the subject normally comes first.","common_mistake":"Two mistakes are common. One keeps the right meaning but swaps the partner: 只要你努力，才能成功 mixes a sufficient condition with a necessary one. The other is word order — 就 must follow the subject of the second clause, so 只要你说一声，就我来办 should be 只要你说一声，我就来办.","examples":[{"zh":"只要先把整体讲清楚，后面的限制就容易接受。","py":"zhǐ yào xiān bǎ zhěng tǐ jiǎng qīng chu hòu miàn de xiàn zhì jiù róng yì jiē shòu","en":"As long as you set out the whole picture first, the limits that follow are easy to accept."},{"zh":"你只要提前十分钟出门，就不会迟到。","py":"nǐ zhǐ yào tí qián shí fēn zhōng chū mén jiù bú huì chí dào","en":"As long as you leave ten minutes earlier, you will not be late."},{"zh":"只要大家把话说开，彼此就不会误会。","py":"zhǐ yào dà jiā bǎ huà shuō kāi bǐ cǐ jiù bú huì wù huì","en":"As long as everyone speaks openly, neither side will misunderstand the other."}],"drills":[{"q":"____你提前打个电话，我们就给你留个位置。","options":["只要","只有","除非","即使"],"answer":0,"explain":"就 in the result clause fixes the partner as 只要. 只有 must be answered by 才, 除非 needs 否则 (or 才) rather than 就, and 即使 requires 也 — besides, nothing in the sentence is being conceded."},{"q":"你只要提前十分钟出门，____不会迟到。","options":["才","就","也","又"],"answer":1,"explain":"只要 is answered by 就 in the result clause. 才 belongs with 只有, 也 would need a frame such as 无论……都…… or 也……也……, and 又 marks repetition rather than a consequence."}]},"reading":{"title":"换个说法，结果真的不同","text":"小时候读猴子分橡子的寓言，只觉得猴子笨。长大以后才明白，同样七颗橡子，早上三颗晚上四颗，和早上四颗晚上三颗，猴子的反应完全不同。东西没有变，变的只是说话的方式。\n\n公司里也常有这样的事。去年年底，福利要调整，第一次开会时负责人只讲了减少的部分，会议室里格外安静，同事们脸上的表情都不太好看。第二次，他换了一个顺序：先讲公司保住了什么，再说明需要节省的地方。同样的内容，大家的反应缓和了很多，有人还提出了几个省钱的办法。\n\n这似乎并不是说话技巧的问题。人看事情，很难一下子看到整体，总是先注意自己关心的那一部分。只要把完整的图景放在前面，人就比较容易接受后面的限制。人和人相处，彼此之间很多误会并非来自事情本身，而是来自说话的顺序。","translation":"When I read the fable about monkeys and acorns as a child, I only thought the monkeys were stupid. Years later I understood: with the same seven acorns, three in the morning and four in the evening versus four in the morning and three in the evening, the monkeys reacted completely differently. Nothing had changed except the way it was said.\n\nThe same thing happens at the office. At the end of last year our benefits were being adjusted. At the first meeting the person in charge described only the cuts, the room went unusually quiet, and nobody's expression looked good. At the second meeting he changed the order: first what the company had kept, then where savings were needed. Same content, and people took it much more calmly; someone even suggested a few ways to save money.\n\nThis seems to be more than a matter of technique. When people look at something, they rarely take in the whole at once; they notice their own concern first. As long as the complete picture comes first, the limits that follow are easier to accept. Between people, plenty of misunderstanding comes not from the facts but from the order in which they are told.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想说的是____。","options":["猴子分东西的方法很笨","同样的内容换个说法会改变人的感受","公司不该减少员工的福利","开会的时候最好不要谈数字"],"answer":1,"explain":"The acorn story and the two meetings both make the same point, stated in the last paragraph: the order of delivery changes how people take the news."},{"q":"第二次开会时，负责人先讲了____。","options":["公司减少了哪些福利","公司保住了哪些福利","明年的工作计划","员工提出的省钱办法"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage says he 先讲公司保住了什么，再说明需要节省的地方 — the kept part came first."},{"q":"从文章看，作者对换个说法的态度是____。","options":["认为这是在骗人","认为完全没有必要","认为有实际作用","认为只对猴子有用"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing lines treat it as a real feature of how people listen — 误会并非来自事情本身，而是来自说话的顺序 — not as trickery."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这个寓言讲的是猴子分橡子的故事。","他说话的方式很客气，大家都愿意听。","请把完整的计划发给我，我需要看整体。","家里开始节省用电，每个月省下不少钱。","同事之间相处得好，工作会轻松很多。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Think of a message you had to deliver at work or at home — a change, a limit, a no. Describe how you phrased it the first time and what you changed. Use the words below.","required_words":["整体","节省","方式","相处"],"min_chars":80,"model":"家里去年开始记账。刚开始，我们只盯着少买了什么，谁都不高兴。后来换了一种方式：先看完整的收入，再看可以节省的地方。这样讨论起来气氛好多了，也没有人觉得自己吃亏。人和人相处也是这样，先让对方看到整体，再谈具体的要求，对方就比较容易接受。","tips":"Start with the situation and the first, clumsy attempt. Then give the concrete re-ordering you tried, with one detail. Finish with the general lesson in a single short sentence."}},{"n":9,"zh":"别样鲁迅","en":"The Lu Xun You Don't Know","book":1,"theme":"Another side of a familiar kind of person: a street-corner pastry shop and its reserved owner, judged by what he does rather than how warm he looks.","grammar":{"id":"g09","point":"除非……否则……","point_en":"unless A, otherwise B","structure":"除非 + the only exception + 否则 + the bad outcome","explain_en":"除非……否则…… means 'unless A, otherwise B'. It isolates the one exception that would prevent B, then states B — the outcome that will happen in every other case. The 除非 clause comes first; 否则 opens the second clause and introduces the unwanted result, usually with 会, 就 or 很难. 除非 is the only partner for 否则 in this frame, and 否则 may not be replaced by 就 or 所以. A second, positive version exists: 除非 can be answered by 才 when the exception leads to a good result (除非你亲自去，他才会同意). Compare 只有……才……, which presents the single way to get something done and sounds insistent; 除非……否则…… is framed around what goes wrong if that one condition is missing, so it reads like a warning or a rule of thumb. In conversation 不然 and 要不 can stand in for 否则, and 除非 may be followed by 是 (除非是你亲自去). Keep the second clause in plain declarative order after 否则.","common_mistake":"The classic error is to mix the two frames: 除非你提前说，我就没办法安排 and 只有你提前说，否则没办法安排 are both wrong. 除非 pairs with 否则 (or 才), 只有 pairs with 才, and 否则 must open the second clause rather than sit inside it.","examples":[{"zh":"除非你每天亲自做，否则很难做出这个味道。","py":"chú fēi nǐ měi tiān qīn zì zuò fǒu zé hěn nán zuò chū zhè ge wèi dào","en":"Unless you make it yourself every day, it is hard to get this flavour."},{"zh":"除非老板同意，否则这个计划不能改。","py":"chú fēi lǎo bǎn tóng yì fǒu zé zhè ge jì huà bù néng gǎi","en":"Unless the boss agrees, the plan cannot be changed."},{"zh":"除非把资料看完，否则讨论没有意义。","py":"chú fēi bǎ zī liào kàn wán fǒu zé tǎo lùn méi yǒu yì yì","en":"Unless the material has been read, the discussion is pointless."}],"drills":[{"q":"这件事必须今天做完，____就要影响下周的计划了。","options":["否则","因此","而且","哪怕"],"answer":0,"explain":"否则 means 'otherwise' and introduces the result of not doing what was just stated. 因此 draws a conclusion from what has already happened, not from what has not; 而且 adds information; 哪怕 opens a concessive clause (哪怕……也……)."},{"q":"除非老板亲自同意，____。","options":["否则谁也不能改这个计划","所以谁也不能改这个计划","因此谁也不能改这个计划","而且谁也不能改这个计划"],"answer":0,"explain":"除非 must be completed by 否则, which states what holds in every case other than the exception. 所以 and 因此 report the result of a cause already given as fact, which is the 因为……所以…… frame, and 而且 simply adds a further point."}]},"reading":{"title":"看起来冷的人","text":"我们单位旁边有一家很小的点心店，开在一条老胡同里，店面不大，装修也谈不上豪华。老板是位六十多岁的先生，话很少，表情总是淡淡的。第一次去的人，常常以为他不太欢迎客人。\n\n后来熟了才知道，他年轻时做过编辑，收藏了很多旧资料，对老北京的饭菜讲究得很。哪位客人第一次光临，他都会亲自端上一碟刚做好的点心，然后站在一边，听别人说好不好吃。作为一位好客的人，他很少大声招呼，也不喜欢交际，可是谁家有困难，他从来不小气。\n\n有人形容他像一个旧时代的人。他听了只是笑，说这样的形象挺好。他常说，做点心这件事，除非你每天亲自做，否则很难做好。明明是很小的一家店，却让人愿意一年一年地回去。","translation":"Next to my office there is a very small pastry shop down an old alley. The front is cramped and the decoration is nothing anyone would call luxurious. The owner is a man in his sixties who says little and whose face is always rather flat. People going in for the first time often assume he does not want customers.\n\nAfter a while you learn that he worked as an editor when he was young, that he has kept a large collection of old documents, and that he is extremely particular about old Beijing cooking. When a customer comes in for the first time, he carries over a plate of freshly made pastries himself and then stands to one side, listening to whether people like them. For a hospitable man he greets people quietly and dislikes small talk, yet no neighbour in trouble has ever found him stingy.\n\nSomeone once described him as a man from another age. He only laughed and said he liked that image. He often says that when it comes to pastries, unless you make them yourself every day, it is hard to do them well. The shop is small indeed, and yet you want to come back, year after year.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想说的是____。","options":["老胡同里的小店越来越少","第一次见面很难看清一个人","做点心需要很多旧资料","装修豪华的店更受欢迎"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage spends its first paragraph on the cold first impression and the rest overturning it, and ends with people returning year after year — the point is that a first look does not settle who someone is."},{"q":"文中说，老板年轻时做过____。","options":["老师","编辑","厨师","司机"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph states 他年轻时做过编辑，收藏了很多旧资料."},{"q":"老板说“这样的形象挺好”，说明他____。","options":["不喜欢别人夸他","认可自己像旧时代的人","希望店里装修得更好","不愿意再跟客人说话"],"answer":1,"explain":"He answers the description with a laugh and agreement, so he accepts the image rather than resisting it."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这家点心店开在一条老胡同里。","他亲自做的点心，味道一直没变。","欢迎光临，请随便看看，不要客气。","他对吃什么很讲究，也很少在外面吃饭。","我曾经去过那家店，老板非常大方。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about someone you misjudged at first — a quiet colleague, a strict manager, a shop owner. Show the first impression and the moment it changed. Use the words below.","required_words":["表现","讲究","亲自","曾经"],"min_chars":80,"model":"刚进公司时，我以为老张是个不好相处的人。他很少说话，会议上几乎没有什么表现，别人都觉得他很冷。后来我跟着他做项目，才发现他做事非常讲究：资料按日期保存，每个数字都要亲自核对。他曾经说过，工作做得好不好，客人第一次来就能感觉到。原来安静的人，往往把力气都用在了事情上。","tips":"Give the flat first impression in two sentences, then one concrete scene that corrects it. Keep the closing observation short and let the detail do the arguing."}},{"n":10,"zh":"争论的奇迹","en":"Miracle of Debate","book":1,"theme":"A neighbourhood argument over a sports ground that turned productive once the group agreed on what they already shared.","grammar":{"id":"g10","point":"既然……就……","point_en":"since A, then B","structure":"既然 + accepted fact + 就 + conclusion or next step","explain_en":"既然……就…… links a premise the speaker treats as already true and already known to both sides to the conclusion, advice or next step that follows from it: 'since A, then B'. 既然 opens the first clause, or comes right after its subject (你既然……); 就 comes after the subject of the second clause and before its predicate. In speech 既然 can also be answered by 那么, or by nothing at all, but 就 is the normal written partner. Compare 因为……所以……: 因为 introduces a cause the listener may not know and the sentence explains why something happened or is true; 既然 takes the fact as granted and then moves forward, so the second clause is usually a decision, a suggestion or a question. Compare 如果……就……, which is a pure hypothesis and may be wrong about reality. Word order is fixed: 既然 never follows the verb, and 就 cannot open the sentence in front of the second subject.","common_mistake":"Learners translate 既然 as a plain 'because' and attach 所以, producing 既然你病了，所以你休息吧. The reason is already marked by 既然, so the second clause needs 就 — or no connector at all — and never 所以.","examples":[{"zh":"既然大家都同意，就不用再讨论了。","py":"jì rán dà jiā dōu tóng yì jiù bú yòng zài tǎo lùn le","en":"Since everyone agrees, there is no need to discuss it any further."},{"zh":"你既然知道问题在哪里，就早点改。","py":"nǐ jì rán zhī dào wèn tí zài nǎ lǐ jiù zǎo diǎn gǎi","en":"Since you know where the problem is, fix it early."},{"zh":"既然试验已经做完，就按结果改进吧。","py":"jì rán shì yàn yǐ jīng zuò wán jiù àn jié guǒ gǎi jìn ba","en":"Since the trial is finished, let us improve it according to the results."}],"drills":[{"q":"____你已经把资料看完了，____说说你的判断吧。","options":["既然……就……","只有……才……","与其……不如……","除了……还……"],"answer":0,"explain":"The first clause states something both sides already accept and the second asks for a conclusion, which is the job of 既然……就……. 只有……才…… would put 才 in front of an imperative (才说说), which 才 cannot do; 与其……不如…… compares two options; 除了……还…… adds an item to an existing one."},{"q":"既然你已经决定了，____。","options":["就直接去做吧","所以就直接去做吧","因为就直接去做吧","而就直接去做吧"],"answer":0,"explain":"既然 already marks the reason, so the second clause simply follows with 就; adding 所以 would double the connector and belongs to the 因为……所以…… frame. 因为 cannot open a result clause, and 而 only links parallel or contrastive items."}]},"reading":{"title":"争出来的方案","text":"去年夏天，我们组为社区要不要修一个操场争了整整两周。有人担心孩子奔跑时太吵，有人觉得那块空地闲着可惜。会议一开始，大家围绕图纸各说各的，谁也说服不了谁。\n\n第三周，组长换了做法。他先请每个人写下一条自己最在意的担心，再把大家意见一致的部分标出来。这时我才意识到，多数人的想法并没有那么大的差距，真正对不上的只有两点。\n\n既然安全是大家都同意的前提，就先把两种方案各做一个小试验。试验只用了两周，问题就显示出来了：操场离楼房太近，拍球的声音确实很响。方案逐渐改进，最后大家都点了头。\n\n这次争论让我明白，好的讨论不靠声音大，而靠把事实放上桌面。毕竟大家要的是同一件事。","translation":"Last summer our team argued for two solid weeks about whether the neighbourhood should build a sports ground. Some worried it would be too noisy with children running about; others thought it a shame to leave the empty lot unused. From the first meeting everyone talked around the drawings, and nobody convinced anybody.\n\nIn the third week the team leader changed tack. He asked each person to write down the one worry they cared about most, then marked the points everyone agreed on. Only then did I realise that most of us were not far apart at all — the genuine disagreements were just two.\n\nSince safety was a premise everyone accepted, we first ran one small trial of each design. The trial took two weeks and the problem showed up immediately: the court was too close to the buildings and the sound of a bouncing ball really did carry. The plan was gradually improved, and in the end everyone nodded.\n\nThat argument taught me that a good discussion does not depend on who is loudest but on putting the facts on the table. After all, we wanted the same thing.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要讲的是____。","options":["社区操场是怎么修起来的","一场争论怎样变成有用的讨论","孩子为什么喜欢在操场玩","组长怎样批评自己的同事"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage follows the argument from deadlock to agreement and ends by naming what made the difference, so the process of the argument is the subject."},{"q":"第三周，组长让每个人先写下____。","options":["自己最担心的一个问题","自己最喜欢的方案","自己对组长的意见","自己周末的安排"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 他先请每个人写下一条自己最在意的担心."},{"q":"从文章看，作者认为好的讨论主要靠____。","options":["声音比别人大","经验比别人多","把事实摆出来","组长直接做决定"],"answer":2,"explain":"The last paragraph sets 不靠声音大 against 靠把事实放上桌面, which is the author's own conclusion."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这次争论没有结果，大家都很累。","我们先做一次小试验，再决定用哪个方案。","两个人的差距没有想象中那么大。","我逐渐意识到，问题出在沟通上。","他花了一个小时，终于说服了对方。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe an argument at work where both sides had good reasons. Explain how the disagreement was settled and what you would do sooner next time. Use the words below.","required_words":["争论","试验","改进","毕竟"],"min_chars":80,"model":"上个月我和同事为一个页面该怎么排争论了三天。他觉得标题放在下面，我认为放在上面更清楚，谁也说服不了谁。后来我们做了一个小试验：请五位同事分别用两个版本做同一个任务，大家都能更快找到上面的按钮。我们照结果改进，事情当天就定了。毕竟争论不是目的，谁的想法更好，试一下就知道。","tips":"Open with the deadlock in one or two sentences, then show the test that broke it and what the result was. Close on the general rule you now follow."}},{"n":11,"zh":"闹钟的危害","en":"Harm of Alarm Clocks","book":1,"theme":"What a loud alarm does to the first hours of your morning, and how light and a steady schedule do the same job more gently.","grammar":{"id":"g11","point":"一……就……","point_en":"as soon as A, then B","structure":"subject + 一 + verb 1 + (subject 2) + 就 + verb 2","explain_en":"一……就…… marks two things happening immediately one after the other: as soon as the first action happens, the second follows. 一 sits directly in front of the first verb; 就 comes before the second verb, after the second subject when the two subjects differ (他一说，我就明白了). The same frame also describes a standing habit — whenever A happens, B always follows (他一喝酒脸就红) — and a reaction you cannot control (一说到考试，我就紧张). When both clauses share one subject, put the subject at the front and keep 一 next to the verb: 我一进门就看见他, not 一我一进门就……. Compare 刚……就……, which reports a past sequence where the first action had only just finished, so it is tied to a single moment; 一……就…… is not tied to the past and is the natural choice for rules, habits and general statements. Compare 如果……就……, which leaves the first event as a possibility instead of presenting it as immediate.","common_mistake":"A common error is to slide a time word between 一 and the verb: 我一昨天就见过他. 一 must touch the verb itself, so the time word moves outside the frame. Learners also write 才 in the second clause, which reverses the immediacy the pattern is built on.","examples":[{"zh":"他一进门就发现气氛不对。","py":"tā yí jìn mén jiù fā xiàn qì fēn bú duì","en":"The moment he came in, he sensed that the mood was wrong."},{"zh":"铃声一响，我就坐了起来。","py":"líng shēng yì xiǎng wǒ jiù zuò le qǐ lái","en":"As soon as the bell rang, I sat up."},{"zh":"这个孩子一看见水就不肯走。","py":"zhè ge hái zi yí kàn jiàn shuǐ jiù bù kěn zǒu","en":"The moment this child sees water, he refuses to leave."}],"drills":[{"q":"他____听到这个数字就皱起了眉头。","options":["一","也","再","又"],"answer":0,"explain":"一 before the first verb plus 就 before the second is the frame for an immediate reaction. 也 would need a parallel clause or 无论……都……, 再 marks repetition or a future 'again', and 又 marks a repeated past action — none of them pairs with 就 to express immediacy."},{"q":"他一听到这个消息，____坐不住了。","options":["才","就","还","再"],"answer":1,"explain":"一 in the first clause is answered by 就 in the second. 才 belongs with 只有 or 除非 and would reverse the relation; 还 marks continuation or 'still' and does not fit a single reaction; 再 marks repetition or a future 'again'."}]},"reading":{"title":"别让铃声打断睡眠","text":"我以前的闹钟声音很大，放在枕头旁边，每天早上都像被推了一把。铃声一响，我立刻就坐起来，人还没醒，心已经开始快跳。\n\n后来我发现，这样醒来的头两个小时，几乎没法思考。开会时能听见别人说话，却常常记不住内容。一位研究睡眠的朋友说，这不是懒，是身体还没有准备好。\n\n人从睡着到清醒需要一个过渡。早上被突然叫醒，大脑还停在浅睡状态，呼吸和心跳都没调整过来，情绪自然容易低落。光线比铃声柔和得多，也更容易让身体慢慢醒过来。这些危害看着不大，累起来却并不小。\n\n现在我换了个办法：晚上把窗帘留一条缝，早上让光线进来；闹钟改成很轻的音乐，时间往后放十分钟。我做了个实验，坚持三个星期，起不来的次数少了很多。睡眠有它自己的规律，我们能做的，是尽量不去打断它。","translation":"My old alarm clock was very loud and sat right by the pillow, so every morning felt like being shoved. The moment the bell rang I sat up at once — my body still asleep, my heart already racing.\n\nLater I noticed that for the first two hours after waking that way I could barely think. In meetings I could hear other people talking but often could not remember what they said. A friend who studies sleep told me it was not laziness; the body simply was not ready.\n\nGoing from asleep to awake takes a transition. Woken abruptly in the morning, the brain is still in light sleep, breathing and heartbeat have not adjusted, and the mood drops easily. Light is far gentler than a bell, and it brings the body round more easily. These harms look small, but added up day after day they are not small at all.\n\nSo I changed two things: at night I leave a gap in the curtains so that light comes in in the morning, and the alarm is now very soft music set ten minutes later. I ran a small experiment for three weeks, and the number of mornings I could not get up dropped a lot. Sleep has its own regular pattern; what we can do is try not to interrupt it.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想说明____。","options":["现代人应该完全不用闹钟","被突然叫醒会影响早上的状态","音乐比光线更让人清醒","早起的人身体一定更好"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second and third paragraphs describe the foggy mornings and the transition the body needs, and the last paragraph offers a gentler way to wake — the harm of abrupt waking is the subject."},{"q":"作者现在早上靠____醒过来。","options":["很响的闹钟铃声","朋友打来的电话","窗帘透进来的光线和轻音乐","每天自然睡到八点"],"answer":2,"explain":"The last paragraph lists both changes: 窗帘留一条缝，让光线进来 and 闹钟改成很轻的音乐."},{"q":"从文章看，作者对睡眠规律的态度是____。","options":["应该完全取消闹钟","应该顺着身体自己的规律","应该多做实验改造习惯","应该每天晚起一个小时"],"answer":1,"explain":"The closing line — 我们能做的，是尽量不去打断它 — shows acceptance of the body's own rhythm rather than a fight against it."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["我的闹钟声音太大，每天早上都被吓醒。","拉开窗帘，让光线进来，人会清醒得快一些。","快走几步，呼吸会变得深一点。","他的情绪不好，可能跟最近睡得太少有关。","生活有规律，身体的状态才会稳定。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe your own morning routine and one change you made to it. Was it worth the trouble? Write for a colleague who keeps hitting snooze. Use the words below.","required_words":["闹钟","清醒","情绪","规律"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我以前的闹钟放在枕头边上，声音很响。每天早上一响，我就跳起来，可是人并不清醒，情绪也很差，到了下午才慢慢好起来。后来我做了两个改变：把闹钟换成轻一点的声音，晚上固定时间关灯。开始时很难，坚持三周以后，早上醒得比闹钟还早。规律的生活看起来慢，其实省下了很多力气。","tips":"Set the old routine first, then the change and how long it took to work. End with a plain sentence on what you gained, not a lecture."}},{"n":12,"zh":"海外用户玩儿微信","en":"Overseas Users of WeChat","book":1,"theme":"How a small app team learned that going abroad means rebuilding the product around local habits, not just translating it.","grammar":{"id":"g12","point":"越……越……","point_en":"the more A, the more B","structure":"越 + change 1 + 越 + change 2","explain_en":"越……越…… links two changes that move together: the more A, the more B. Each clause carries its own 越, placed directly before the adjective or verb it changes, and the two halves sit in one sentence without any other connective. When the two subjects are different, the second subject comes before the second 越: 你说得越多，我越糊涂. When both clauses share a subject, the subject may stand at the very front (我越说越糊涂) or be repeated. The second clause often takes 就 for emphasis — 越……就越…… — and 是 can be added for weight (越是忙，越要小心). Compare 越来越, which has a single 越 and describes one thing changing over time without linking it to a second change: 天气越来越热 simply reports a trend. Do not double up 越来越 inside the two-part frame. Compare 一……就……, which is about immediate sequence, not proportional change.","common_mistake":"The typical slip is to write 越来越 in both halves — 越来越便宜，越来越多人买 — which gives two separate trends instead of one dependent pair. Each clause needs one plain 越: 越便宜，买的人越多.","examples":[{"zh":"越早开始准备，后面越轻松。","py":"yuè zǎo kāi shǐ zhǔn bèi hòu miàn yuè qīng sōng","en":"The earlier you start preparing, the easier things are later."},{"zh":"他越解释，我越不明白。","py":"tā yuè jiě shì wǒ yuè bù míng bai","en":"The more he explained, the less I understood."},{"zh":"这个软件用得越多，越觉得好用。","py":"zhè ge ruǎn jiàn yòng de yuè duō yuè jué de hǎo yòng","en":"The more you use this software, the better it seems."}],"drills":[{"q":"____往后拖，这件事____难办。","options":["越……越……","越来越……","越……越来越……","越来越……越来越……"],"answer":0,"explain":"The frame is exactly 越 + A + 越 + B, one 越 in each clause. 越来越 takes a single adjective and reports a trend over time (越来越难办), so it has no second half to open a two-part sentence, and the mixed forms in the other two options are not patterns at all."},{"q":"你说得越快，我____听不清楚。","options":["更","最","越","太"],"answer":2,"explain":"The first clause already carries 越, so the second needs its own 越 before the predicate to complete the pair. 更, 最 and 太 are plain degree adverbs: 最 cannot describe a two-way correlation at all, and the other two leave the frame unfinished."}]},"reading":{"title":"从“能用”到“好用”","text":"朋友在一家做手机应用的公司上班。三年前，他们开始把产品带向海外，第一批用户来自东南亚。刚开始，团队的想法很简单：把国内的版本翻译成英文，能注册、能聊天就够了。\n\n真正上线以后，问题一个接一个。当地网络还不发达，图片经常打不开；用户习惯在手机上付钱，他们却没有准备好；客服只会说中文，一个问题常常要等两天。\n\n公司召开了几次会，决定从头改。产品经理去当地的市场待了两个月，回来重新设计了界面，又请本地人参与测试。推广也换了方式：短视频里请本地的小明星做示范，效果比广告好得多。\n\n一年以后，我最明显的感受是：用户越容易上手，就越愿意把朋友也拉进来。现在这款应用的业务覆盖了好几个国家，团队也比原来大了好几倍。","translation":"A friend of mine works at a company that makes a phone app. Three years ago they began taking the product overseas, starting with users in Southeast Asia. At first the team's thinking was simple: translate the Chinese version into English, and as long as people can register and chat, that is enough.\n\nOnce it actually launched, problems came one after another. Local networks were not yet well developed and pictures often failed to load; users were used to paying on their phones and the company was not ready for that; customer service spoke only Chinese, so a single question could take two days.\n\nAfter several meetings the company decided to rebuild from the start. The product manager went to the local market and stayed two months; when he came back the interface was redesigned and local people were brought in to test it. Promotion changed too: in short videos, small local celebrities demonstrated it, and that worked far better than advertising.\n\nA year on, what strikes me most is this: the easier users find the app, the more willing they are to pull their friends in. Today the business covers quite a few countries, and the team is several times larger than it was.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要讲的是____。","options":["一家公司怎样把产品改到适合当地用户","短视频为什么比广告更受欢迎","出国工作会遇到哪些困难","手机应用靠什么赚钱"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage runs from the naive translate-only plan through the launch problems to the local rebuild, so the subject is adapting the product to the people who use it."},{"q":"文中说，产品刚上线时，当地用户习惯____。","options":["用电脑上网找工作","在手机上付钱","写信联系客服","不用手机看视频"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph says 用户习惯在手机上付钱，他们却没有准备好."},{"q":"从最后一段看，作者认为用户愿意留下来的原因是____。","options":["广告投入比较大","请明星做代言","觉得用起来容易","价格比别人便宜"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing lines tie growth to 用户越容易上手，就越愿意把朋友也拉进来: people stay because the app is easy to use. Advertising and price are not part of that conclusion."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["新用户只要填一个手机号就能注册。","我们下个月开始在当地推广新产品。","这个功能是去年开发的，用起来很方便。","两家公司合作以后，业务增长得很快。","这个应用的市场主要在东南亚。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a product, a service or a document that worked for your team but confused outsiders. What did you change, and what did you learn about your users? Use the words below.","required_words":["用户","当地","推广","合作"],"min_chars":80,"model":"去年我们做了一款小工具，最早只在公司内部用。后来决定推广出去，才发现问题很多：界面上的说法，新用户看不明白。我们找了一家当地的公司合作，请他们的员工先试用，再把意见一条一条改掉。半年以后，新的用户第一次就能自己完成注册。越了解用户，越知道该改哪里。","tips":"Start with what worked inside and failed outside, then the concrete fix. End by naming the general lesson in one short 越……越…… sentence."}},{"n":13,"zh":"锯掉生活的“筐底”","en":"Cutting Off the “Bottom of the Basket” in Life","book":1,"theme":"How one engineer questioned a step nobody could justify, and what a basketball basket with no bottom has to do with it.","grammar":{"id":"g13","point":"由于……而……","point_en":"because of X, and therefore Y (formal written cause and result)","structure":"主语 + 由于 + 原因 + 而 + 结果（动词短语）","explain_en":"Use 由于……而…… when you want to give a reason and its result inside one sentence, in a formal or written register. The reason follows 由于, and 而 introduces the verb phrase that shows the result; you do not add 所以. The subject normally sits before 由于, and 而 must stay close to the verb: 由于准备不足而推迟. Compare it with 因为……所以……, which is neutral, spoken-friendly and takes a full clause after 所以. 由于……而…… is tighter: it combines cause and consequence into a single predicate, so it suits reports, news items and essays. Do not put a comma plus a new subject right after 而, because 而 needs a verb or adjective phrase that continues the same subject. The result after 而 is often something unwanted or outside the speaker's control, though neutral results are possible; the whole sentence sounds objective rather than emotional.","common_mistake":"Learners often add 所以 after 而 (由于下雨而所以推迟), or drop a fresh subject after 而. Remember: 由于 supplies the cause, 而 introduces the result verb phrase, and no 所以 is needed.","examples":[{"zh":"他由于缺乏经验而一再重复同样的错误。","py":"tā yóu yú quē fá jīng yàn ér yí zài chóng fù tóng yàng de cuò wù","en":"Because he lacked experience, he repeated the same mistakes again and again."},{"zh":"这个项目由于预算不足而推迟了两个月。","py":"zhè ge xiàng mù yóu yú yù suàn bù zú ér tuī chí le liǎng ge yuè","en":"The project was delayed by two months because the budget fell short."},{"zh":"会议由于时间关系而提前结束。","py":"huì yì yóu yú shí jiān guān xì ér tí qián jié shù","en":"The meeting ended early because of time constraints."}],"drills":[{"q":"球队____训练不足而在下半场失去了主动。","options":["由于","因此","虽然","所以"],"answer":0,"explain":"由于 introduces the cause 训练不足, and 而 later carries the result. 因此 and 所以 are result connectives and cannot open a cause clause, while 虽然 marks concession and would leave the following 而 with nothing to explain."},{"q":"这支队伍由于准备充分____在比赛中一直很主动。","options":["而","而且","然而","并且"],"answer":0,"explain":"而 links 由于准备充分 to the result verb phrase 在比赛中一直很主动. 而且 and 并且 join two full clauses and would need their own subject, and 然而 marks contrast, which does not fit a cause and result link."}]},"reading":{"title":"没必要的那一步","text":"公司去年调整了报销流程，可新流程反而多出三步。李工是负责这个项目的工程师，做事一向认真，却一再被这些步骤困扰。有一次开会，他忍不住问：“这一步为什么要重复做？”会议室里安静了几秒，气氛有些尴尬。没有人答得上来，大家只知道以前的同事就是这么做事的。\n\n李工是个球迷，周末常看球，也陪孩子练习投篮。他忽然想到一个比方：如果篮球筐底下是封着的，每投进一个球都得有人爬上去取，比赛怎么可能顺畅？多亏有人用锯子把筐底锯掉，比赛才快了起来。\n\n项目组由于说不清这几步的用处而决定先停掉它们。一个月后，报表错得少了，同事之间也轻松了不少。李工说，真正阻碍我们的，往往不是缺少工具，而是那些没人再问一句“为什么”的老习惯。","translation":"Last year the company changed its expense-reimbursement process, and the new version somehow ended up with three extra steps. Li is the engineer in charge of the project. He is careful by nature, yet those steps troubled him time and again. In one meeting he finally asked, “Why do we do this step twice?” For a few seconds the room was quiet and the atmosphere was a little awkward. Nobody could answer; all anyone knew was that earlier colleagues had always done it that way.\n\nLi is a basketball fan who watches games at weekends and practises shooting with his child. A comparison came to him: if the bottom of a basketball basket were sealed, someone would have to climb up and fetch the ball after every shot, so how could the game ever run smoothly? It took someone with a saw to cut the bottom out, and only then did the game speed up.\n\nBecause nobody could explain what those steps were for, the project team decided to suspend them first. A month later the reports had fewer mistakes, and people got along more easily. What really blocks us, Li says, is often not a shortage of tools but an old habit that nobody has asked “why” about for years.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想告诉读者____。","options":["老习惯不一定合理，值得问一句为什么","报销流程越简单，公司效率就越高","篮球比赛的规则需要不断修改","年轻员工应该多听老同事的意见"],"answer":0,"explain":"The last paragraph states the point directly: what blocks us is often an old habit nobody has questioned, not a lack of tools."},{"q":"会上没有人回答李工的问题，是因为____。","options":["大家对这一步的用途并不清楚","大家觉得李工的问题太简单","会议时间不够，来不及讨论","这一步刚刚才被取消掉"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage says nobody could answer and that people only knew earlier colleagues had done it this way."},{"q":"一个月后的情况说明，停掉那几步____。","options":["并没有让工作变得糟糕","让报表的错误更多了","让同事之间出现矛盾","只对少数人有帮助"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage reports fewer mistakes in the reports and easier relations between colleagues, so removing the steps did no harm."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这台机器是上周安装好的，运行一直很顺畅。","他由于缺少训练而在比赛中一再重复错误。","讨论得越激烈，会议室里的气氛就越紧张。","这些工具是给新来的工程师准备的。","他好奇地瞧了一眼，连忙跑过去扶住栏杆。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Think of a rule or habit at work that nobody can explain. Where did it come from, and what happened when someone questioned it? Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["项目","重复","顺畅","启发"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我们组的周报原来要填十几项，其中三项的内容几乎重复。我问过老同事，没人说得出理由，只知道一直是这样。上个月，我把这三项合成一项，先在小项目里试了两周。结果并没有人抱怨，写报告的时间也少了不少。我的启发是：规则需要定期更新，顺畅的流程不是靠多加一步，而是靠去掉没用的那一步。","tips":"Open with the rule itself, then give one concrete scene in which you asked about it. Close with what changed, or with the question you still keep asking."}},{"n":14,"zh":"北京的四合院","en":"Quadrangle Courtyards in Beijing","book":1,"theme":"An afternoon in an old courtyard home, and why its shared yard still makes people feel close.","grammar":{"id":"g14","point":"之所以……是因为……","point_en":"the reason that X is so is that Y","structure":"之所以 + 结果 + 是因为 + 原因","explain_en":"之所以……是因为…… puts the result first and explains it afterwards, so the listener hears the effect before the cause. 之所以 opens the sentence (or follows the subject) and marks the result; 是因为 introduces the reason and answers the question that the first half has just raised. Use it when you want to explain, defend or analyse something rather than simply report it, for instance 这座院子之所以受欢迎，是因为…… . It differs from 因为……所以…… in emphasis: 因为……所以…… moves forward from cause to effect in a neutral way, while 之所以……是因为…… moves backwards, putting the fact on the table before justifying it. The two halves share the same subject, and the second half can be emphasised with 就是因为 when you want to stress the cause. Do not use 所以 in the second half, and do not reverse the two halves.","common_mistake":"The usual error is to reverse the order and write 是因为……之所以……, or to keep 所以 after 是因为. Start with the result, then explain it with 是因为.","examples":[{"zh":"这种民居之所以受欢迎，是因为它住起来很方便。","py":"zhè zhǒng mín jū zhī suǒ yǐ shòu huān yíng shì yīn wèi tā zhù qǐ lái hěn fāng biàn","en":"This kind of dwelling is popular because it is convenient to live in."},{"zh":"他之所以没有参加会议，是因为临时有客户来访。","py":"tā zhī suǒ yǐ méi yǒu cān jiā huì yì shì yīn wèi lín shí yǒu kè hù lái fǎng","en":"The reason he missed the meeting was that a client turned up at short notice."},{"zh":"老房子之所以让人留恋，是因为里面有很多人共同生活的记忆。","py":"lǎo fáng zi zhī suǒ yǐ ràng rén liú liàn shì yīn wèi lǐ miàn yǒu hěn duō rén gòng tóng shēng huó de jì yì","en":"Old houses are hard to leave behind because they hold the memory of many people living together."}],"drills":[{"q":"这座老院子____还有人愿意住，是因为它冬暖夏凉。","options":["之所以","是因为","因此","虽然"],"answer":0,"explain":"之所以 marks the result that the second half explains with 是因为. 是因为 would repeat the marker, 因此 introduces a consequence rather than a fact to be explained, and 虽然 marks concession."},{"q":"这座院子之所以让人住得舒服，____它的空间安排很合理。","options":["是因为","所以","因此","何况"],"answer":0,"explain":"是因为 follows 之所以 to name the reason. 所以 and 因此 would present the second half as a result, reversing the logic, and 何况 means let alone, which cannot introduce a cause."}]},"reading":{"title":"院子里的那杯茶","text":"去年秋天，我去同事老周家做客。他住在一座老四合院里，院子不大，却收拾得很干净。\n\n一进大门，先是一条短短的走廊，两边是东西厢房。北房通常留给家里的长辈，东、西厢房则由年轻的一代居住。四座房子围住院子，组合成一个方正的空间。院里种着竹子，墙角有一缸金鱼，太阳一出来，水面亮亮的，很有情趣。\n\n老周说，这种民居之所以让人留恋，是因为一家人的日常起居都在同一个院子里：谁家做了好吃的，邻居隔着墙就能闻见香味；孩子放学回来，在院子里写作业，也不用大人一直看着。关上院门，世界安静下来，却并不封闭。\n\n我坐在院子里喝完一杯茶，觉得这种建筑最珍贵的地方不是样式，而是它给人的那份亲切。","translation":"Last autumn I went to my colleague Zhou's home for tea. He lives in an old quadrangle courtyard; the yard is small but kept very tidy.\n\nBeyond the gate there is a short corridor with the east and west wing rooms on either side. The north room is usually kept for the elders of the family, while the east and west wings are lived in by the younger generation. Four buildings around the yard combine into a square space. Bamboo grows in the yard and a jar of goldfish stands in the corner; once the sun is out the water shines, and the place has real charm.\n\nZhou says the reason this kind of dwelling is hard to leave is that the whole family's daily life happens in one yard. When someone cooks something good, the neighbours can smell it through the wall; when the children come home from school they do their homework in the yard, and no adult has to watch them all the time. With the gate shut, the world goes quiet, but the yard is not sealed off.\n\nI finished a cup of tea in the yard and felt that the most precious thing about this architecture is not its style but the warmth it gives people.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["一座四合院里的居住生活","北京老房子的建筑历史","老周一家搬家的原因","城市里新的住房样式"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage follows a visit to one courtyard home and describes the yard, the rooms and the family life inside it."},{"q":"根据文章，北房通常住的是____。","options":["家里的长辈","年轻的一代","来做客的同事","放学回来的孩子"],"answer":0,"explain":"The second paragraph says 北房通常留给家里的长辈, while the younger generation lives in the east and west wings."},{"q":"从“关上院门……却并不封闭”可以看出，作者认为这种院子____。","options":["安静，但人和人之间并不疏远","太封闭，不适合年轻人住","只有老人才会觉得舒服","需要重新设计和改造"],"answer":0,"explain":"The gate shuts out noise, yet neighbours still smell each other's cooking and children play in the shared yard, so the life inside stays open."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这座四合院已经有八十多年的历史了。","院子的两边是厢房，中间是一条走廊。","长辈们通常起得很早，喜欢在院子里劳动。","屋里的空间不大，布置得却很有情趣。","这种民居的样式很常见，功能也很实用。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a home or building you remember well. What did its layout make you feel? Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["建筑","空间","情趣","亲切"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我小时候住的是单位分的楼房，三间屋子连在一起，空间并不大。厨房在走廊尽头，谁家做饭，整层楼都能闻到。邻居们常在楼道里聊天，孩子们在楼梯口写作业。那座建筑很普通，样式也谈不上好看，可是它有一种特别的情趣：人和人离得很近。现在回想起来，最让我怀念的不是房子，而是那份亲切。","tips":"Name the building first, then describe one or two concrete parts of its layout. Close with the feeling those details still leave you with."}},{"n":15,"zh":"纸上谈兵","en":"Being an Armchair Strategist","book":1,"theme":"A half-day business simulation in which the strongest theorist on the team learns what happens when the facts change.","grammar":{"id":"g15","point":"因此 / 因而 / 从而","point_en":"therefore; as a result; and thereby","structure":"原因或做法 + 因此/因而/从而 + 结果","explain_en":"All three words introduce a result, but they are not interchangeable. 因此 and 因而 are close to “therefore”: the first half gives a cause or a fact, and the second half gives the consequence. 因此 is the most common in written and semi-formal Chinese and can follow either a comma or a full stop; 因而 is a little more literary, usually keeps both halves inside one sentence and often pairs with 由于. 从而 is different: it links a means or a step to the result achieved by it, so the first half must be something someone did, and the second half is what that action produced — 他改进了流程，从而减少了错误. With 从而 the two halves normally share a subject, and it cannot be used when the first half is only a situation or a state. In short: use 因此 and 因而 for cause and effect, and 从而 for means and result.","common_mistake":"The classic mistake is to use 从而 for a plain cause, as in 昨天下雨，从而比赛取消了, where rain is a situation rather than a method. Use 因此 or 因而 there, and keep 从而 for an action that produces a result.","examples":[{"zh":"他没有检查数据，因此报告里出现了两个错误。","py":"tā méi yǒu jiǎn chá shù jù yīn cǐ bào gào lǐ chū xiàn le liǎng ge cuò wù","en":"He did not check the figures, so two errors appeared in the report."},{"zh":"由于准备得比较充分，因而这次演练非常顺利。","py":"yóu yú zhǔn bèi de bǐ jiào chōng fèn yīn ér zhè cì yǎn liàn fēi cháng shùn lì","en":"Because the preparation was fairly thorough, the exercise went very smoothly."},{"zh":"公司简化了审批步骤，从而缩短了项目的时间。","py":"gōng sī jiǎn huà le shěn pī bù zhòu cóng ér suō duǎn le xiàng mù de shí jiān","en":"The company simplified its approval steps and thereby shortened the project timeline."}],"drills":[{"q":"昨天下了一夜的大雨，____比赛推迟了一天。","options":["因此","从而","何况","甚至"],"answer":0,"explain":"因此 reports the consequence of a situation. 从而 needs the first half to be an action taken in order to achieve something, but a night of rain is a situation, not a method; 何况 and 甚至 do not introduce a result."},{"q":"他把每次会议的记录整理成模板，____让新同事也能很快上手。","options":["从而","因为","由于","尽管"],"answer":0,"explain":"从而 introduces the result produced by the action 整理成模板, with the same subject in both halves. 因为 and 由于 introduce a reason, and 尽管 needs a concession, so none of them fits this result slot."}]},"reading":{"title":"会议室里的四个字","text":"公司每年秋天有一次内部培训，内容是半天的模拟经营。五个人一组，每组要在半天里“经营”一家小公司。\n\n小陈是我们组理论最强的人。他读过很多管理书，一开口就是数据和方法，大家很快同意了他的方案。前半场我们一直领先，气氛很轻松。\n\n到了后半场，形势变了：客户的要求一变再变。小陈仍然按原来的计划推进，别人提醒他灵活一点，他却说方案没有问题。两个小时过去，我们从第一变成了最后。\n\n讨论时，带队的经理没有批评谁，只说了四个字：“纸上谈兵。”他说，理论很重要，但不能盲目相信纸上的方案。由于只顾方案而没有听客户的声音，我们组因而失去了机会。\n\n那次培训以后，小陈变了。他开始主动去客户那里听意见，从而发现自己方案里的毛病。","translation":"Every autumn the company runs an internal training session: half a day of business simulation. We work in groups of five, and each group has half a day to “run” a small company.\n\nChen was the strongest theorist in our group. He had read a lot of management books, and the moment he opened his mouth it was data and methods, so the rest of us quickly agreed to his plan. For the first half we led the field and the mood was relaxed.\n\nIn the second half the situation changed: the client's requirements kept shifting. Chen carried on with the original plan; when people suggested he stay flexible, he said the plan was fine. Two hours later we had gone from first place to last.\n\nIn the discussion the team leader did not criticise anyone. He said four words: “Armchair strategy.” Theory matters, he went on, but you cannot blindly trust a plan on paper. Because we looked only at the plan and did not listen to the client, our group lost its chance.\n\nAfter that session Chen changed. He began going to clients to hear their views, and in this way he found the flaws in his own plans.","questions":[{"q":"这次培训最想让参加的人明白____。","options":["理论必须和事实结合才有用","模拟经营比真实工作容易","团队应该由理论最好的人决定","客户的要求总是在变"],"answer":0,"explain":"The team leader's remark — theory matters but you cannot blindly trust a paper plan — states the lesson the exercise was meant to teach."},{"q":"我们组在后半场落后的直接原因是____。","options":["小陈不肯按变化调整方案","客户临时取消了合作","组里有人没有参加培训","经理提前结束了练习"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says Chen kept to the original plan and insisted it was fine while the client's requirements kept changing."},{"q":"从小陈后来的变化可以看出，他____。","options":["接受了那次失败的教训","对管理理论失去了兴趣","希望换一个团队工作","认为培训没有意义"],"answer":0,"explain":"He now goes to clients to listen and finds the flaws in his own plans, which shows he took the lesson to heart."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["他的方案写得很好，可惜只是纸上谈兵。","形势变了，我们必须马上调整计划。","经理再三提醒我们，不要盲目相信数据。","他主动承认了自己的毛病，大家都笑了。","他讲的道理没错，只是缺少实际的经验。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Think of a plan that looked perfect on paper but met reality. What did you change, and what did you learn? Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["方案","盲目","灵活","宝贵"],"min_chars":80,"model":"刚接手客户工作时，我总想写一份完美的方案，把每一步安排好。第一次提案，客户只问了一句：“如果预算减一半，你们怎么办？”我当场愣住了。那次失败很宝贵：我明白只按计划做事是不够的，方案必须留出调整的余地。后来我先听客户的实际困难，把几种可能都写进去。计划可以简单，但要灵活，不能盲目相信纸上的数字。","tips":"Set up the plan briefly, then show the moment reality intervened. End with the one principle you now apply, not a general moral."}},{"n":16,"zh":"体重与节食","en":"Weight and Diet","book":1,"theme":"A canteen makes small changes to the food environment, and a report asks whether dieting is really the answer.","grammar":{"id":"g16","point":"以便 / 以免 / 免得","point_en":"so that; in order to avoid; so as not to","structure":"做法 + 以便/以免/免得 + 目的或要避免的情况","explain_en":"These three words all connect an action to its purpose, but the purpose is positive with 以便 and negative with 以免 and 免得. 以便 means “so that, in order to make something possible” and is followed by what you want to happen: 提前十分钟到，以便做好准备. 以免 and 免得 both mean “so as not to”, and the clause after them names something you want to prevent: 早点出发，以免堵车. The difference between 以免 and 免得 is register: 以免 is formal and belongs in notices, rules and reports, while 免得 is conversational and often suggests saving yourself trouble — 你给他打个电话，免得他白跑一趟. All three come after the main action, and the second clause usually has the same subject as the first, so do not insert a new subject right after them. With 以便 the second clause often contains 能 or 可以; with 以免 and 免得 it usually contains 不 or names an unwanted situation.","common_mistake":"Learners mix up the polarity: they put the thing they want to avoid after 以便, or the goal they want after 以免. Decide first whether the second half is a purpose (以便) or something to prevent (以免/免得).","examples":[{"zh":"请提前十分钟到会议室，以便做好准备工作。","py":"qǐng tí qián shí fēn zhōng dào huì yì shì yǐ biàn zuò hǎo zhǔn bèi gōng zuò","en":"Please come to the meeting room ten minutes early so that we can prepare."},{"zh":"出门前检查一遍，以免忘记带文件。","py":"chū mén qián jiǎn chá yí biàn yǐ miǎn wàng jì dài wén jiàn","en":"Check once before you leave so as not to forget the documents."},{"zh":"你把地址发给我，免得我走错路。","py":"nǐ bǎ dì zhǐ fā gěi wǒ miǎn de wǒ zǒu cuò lù","en":"Send me the address so that I don't take the wrong road."}],"drills":[{"q":"会议材料请提前一天发给大家，____每个人都能先看一遍。","options":["以免","以便","何况","免得"],"answer":1,"explain":"以便 introduces a goal you want to make possible, and 每个人都能先看一遍 is exactly that goal. 以免 and 免得 introduce things to prevent, which reverses the meaning here, and 何况 means let alone."},{"q":"把常用的文件放在手边，____每次都要花时间找。","options":["以便","从而","以免","何况"],"answer":2,"explain":"以免 introduces the situation you want to prevent, 每次都要花时间找. 以便 needs a positive goal, 从而 links a means to an achieved result rather than a prevented one, and 何况 is used for rhetorical escalation."}]},"reading":{"title":"食堂里的小碗","text":"去年，公司食堂做了一次小小的调整：把大碗换成小碗，甜饮料放到最里面一排，蔬菜摆在最显眼的位置。行政部没有宣传，也没有要求谁节食。\n\n三个月后，工会做了一次调查。问卷不问体重，只问参与的人几个问题：最近吃得怎么样？下午会不会犯困？结果有些意外：说“吃得更舒服”的人明显多了，抱怨下午没精神的人却少了。\n\n负责这件事的小林说，他们分析了一些公开的研究：人一次摄入多少食物，和碗的大小有关系；把不健康的食物放远一点，人们就会少吃一点。这些措施并不神秘，只是很少有人真正去做。\n\n小林在报告里写道：与其下决心节食，不如调整环境。食堂还准备在桌上放一小瓶水，以免大家忙起来忘记喝水；把菜的营养信息贴在窗口，以便员工自己挑选。","translation":"Last year the company canteen made a small change: big bowls became smaller ones, sweet drinks moved to the furthest shelf, and vegetables were placed where the eye lands first. The admin office put up no posters and asked nobody to diet.\n\nThree months later the staff committee ran a survey. The questionnaire did not ask about weight, only a few questions for the people taking part: how have your meals been lately? Do you get sleepy in the afternoon? The result was a little unexpected: noticeably more people said they ate more comfortably, while fewer complained of having no energy in the afternoon.\n\nXiao Lin, who was in charge, says they analysed some published research: how much food a person takes in at one meal is related to bowl size, and if unhealthy food is placed further away, people eat a little less. These measures are no secret; it is just that few people actually apply them.\n\nAt the end of the report Xiao Lin wrote: rather than resolving to diet, adjust the environment. The canteen also plans to put a small bottle of water on every table so that nobody forgets to drink when things get busy, and to post the nutrition information at the counter so that staff can choose for themselves.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要介绍的是____。","options":["食堂用小的改变改善员工饮食","一种能快速减重的节食方法","员工对食堂价格的看法","营养研究人员的工作方式"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage describes the canteen's small changes and the survey that followed, and ends with the idea of adjusting the environment instead of dieting."},{"q":"根据文章，问卷里问到的是____。","options":["下午是否犯困","员工的体重","每年的体检结果","食堂的采购成本"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says the questionnaire did not ask about weight but did ask whether people got sleepy in the afternoon."},{"q":"从食堂的做法可以看出，他们相信____。","options":["改变环境比依靠意志更可靠","员工应该每天计算热量","节食是保持健康最好的办法","食堂的饭菜需要提高价格"],"answer":0,"explain":"The report's conclusion is to adjust the environment rather than resolve to diet, which trusts surroundings more than willpower."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["医生建议他少吃甜食，但不必完全节食。","研究人员分析了志愿者一年内的体重变化。","他的体重一直很稳定，没有明显的波动。","公司采取了几项措施，希望大家吃得更健康。","把水果放在桌上，以便大家随手拿到。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe one small change to your daily routine that made healthy eating easier. Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["营养","摄入","采取","可靠"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我以前常常忙到下午才想起吃饭，然后一次吃很多。后来我在办公桌的抽屉里放了几包坚果和一个水果盒，中午再忙也先吃一点。这样做的目的不是节食，而是让身体有稳定的营养来源，不至于晚上一次摄入太多。这个办法很普通，却比任何临时的计划都可靠。我还在手机上设了提醒，采取的措施不多，但一直坚持着。","tips":"Start with the old habit and its problem, then describe the change in one concrete detail. Finish with how reliable it proved in ordinary weeks."}},{"n":17,"zh":"在最美好的时刻离开","en":"Ending at the Best Moment","book":1,"theme":"A director closes a long-running play while tickets still sell, and a visitor works out what that decision means for work and leaving.","grammar":{"id":"g17","point":"关于 / 对于 / 至于","point_en":"about / regarding; towards; as for","structure":"关于 + 话题；对于 + 对象；至于 + 另起的话题","explain_en":"All three introduce a topic, but they frame it differently. 关于 means “about, concerning” and simply names the subject matter; it can start a sentence or sit before a noun, as in 关于这个问题 or 一本关于历史的书. 对于 means “towards, with regard to” and points at the object that a judgement, feeling or action is directed at, after which the sentence says how someone feels or acts towards it: 对于新的规定，大家还有疑问. 至于 means “as for” and moves to a second, related topic after the first has been dealt with; it opens the new clause, often implies a contrast or a shift, and cannot introduce the opening topic of a sentence. A quick test: naming what something is about calls for 关于, stating an attitude towards something calls for 对于, and switching to another item on the list calls for 至于. 关于 and 对于 overlap in some sentences, but only 关于 can attach extra information to a noun.","common_mistake":"A common slip is to open a sentence with 至于 when there is no earlier topic for it to contrast with, and to use 关于 where the sentence expresses an attitude: 对于新的流程很满意, not 关于新的流程很满意.","examples":[{"zh":"关于这次培训的安排，行政部会发一封邮件。","py":"guān yú zhè cì xùn liàn de ān pái xíng zhèng bù huì fā yì fēng yóu jiàn","en":"The admin office will send an email about the arrangements for this training."},{"zh":"对于新的报销规定，同事们还有一些疑问。","py":"duì yú xīn de bào xiāo guī dìng tóng shì men hái yǒu yì xiē yí wèn","en":"The colleagues still have some questions about the new expense rules."},{"zh":"至于演出时间，我们下周再确认。","py":"zhì yú yǎn chū shí jiān wǒ men xià zhōu zài què rèn","en":"As for the performance time, we will confirm it next week."}],"drills":[{"q":"会上讨论了一个____员工培训的问题。","options":["关于","对于","至于","因而"],"answer":0,"explain":"关于 can attach a topic to a noun, so 一个关于员工培训的问题 means a question about staff training. 对于 and 至于 cannot modify a noun this way, and 因而 is a result connective."},{"q":"他____这份工作一直很认真。","options":["关于","至于","对于","何况"],"answer":2,"explain":"对于 marks the object towards which the attitude 很认真 is directed. 关于 names a subject matter rather than an attitude target, 至于 needs an earlier topic to contrast with, and 何况 means let alone."}]},"reading":{"title":"散场之前","text":"小剧场的话剧《长街》演了六年，票依然很好卖。上个月，导演却宣布：这一季演完就结束，不再加场。\n\n很多人不理解。有人问他，为什么不趁着观众还多再演两年？他说，一部戏是有生命的。它的服装和道具都在变旧，化妆也过时了，演员的年纪也在变。如果一定要等到没人买票才停，最后留在观众记忆里的，可能是一场糟糕的演出。\n\n他宁可自己在高峰时告别。这样，观众记住的是它最好的样子，而不是一个烂掉的结尾。\n\n我看的是最后一场。散场时没有人急着走，大家安静地坐着，仿佛还想再听一句台词。那一刻我体会到：结束得漂亮，本身也是一种能力。至于什么时候该停下来，这部戏给了我一个提醒——不必等到掌声停了才下台。对于离开，我们平常想得太少，好像只有失败才需要退场。","translation":"The play “Long Street” has run in a small theatre for six years, and tickets still sell well. Last month, though, the director announced that it would close at the end of this season, with no extra performances.\n\nMany people did not understand. Someone asked him why he would not ride the audience wave for another two years. He said a play is a living thing: its costumes, make-up and props are slowly wearing out, and the actors are getting older too. If you insist on waiting until nobody buys a ticket, what stays in the audience's memory may be a bad production.\n\nHe would rather say goodbye at the peak. That way the audience remembers the play at its best, not with a rotten ending.\n\nI saw the last performance. When it ended, nobody hurried out; everyone sat quietly, as if hoping for one more line. In that moment it struck me that ending well is itself a skill. As for when to stop, the play gave me a reminder: you do not have to wait until the applause dies down before leaving the stage. We think too little about leaving; it is as if only failure calls for an exit.","questions":[{"q":"导演决定停演的主要原因是____。","options":["他希望把最好的样子留给观众","剧场要重新装修","演员们不愿意再演下去","观众已经不买票了"],"answer":0,"explain":"The director says a play is alive, its costumes and props are wearing out, and he would rather leave at the peak so the audience remembers the best version."},{"q":"关于最后一场演出，文章提到____。","options":["散场时观众坐着，没有人急着离开","演出结束后导演上台说了话","演员们一起唱了一首歌","剧场提前关了门"],"answer":0,"explain":"The fourth paragraph says nobody hurried away after the final performance and everyone sat quietly as if wanting one more line."},{"q":"从“结束得漂亮，本身也是一种能力”可以看出，作者____。","options":["认为适时结束需要判断力","不喜欢看戏剧的结尾","觉得失败的人才需要离开","希望这部戏能再演两年"],"answer":0,"explain":"Calling a good ending a kind of ability means the writer sees timing an exit as a skill, which the last paragraph applies to leaving in general."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这部戏剧在周末的开幕式上首次演出。","演员的服装和道具都是自己准备的。","他化妆用了半个小时，然后安静地坐着。","导演对这部作品的评价非常高。","婚礼结束以后，客人们陆续离开了。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a time you ended something while it was still going well — a job, a project or a hobby. Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["告别","高峰","平常","体会"],"min_chars":80,"model":"教了五年课后，我决定在上学期结束时停下来。那时班里的学生最多，家长的评价也最好，很多人劝我再教两年。可我知道自己的精力已经不如从前，再教下去，课会慢慢变差。最后一节课，我没有讲新内容，只和每个人说了几句话，然后像平常下课那样告别。这件事让我体会到：在高峰时说再见，比在低谷时离开更需要勇气。","tips":"Open with the decision and the moment you made it, add one detail that shows things were still going well, then close on what the ending taught you."}},{"n":18,"zh":"抽象艺术美不美","en":"Abstract Art: Beautiful or Not?","book":1,"theme":"Two visitors argue in front of a blue canvas, and an afternoon at the gallery changes how one of them looks at abstract art.","grammar":{"id":"g18","point":"由……组成","point_en":"to be made up of; to consist of","structure":"整体 + 由 + 部分 + 组成","explain_en":"由……组成 describes what a whole is made of: the whole comes first, 由 introduces the parts, and 组成 closes the phrase — 一个班由二十个学生组成. The parts are usually nouns listed with 、 or 和, and there should be at least two of them. The pattern is stative rather than an action: you are describing composition, so no 了 goes after 组成, and the sentence often reads as a plain statement of fact. Note that 由 also appears in other frames with a different meaning, such as 由他负责 “he is in charge”, so check that the parts sit between 由 and a closing verb. Compare 组成 with 包括: 包括 lists members and may cover only some of them (包括我), while 由……组成 presents the full recipe, so the parts should add up to the whole. Do not put 组成 before the parts, and do not use 由 to mean “because of” — that idea needs 由于.","common_mistake":"The usual error is word order: 组成部分由这幅画 is wrong because the whole must come before 由. Also avoid adding 了 to 组成, since composition is a state rather than a completed action.","examples":[{"zh":"这幅画由深浅不同的蓝色组成。","py":"zhè fú huà yóu shēn qiǎn bù tóng de lán sè zǔ chéng","en":"This painting is made up of blues of different depths."},{"zh":"我们的项目组由五名工程师和两名设计师组成。","py":"wǒ men de xiàng mù zǔ yóu wǔ míng gōng chéng shī hé liǎng míng shè jì shī zǔ chéng","en":"Our project team consists of five engineers and two designers."},{"zh":"这本教材由三部分组成，每一部分都有练习。","py":"zhè běn jiào cái yóu sān bù fen zǔ chéng měi yī bù fen dōu yǒu liàn xí","en":"The textbook consists of three parts, and each part has exercises."}],"drills":[{"q":"这个展览由三个部分____。","options":["组成","组合","成为","形成"],"answer":0,"explain":"由……组成 is the fixed frame for composition, so the parts sit between 由 and 组成. 组合 means to combine actively, 成为 means to become something, and 形成 means to take shape."},{"q":"我们的小组由六个人____。","options":["组织","组成","组建","组合"],"answer":1,"explain":"Only 组成 completes the 由 phrase and states what the group is made of. 组织 means to organise, 组建 means to set up, and 组合 means to combine, none of which follows a 由 phrase this way."}]},"reading":{"title":"一块蓝色的布","text":"周末，美术馆有一个现代绘画展。我本来只想随便看看，没想到待了三个小时。\n\n第一展厅挂着一幅很大的作品：一块深蓝色的布，中间洒了几点白，其余的地方什么也没有。我看了很久，也没看出它想说什么。两位观众在小声争论，一个说它极其简单，贵在自由；另一个说，这样的画谁都会画。\n\n后来我遇到一位常来看展的中年人。他说，抽象画不负责讲故事，它把颜色、线条这些元素放在一起，让你自己去感受。他还说，一幅画不是只由一块颜色组成的，画布上每一块颜色的位置，都经过反复调整。\n\n离开之前，我又回到那幅画前面。这一次，我不再问“画的是什么”，而是问自己：站在这里，我感觉怎么样？答案并不清晰，可那种安静确实存在。可见，欣赏不一定非要得出结论。","translation":"At the weekend there was an exhibition of modern painting at the art gallery. I had meant to look round quickly and ended up staying three hours.\n\nIn the first room hung a very large work: one piece of deep blue cloth with a few white drops in the middle and nothing at all elsewhere. I looked at it for a long time and still could not see what it was trying to say. Two visitors were arguing in low voices; one said it was extremely simple and its value lay in its freedom, the other said anyone could paint something like that.\n\nLater I met a middle-aged man who came to exhibitions often. He said abstract painting does not tell a story; it puts colours, lines and other elements together and lets you feel your own response. He added that a painting is not made of just one block of colour — the layout on the canvas, the position of every patch of colour, have all been adjusted again and again.\n\nBefore leaving I went back to the painting. This time I stopped asking what it showed and asked myself how I felt standing there. The answer was not clear, but the calm was really there. It seems that appreciating a painting does not have to end in a conclusion.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["作者一次看抽象画展的经历","美术馆的展览安排","怎样画好一幅抽象画","观众对美术馆的意见"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage follows the writer through one gallery visit, from the first confusing painting to a second look before leaving."},{"q":"两位观众争论的问题是____。","options":["这样简单的画算不算好作品","这幅画应该卖多少钱","画家是哪一年出生的","展厅的灯光是不是太亮"],"answer":0,"explain":"One calls the painting extremely simple and valuable for its freedom, the other says anyone could paint it — a disagreement about whether it is a good work."},{"q":"从最后一段可以看出，作者____。","options":["不再要求自己看懂每一幅画","决定以后不再来看展览","认为抽象画没有价值","想把那幅画买回家里"],"answer":0,"explain":"The writer stops asking what the painting shows and accepts an unclear but real feeling, which means giving up the demand to fully understand it."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这幅画由几个简单的色块组成。","美术馆目前正在展出几位年轻画家的作品。","他随手在纸上画了几笔，看起来很抽象。","我分辨不出这幅画和那幅画有什么区别。","艺术没有统一的规则，每个人都可以有自己的看法。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Think of a piece of art, music or design you did not understand at first. Write about how your view changed. Use 4 of the words below.","required_words":["欣赏","元素","调整","事实"],"min_chars":80,"model":"第一次看现代舞时，我几乎睡着了。台上没有故事，只有几个人在重复简单的动作。散场后我很失望，觉得这不叫艺术。后来朋友给了我一本书，我才知道编舞者把音乐、灯光和身体这些元素放在一起，是为了让人注意时间。我重新看了一次，调整了自己的期待，这次看到了细节。事实是，欣赏一件作品，有时需要先放下习惯。","tips":"Describe the first, puzzled reaction, then the piece of information that shifted it. Close with what you notice now that you did not notice before."}},{"n":19,"zh":"家乡的萝卜饼","en":"Turnip pancakes in my hometown","book":2,"theme":"A winter kitchen memory: the making of one home-town dish, and why its taste belongs to a person rather than to a recipe.","grammar":{"id":"g19","point":"以……为……","point_en":"to take X as / to be based on X","structure":"以 + A + 为 + B","explain_en":"以……为…… literally means 'take A as B'. It states what something has as its standard, main element, example or identity, and it is a written, slightly formal pattern that turns up constantly in menus, reports, job descriptions and short essays: 以清淡为主 (mainly mild), 以这本小说为例 (taking this novel as an example), 以质量为标准 (with quality as the standard), 以做菜为乐 (to take cooking as a pleasure). The A slot is a noun or an adjective phrase, never a full clause, and B is a noun, a short adjective, or one of the fixed nouns 主 / 例 / 荣 / 乐 / 标准 / 基础. The frame can be the predicate after a subject (我们家的早饭以粥为主), or it can modify a noun from in front (以汉语为母语的人). Compare 把……当作……: that pattern also means 'treat A as B', but it reports a person's attitude or a temporary use and belongs in speech, while 以……为…… states a rule, a category or a general characteristic and belongs in writing. The word order never changes: 以 comes first, then A, then 为, then B.","common_mistake":"Learners put a full clause or a verb after 为 (以他很努力为例子), or they replace 为 with 是 (以质量是标准). Keep B short and nominal, and do not use this written pattern where a casual 把……当作…… would sound more natural.","examples":[{"zh":"我们家的早饭以粥和小菜为主。","py":"wǒ men jiā de zǎo fàn yǐ zhōu hé xiǎo cài wéi zhǔ","en":"Our family's breakfast is mainly congee and a few side dishes."},{"zh":"以这道萝卜饼为例，它的原料只有三样。","py":"yǐ zhè dào luó bo bǐng wèi lì tā de yuán liào zhǐ yǒu sān yàng","en":"Take this turnip pancake as an example: it has only three ingredients."},{"zh":"奶奶以做饭为乐，从来不觉得麻烦。","py":"nǎi nai yǐ zuò fàn wéi lè cóng lái bù jué de má fan","en":"Grandma takes pleasure in cooking and never finds it a bother."}],"drills":[{"q":"我们家的晚饭一直____清淡为主，很少放辣椒。","options":["以","把","对","从"],"answer":0,"explain":"Only 以 can head the frame that ends in 为: 以……为…… is fixed. 把 needs an object and a verb result after it, 对 marks a target or an attitude, and 从 marks a starting point, so none of them can stand before 为."},{"q":"这家小店____特色，吸引了不少外地客人。","options":["以萝卜饼为","以萝卜饼是","把萝卜饼为","萝卜饼以"],"answer":0,"explain":"Only 以……为…… completes the frame. 是 cannot replace 为 after 以, 把 cannot be followed by 为 here, and reversing the order breaks the pattern completely."}]},"reading":{"title":"冬天的萝卜饼","text":"每年冬天，我都会想起家乡的萝卜饼。那时候，奶奶做的饼以薄、软为特色，邻居常来问做法。她的原料很简单：萝卜、面粉、少许盐。萝卜切成细丝，拌上一点醋，馅就做好了。面要擀得几乎透明，再折叠几次，放进锅里用文火慢慢煎。锅里不能放太多油，火一大就容易糊。屋里很快有了香味，奶奶把第一张放在盘子里，淋几滴酱油，让我先尝。我总趁热吃，一边吃一边说好吃，她就笑。奶奶说，萝卜清淡，冬天吃它，平安。那时我不太懂这句话，只觉得可口。如今我在城里也做过几次，颜色和味道总差一点。后来我才明白，我怀念的不只是饼，还有那个慢下来的下午。","translation":"Every winter I think of the turnip pancakes from my home town. Back then my grandmother's pancakes were known for being thin and soft, and the neighbours often came over to ask how she made them. Her ingredients were simple: turnip, flour, a little salt. The turnip was cut into fine shreds and mixed with a little vinegar, and the filling was done. The dough had to be rolled out until it was almost transparent, folded a few times, and then fried slowly in the pan over a low flame. There must not be too much oil, and a high flame burns it easily. Soon the whole room smelled good; Grandma put the first one on a plate, drizzled a few drops of soy sauce on it and let me taste it first. I always ate it while it was hot, saying how good it was between bites, and she would laugh. Grandma used to say that turnip is mild and that eating it in winter keeps you safe and well. I did not really understand that sentence then; I only knew it tasted good. Now I have made it a few times in the city, and the colour and the taste always come out a little different. Only later did I understand that what I miss is not just the pancake, but that slow afternoon as well.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写了____。","options":["奶奶做萝卜饼的方法和作者对家乡的怀念","作者在城里开小饭馆的经历","萝卜的营养价值和不同的吃法","邻居们向奶奶学习做菜的原因"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage moves from how the pancakes were made to what the author misses now; the last sentence says the memory is about more than food."},{"q":"奶奶做饼的时候，面要____。","options":["擀得几乎透明","切得很细","泡在水里","炸成金黄色"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 面要擀得几乎透明，再折叠几次. Thin shreds describe the turnip, and nothing in the passage is soaked or deep-fried."},{"q":"作者说城里的饼“总差一点”，最可能的原因是____。","options":["城里买不到新鲜的萝卜","少了家乡和亲人在身边的感觉","她一直没有学会用文火","城里的锅不适合做饼"],"answer":1,"explain":"The closing sentence turns from taste to the person and the slow afternoon, so the missing element is the setting and the grandmother, not the technique."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["我的家乡在北方，冬天经常下雪。","奶奶做的萝卜饼颜色好看，味道也很清淡。","我每次回家都特别想念妈妈做的家常菜。","这道菜以清淡为特色，老人和孩子都喜欢。","闻到厨房的香味，我就想起小时候的冬天。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a dish from your home town that you miss. Say who used to make it, what it tasted like, and what you notice now that you cook it yourself. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["家乡","怀念","清淡","可口"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我的家乡在北方，冬天很冷，最让我怀念的是街口那家小店的萝卜饼。它看起来普通，吃起来却很可口。老板把萝卜切成细丝，用文火慢慢煎，口味清淡，不油不腻。每次回去，我都要买两个，趁热吃完。现在那家店已经搬走了，但那个味道我一直记得。","tips":"Open with the dish and the person who made it, add two concrete details such as ingredients or cooking time, and finish with what has changed since then."}},{"n":20,"zh":"小人书摊","en":"Picture-story book stalls","book":2,"theme":"A street-corner picture-book stall from childhood, and the cheap shared pleasure of reading before screens took over.","grammar":{"id":"g20","point":"为……而……","point_en":"for the sake of / because of","structure":"为 + purpose or cause + 而 + verb phrase","explain_en":"为……而…… puts a purpose or a cause in front of an action, literally 'for the sake of X, do Y'. Two uses matter. The first is purpose: 为家人而努力 (work hard for one's family), 为这本书而坚持 (keep going for the sake of this book), 为梦想而搬到北京 (move to Beijing for a dream). The 为-phrase names the goal the action serves. The second is cause or emotion: 为这样的进步而高兴 (be glad about progress like this), 为孩子的安全而担心 (worry about the child's safety), 为那段经历而感谢他 (thank him for that experience). Here the 为-phrase names what triggers the feeling. The 而 is not optional — without it the sentence turns into a bare preposition and loses its pivot. The register is written and semi-formal: it belongs in speeches, essays and news copy rather than in a quick chat. Compare 为了……: it also comes before the verb and marks purpose, but it takes a purpose phrase and never needs 而 (为了省时间，他坐地铁). Compare 因为……所以……: that pair marks plain cause and effect in speech, while 为……而…… fuses the cause and the action into one compact written phrase. Position: the subject comes first, then 为 + noun phrase + 而 + verb phrase; 而 never comes before 为.","common_mistake":"The usual slip is putting a whole clause after 为 (为我他很高兴) or dropping 而 and breaking the frame. Remember 为 is read wèi here, and the 为-phrase follows the subject instead of opening the sentence.","examples":[{"zh":"他每天早起，为自己的目标而努力。","py":"tā měi tiān zǎo qǐ wèi zì jǐ de mù biāo ér nǔ lì","en":"He gets up early every day and works hard for his own goals."},{"zh":"老人为这些旧书而自豪，它们陪了他四十年。","py":"lǎo rén wèi zhè xiē jiù shū ér zì háo tā men péi le tā sì shí nián","en":"The old man is proud of these old books; they have been with him for forty years."},{"zh":"我们为这个小小的进步而高兴。","py":"wǒ men wèi zhè ge xiǎo xiǎo de jìn bù ér gāo xìng","en":"We are delighted about this small amount of progress."}],"drills":[{"q":"请不要____一点小事而生气，先把情况说清楚。","options":["为","以","把","由"],"answer":0,"explain":"为……而…… is the fixed frame for a cause that triggers a feeling or an action. 以 would need another 为 later, 把 needs an object plus a verb result, and 由 marks the doer in a passive."},{"q":"他为____而坚持每天写作，十年没有停过。","options":["自己的梦想","自己的梦想是","他有一个梦想","因为梦想"],"answer":0,"explain":"Only a noun phrase can stand between 为 and 而. 是 cannot appear inside the phrase, 他有一个梦想 is a complete clause, and 因为梦想 repeats the meaning of 为."}]},"reading":{"title":"街边的书摊","text":"我小时候，最热闹的地方是街边的书摊。摊主用砖头和木板搭了一个棚子，上面铺着旧布，很粗糙，却收拾得整整齐齐。架上摆着几百册连环画，题材大多是历史和英雄故事。看一本要付两分钱，还要交五分钱押金。对小学生来说，那是最便宜的娱乐。放学以后，我们挤在棚子下面，一页一页地翻，谁也不说话。那时没有网络，也没有动画片，电视只有几个台，节目单调，可我们一点也不觉得闷。摊主是位老人，年纪很大，身材瘦小，做这行已经三十多年。他常说，假如这些书能让孩子多认几个字，他就满足了。很多年过去了，书摊不见了，那些木头和砖头也找不到了。我仍然为那段简单的快乐而感谢那位老人。","translation":"When I was a child, the busiest spot in the neighbourhood was the book stall by the road. The owner had put up a shed with bricks and wooden boards, covered it with old cloth, and although it was coarse it was kept extremely neat. The shelves held several hundred picture-story books, mostly on history and heroes. Reading one cost two cents, plus a five-cent deposit. For a primary-school pupil that was the cheapest entertainment around. After school we crowded under the shed and turned the pages one by one, and nobody said a word. There was no internet then and no cartoons; the television had only a few channels and the programmes were monotonous, yet we never felt bored. The owner was an old man, very advanced in years and small in build, who had been in this trade for over thirty years. He often said that if these books could get children to recognise a few more characters, he would be satisfied. Many years have passed, the stall is gone, and those wooden boards and bricks cannot be found anywhere. I am still grateful to that old man for those simple pleasures.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写了____。","options":["作者小时候在书摊看连环画的经历","一本连环画从编辑到印刷的过程","动画片为什么比旧书更受欢迎","老人收藏旧书的几种方法"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage describes the stall, its prices, the children reading there and the owner; the final paragraph confirms it is a memory of that period."},{"q":"那时候看一本连环画，需要付____。","options":["两分钱和五分钱押金","五分钱","一角钱","什么也不用付"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 看一本要付两分钱，还要交五分钱押金, so both amounts are needed; five cents alone is only the deposit."},{"q":"老人说“假如这些书能让孩子多认几个字，他就满足了”，可以看出他____。","options":["更在意孩子从书里得到什么","想靠书摊赚很多钱","不喜欢孩子常来看书","打算把书全部卖掉"],"answer":0,"explain":"The condition he sets is about the children learning characters, not about profit; the deposit and low price point the same way."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["那时候没有网络，孩子们最大的娱乐就是看连环画。","他每天下班以后都去书摊翻一翻旧杂志。","现在的孩子更习惯看动画片，很少翻纸质书。","这本连环画很旧了，他却一直收藏着。","周末的娱乐不一定要花很多钱。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a cheap activity you loved as a child. Describe the place, what you did there, and how you feel about it now. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["娱乐","连环画","年代","收藏"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我小时候的娱乐很简单：街口有个旧书摊，摆着几百册连环画。看一本只要两分钱，我常常在那里站一个下午。那个年代没有网络，也没有动画片，可我们一点也不觉得闷。有一本讲船长的书我特别喜欢，后来攒了三个月的零钱才买下来，一直收藏到现在。","tips":"Start with the activity and what it cost, add two concrete details about the place, then close with the difference between then and now."}},{"n":21,"zh":"汉字叔叔：一个美国人的汉字情缘","en":"Uncle Hanzi: The predestined love of an American for Chinese characters","book":2,"theme":"A foreign engineer who turned a chance encounter with ancient script into a twenty-year research project he never got paid for.","grammar":{"id":"g21","point":"把……当作 / 作为……","point_en":"to treat X as / to regard X as","structure":"把 + X + 当作/作为 + Y","explain_en":"把……当作…… and 把……作为…… both mean 'treat or regard X as Y', and the choice between them is a matter of stance and register. 当作 (also written 当成) reports how someone actually treats something, often a personal attitude or a temporary arrangement: 他把沙发当作床, 我把周末当作读书的时间. It belongs in speech and narrative. 作为 is formal: it states a role, a category or a condition that is declared rather than improvised, as in 我们把环保作为今年的重点 or 他把这本书作为教材. 作为 also works as a plain preposition meaning 'as, in the capacity of' at the head of a sentence, with no 把 at all: 作为一名老师，他很耐心. That use is a different construction and must not be mixed with the 把 frame. Word order: subject + 把 + X + 当作/作为 + Y, and Y has to be a noun phrase — both verbs still need an object after them. In conversation 当作 is the safer choice; in a report or a plan 作为 sounds more deliberate.","common_mistake":"Learners drop 作 (把书当教材) or leave Y empty (把这件事当作). A second slip is copying the 作为-as-preposition sentence into the 把 frame: 把一名老师，他有责任 is impossible.","examples":[{"zh":"他把收集汉字当作一种习惯。","py":"tā bǎ shōu jí hàn zì dāng zuò yì zhǒng xí guàn","en":"He treats collecting Chinese characters as a habit."},{"zh":"我们把这本书作为这学期的教材。","py":"wǒ men bǎ zhè běn shū zuò wéi zhè xué qī de jiào cái","en":"We are using this book as the textbook for this term."},{"zh":"作为一名工程师，他很注意细节。","py":"zuò wéi yì míng gōng chéng shī tā hěn zhù yì xì jié","en":"As an engineer, he pays close attention to details."}],"drills":[{"q":"他把学汉语____生活的一部分，每天都练一会儿。","options":["当作","认为","以为","觉得"],"answer":0,"explain":"Only 当作 can follow 把 and take a noun phrase such as 生活的一部分. 认为, 以为 and 觉得 all introduce a clause, so 把 would be left without an object to move."},{"q":"____一名新员工，他每天提早半小时到办公室。","options":["作为","把","当作","为了"],"answer":0,"explain":"作为 opens a sentence meaning 'in the capacity of'. 把 needs a verb later in the clause, 当作 cannot stand alone without 把 and an object, and 为了 would introduce a purpose instead of a role."}]},"reading":{"title":"一个人的汉字库","text":"他第一次见到汉字，是在一个很小的图书馆里。那时他在大学学物理，偶然看到一本介绍古文字的书，从此对中国字产生了兴趣。最初，他只是把认字当作一种游戏，每天记录几个新字。后来他发现，每个字里都包含一段历史，笔画的变化有清楚的内在逻辑。他把这件事当作第二份工作：用二十年时间收集资料，把不同的写法输入电脑，建立一个可以按形状查询的资料库。元旦那天，网站第一次公开，访问量很小，但他很满足。有人称赞他，也有人说他过分认真。他承认自己常常思考同一个问题：这些字为什么这样写？为了尽快找到答案，他把每天的日程排得很紧。现在他已经退休，还在完善这个库。他说，自己最大的梦想，是让更多孩子喜欢上这些字。","translation":"He first saw Chinese characters in a very small library. At the time he was studying physics at university, and he happened to pick up a book about ancient scripts; from then on he was interested in Chinese writing. At first he treated learning characters as a game and noted down a few new ones each day. Later he found that every character contains a piece of history and that the changes in its strokes follow a clear inner logic. He made this his second job: twenty years spent collecting material, keying the different forms into a computer, and building a database that can be searched by shape. On New Year's Day the website went public for the first time; the traffic was tiny, but he was pleased. Some people praised him and some said he was far too serious about it. He admits that he keeps asking himself one question: why are these characters written this way? To find the answer as quickly as possible, he keeps his daily schedule packed. He is retired now and still improving the database. He says his biggest dream is to get more children to like these characters.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要介绍了____。","options":["一个人用很长时间收集和研究汉字的经历","一所大学图书馆的借书规定","中文网站的设计方法","外国人练习汉语口语的几种办法"],"answer":0,"explain":"Every paragraph follows the same person's work on characters, from the first book to the database he still improves after retiring."},{"q":"网站第一次公开是在____。","options":["元旦","春节","中秋节","他的生日"],"answer":0,"explain":"The sentence 元旦那天，网站第一次公开，访问量很小 gives the date directly."},{"q":"从文章中可以看出，作者对这位研究者的态度是____。","options":["佩服他的坚持","觉得他浪费了时间","认为他只是运气好","怀疑他的资料不可靠"],"answer":0,"explain":"The article keeps stressing twenty years of collecting, a full schedule and continued work after retirement; that selection of detail signals admiration."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["他偶然在一本旧书里看到汉字的图片。","建立一个资料库需要很多时间和耐心。","每个汉字的变化都有它自己的逻辑。","他退休以后还在完善自己的研究。","同事们都称赞他的坚持和认真。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a hobby that started by chance and became a long-term project. Say how it began, what you do now, and what it has taught you. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["偶然","收集","思考","梦想"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我开始写读书笔记完全出于偶然。五年前，我在旧书店里翻到一本介绍古文字的小册子，觉得有趣，就开始收集里面提到的书。慢慢地，我养成了习惯：每读完一本，就把自己的想法写下来，再花十分钟思考这本书和我有什么关系。这个习惯看起来很小，却让我离自己的梦想近了一点。","tips":"Open with the chance moment, describe the routine it turned into, and end with one sentence about what the habit has given you."}},{"n":22,"zh":"阅读与思考","en":"Reading and thinking","book":2,"theme":"How a change in reading habits turned a habit of quick judgement into a habit of asking better questions.","grammar":{"id":"g22","point":"拿……来说 / 就……而言","point_en":"taking X as an example / as far as X is concerned","structure":"拿 + X + 来说，…… / 就 + X + 而言，……","explain_en":"Both phrases push a topic to the front of the sentence and limit what the rest of it is about, but they do different jobs. 拿……来说 introduces a concrete, individual example that supports a claim you have just made or are about to make: 这里的书很便宜，拿这本来说，只要十块钱. It answers 'for instance'. 就……而言 narrows the scope or the angle of a judgement — 'as far as X is concerned, as regards X': 就质量而言，这台机器没有问题. It often sets up a contrast or a concession, because it quietly excludes every other angle. 而言 is bookish; in speech people more often say 就……来说 or 从……来看. The slots must be noun phrases, not clauses, and the two halves of each pairing cannot be mixed: 拿 goes with 来说, 就 goes with 而言, and 拿……而言 is a common written slip. Position: sentence-initial, or straight after a short subject. In an exam essay these frames are cheap, effective signposts for an opinion paragraph — one sets an example, the other limits a claim.","common_mistake":"The frequent error is mismatching the partners (拿……而言), or putting a whole clause after 拿 instead of a noun phrase. Also remember that 就……而言 names a scope, not a case, so it cannot be used to give an example.","examples":[{"zh":"拿这本童话来说，孩子读三遍也不会烦。","py":"ná zhè běn tóng huà lái shuō hái zi dú sān biàn yě bú huì fán","en":"Take this fairy tale: a child can read it three times without getting bored."},{"zh":"就阅读方法而言，他觉得朗读比背诵更有用。","py":"jiù yuè dú fāng fǎ ér yán tā jué de lǎng dú bǐ bèi sòng gèng yǒu yòng","en":"As far as reading methods go, he thinks reading aloud is more useful than memorising."},{"zh":"就目前的进度而言，我们还有两周时间。","py":"jiù mù qián de jìn dù ér yán wǒ men hái yǒu liǎng zhōu shí jiān","en":"As far as the current schedule goes, we still have two weeks."}],"drills":[{"q":"拿这次考试____，他的准备还不够充分。","options":["来说","而言","来看","说法"],"answer":0,"explain":"拿 pairs only with 来说. 而言 belongs with 就, 从……来看 is a third frame that needs 从 rather than 拿, and 说法 is a noun and cannot complete the phrase."},{"q":"____，这台机器的质量没有问题。","options":["就质量而言","拿质量而言","就质量而说","质量而言"],"answer":0,"explain":"就 pairs with 而言. 拿 cannot take 而言, 就……而说 is not a form at all, and a bare noun phrase cannot open the sentence without the preposition."}]},"reading":{"title":"慢读的理由","text":"很多人读书有个习惯：先看结论，再看别人的观点，最后才翻正文。我以前也这样，觉得这样省时间。自从开始写读书笔记，我的想法有了转变。就阅读而言，快并不等于好。一本好书之所以值得反复读，是因为它给不同年纪的人准备了不同的答案。拿我最喜欢的一篇童话来说，小时候我只看到那个孩子在冬天里很冷、很饿。长大以后再读，我注意到周围的人并不是坏人，他们只是太忙，太习惯别人的痛苦。作者没有过分强调悲伤，只是把一种常见的冷漠写得很清楚。读到这里，我不再急着判断谁对谁错，而是问自己：如果我在那条街上，我会怎么做？我承认，这个问题没有完美的答案。但阅读的价值就在这里：它让我们愿意停下来，全面地想一想。","translation":"Many people read with a fixed habit: first the conclusion, then other people's opinions, and only at the end the actual text. I used to do the same, thinking it saved time. Since I began keeping reading notes, my view has changed. As far as reading is concerned, fast is not the same as good. A good book deserves a second and third reading because it keeps different answers ready for people of different ages. Take my favourite fairy tale: as a child I saw only that the little girl was cold and hungry in the winter. Reading it again as an adult, I noticed that the people around her are not villains — they are simply too busy, too used to other people's pain. The author does not overdo the sadness; she just makes an ordinary kind of coldness very clear. At that point I stopped rushing to decide who was right and asked myself: if I had been on that street, what would I have done? I admit there is no perfect answer to that question. But perhaps that is where the value of reading lies: it makes us willing to stop and think about the whole picture.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写了____。","options":["作者对怎么读书的看法和它带来的改变","一篇童话的写作背景","作者学习写作文的经历","读书笔记的几种常见格式"],"answer":0,"explain":"The first paragraph describes the old habit and the change, and the rest explains what slow, questioning reading means to the author."},{"q":"作者小时候读那篇童话，注意到的是____。","options":["那个孩子在冬天里很冷、很饿","周围的人只是太忙","作者没有过分强调悲伤","故事里那条街的名字"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text contrasts 小时候我只看到那个孩子在冬天里很冷、很饿 with what the author noticed 长大以后再读."},{"q":"作者说“这个问题没有完美的答案”，作者的态度是____。","options":["承认问题复杂，但值得一直想下去","认为这篇童话写得不好","决定以后不再读童话","觉得孩子不该读这样的故事"],"answer":0,"explain":"The next sentence says the value of reading lies in stopping to think about the whole picture, which accepts the open question instead of rejecting the book."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["读书的时候，千万不要过分相信别人的观点。","我承认这本书的结论并不完美。","从客观的角度看，这个观点还需要更多理由。","自从开始写作文，他比以前认真多了。","读一本好书，常常能让人想得更全面。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a book or story that changed how you see something. Say what you noticed first, what you noticed later, and what question it left you with. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["观点","转变","客观","价值"],"min_chars":80,"model":"大学时我读一篇童话，只觉得故事里的穷人很可怜。工作以后重读，我的观点有了转变。我开始注意那些路过的人：他们并不坏，只是太忙。这个发现让我对自己也客观了一些。一本书的价值也许不在答案，而在它让你多问一句为什么。我在读书笔记里写下这个问题，后来又读了第二遍。","tips":"Begin with your first reading, contrast it with a later one, and finish with the question the book left you instead of summarising the plot."}},{"n":23,"zh":"放手","en":"Letting go","book":2,"theme":"A parent's account of one broken rule, a long family conversation, and the evening she began to let go.","grammar":{"id":"g23","point":"在……方面 / 从……角度看","point_en":"in the area of X / from the perspective of X","structure":"在 + X + 方面，…… / 从 + X + 角度看，……","explain_en":"在……方面 limits a claim to one area of a person or a subject — 'in terms of, as regards'. It answers the question 'where does this statement apply?' and it can also sit inside a phrase to modify a noun: 他在语言方面的能力, 公司在培训方面的投入. 从……角度看 (also 从……来看, 从……看) switches the sentence to a viewpoint, usually because the speaker is about to contrast it with another angle — 'from the point of view of'. It answers 'from whose side are we looking?' The two are not interchangeable: only 在 can attach to a noun with 的 and modify it (在管理方面的经验), while 从 needs 角度 or 看 / 来看 after the noun and never takes 的. Both frames come before the clause they frame, normally at the start of the sentence or straight after the subject. In an exam essay, 在……方面 is handy for scoping a paragraph and 从……角度看 for adding a second opinion before you take sides.","common_mistake":"Learners mix the prepositions and the nouns, producing 在……角度看, which does not exist. The other slip is leaving the frame unfinished (从父母), because 角度 or 看 is what makes 从 a viewpoint marker.","examples":[{"zh":"在教育方面，他和妻子的想法不太一样。","py":"zài jiào yù fāng miàn tā hé qī zi de xiǎng fǎ bú tài yí yàng","en":"Where education is concerned, he and his wife think somewhat differently."},{"zh":"从孩子的角度看，父母安排得太紧了。","py":"cóng hái zi de jiǎo dù kàn fù mǔ ān pái de tài jǐn le","en":"From the child's point of view, the parents' schedule is too tight."},{"zh":"她在沟通方面很有经验。","py":"tā zài gōu tōng fāng miàn hěn yǒu jīng yàn","en":"She has a lot of experience in communication."}],"drills":[{"q":"____，这个规定确实太严了。","options":["从孩子的角度看","在孩子的角度看","以孩子的角度看","在孩子的角度"],"answer":0,"explain":"从……角度看 is the fixed viewpoint frame. 在 pairs with 方面, not with 角度看; 以 belongs to 以……为……; and 在……的角度 on its own never forms a viewpoint phrase."},{"q":"他在写作____很有经验，改稿子的工作可以交给他。","options":["方面","角度","方向","部分"],"answer":0,"explain":"在……方面 is the frame for naming an area of skill or activity. 角度 belongs with 从……看, and 方向 and 部分 do not name an area inside this frame."}]},"reading":{"title":"那一次我没有替她做决定","text":"女儿上高中以后，我们有过一次很长的谈话。起因是她违反了一条家里的规矩：晚上十点才回家，事先没有说一声。我当时很生气，觉得她不够乖。后来才知道，那天班里排练到很晚，她是征求了老师的意见才留下的。晚饭后，我们三个人坐下来谈。在教育方面，我和她爸爸的想法并不完全一致。我认为规矩要严，他觉得孩子需要一个自己判断的阶段。从女儿的角度看，她已经不是小学生了，很多事可以单独处理；可在我这里，她还是那个需要人操心的孩子。最后我们都做了让步：晚归要提前发消息，但具体时间由她自己安排。那天她回房间以后，我在客厅坐了很久。我隐约感觉到，真正的难题不是定规矩，而是学会放手。","translation":"After my daughter started senior high school, we had one very long conversation. It began because she had broken a rule of the house: she came home at ten in the evening without saying anything in advance. I was angry at the time and thought she had not been a well-behaved girl. Only later did I learn that her class had been rehearsing late and that she had stayed after asking her teacher for advice. After dinner the three of us sat down to talk. When it comes to education, my husband and I do not fully agree. I think rules should be strict; he thinks a child needs a stage in which she judges things for herself. From my daughter's point of view she is no longer a primary-school pupil and can handle many things on her own, but in my mind she is still the child who needs someone to worry about her. In the end we both made concessions: she has to send a message before staying out late, but she arranges the exact time herself. That night, after she went back to her room, I sat in the living room for a long while. I had a faint sense that the real difficulty was not making rules but learning to let go.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写了____。","options":["一位母亲在孩子长大时学着放手的经过","女儿考试成绩下降的原因","一次学校家长会的内容","家里重新装修房子的经历"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage runs from the broken rule, through the family talk and the compromise, to the closing line about learning to let go."},{"q":"女儿那天晚归，是因为____。","options":["班里排练到很晚","路上堵车","她和同学去逛书店","老师留她补课"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 那天班里排练到很晚，她是征求了老师的意见才留下的. Nothing about traffic, bookshops or extra lessons appears."},{"q":"文章最后说“真正的难题……是学会放手”，可以看出作者____。","options":["有些不舍，但明白必须这样做","非常生气，准备加重惩罚","很轻松，因为问题彻底解决了","后悔当初定下这条规矩"],"answer":0,"explain":"She sits alone for a long time and calls letting go the real difficulty; the tone is reluctant understanding rather than anger or relief."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这件事你应该先征求一下父母的意见。","家里的规矩不能随便改，要一起商量。","他一个人单独完成了整个报告。","遇到问题要多沟通，别一个人想办法。","这个阶段最重要的是保持耐心。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a time you had to stop managing something and let someone else handle it. Explain what you were worried about and what actually happened. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["沟通","单独","让步","面临"],"min_chars":80,"model":"去年我把一个项目交给新同事。最初我什么都要操心，每天看三次进度。后来我意识到，这样只会让她不敢单独做决定。我们认真沟通了一次，我把要求说清楚，就不再每天追问。她做得比我预想的好，只在关键的地方来问我。我也学会了一点：面临选择时，让步不是不负责，而是把事情交给更合适的人。","tips":"Set the scene in one sentence, show the worry with a concrete detail, then close with what the other person did and what you learned."}},{"n":24,"zh":"支教行动","en":"Volunteer teaching","book":2,"theme":"Two weeks of volunteer teaching in a village school, and what the teacher took away instead of what she gave.","grammar":{"id":"g24","point":"随着……","point_en":"along with / as (something changes)","structure":"随着 + changing condition，+ clause describing the change it brings","explain_en":"随着 links two changes that happen together: the first clause names a gradual change in conditions, and the main clause says what changes along with it. The phrase after 随着 almost always contains a development verb — 随着经济的发展, 随着年纪的增长, 随着网络的普及, 随着时间的变化 — and never a static description. The main clause usually carries 越来越, 不断, 逐渐, 开始 or 也, because it is reporting movement rather than a state. Position: sentence-initial, or after a short subject (情况随着时间变了). The register is neutral; it is common in reports, essays and news copy. Compared with 因为……所以……, 随着 does not name a cause and an effect but two processes running side by side, so the main clause needs no 所以. Compared with 跟……一起 or 跟着, which need a person or a moving object, 随着 takes an abstract change. Two reliable shapes: 随着……，……越来越…… and 随着……，……开始…….","common_mistake":"The usual mistake is putting a fixed fact after 随着 (随着他很忙) or using it with a person moving through space (随着老师走进教室). The first half needs a change, and 随着 cannot be shortened to 随 in careful writing.","examples":[{"zh":"随着年龄的增长，他越来越理解父母。","py":"suí zhe nián líng de zēng zhǎng tā yuè lái yuè lǐ jiě fù mǔ","en":"As he gets older, he understands his parents better and better."},{"zh":"随着网络的普及，人们查资料方便多了。","py":"suí zhe wǎng luò de pǔ jí rén men chá zī liào fāng biàn duō le","en":"With the spread of the internet, looking things up has become much easier."},{"zh":"随着天气转冷，街上的行人少了。","py":"suí zhe tiān qì zhuǎn lěng jiē shàng de xíng rén shǎo le","en":"As the weather turns cold, there are fewer people on the street."}],"drills":[{"q":"____，村里的孩子有了更多的选择。","options":["随着网络的发展","随着网络发展着","跟随网络的发展","随着网络很发展"],"answer":0,"explain":"随着 takes a noun phrase with 的 or a plain change verb. 发展着 adds a progressive particle that 随着 never takes, 跟随 means 'follow' and is used with people, and 很 cannot modify 发展 inside this phrase."},{"q":"随着天气变冷，____。","options":["来上课的人明显少了","来上课的人一直很多","来上课的人特别多","来上课的人非常多"],"answer":0,"explain":"The main clause has to register a change that runs alongside the first one. 一直很多, 特别多 and 非常多 are static descriptions, so 随着 would be left without any matching change."}]},"reading":{"title":"半个月的支教","text":"去年秋天，我请了半个月的假，参加了一个支教项目。出发前，我以为最大的困难是生活条件。到了以后才发现，真正艰巨的是课堂：三个年级在同一间教室里，基础差别很大。第一天讲地理，我讲到一半，就有孩子趴在桌上睡着了。后来我改变方法，把课文分成几段，让他们用朗读的方式互相检查。慢慢地，及格的人多了，愿意举手的人也多了。课余时间，我做家访，走了十几户。有的孩子父母在外打工，大部分家务要由他们承担。随着接触的增多，我开始明白，我们能带来的不只是几节课。离开之前，我们在操场上排练了一个小节目。那天下午，孩子们跳了一支舞蹈，动作也许不整齐，可掌声很热烈。回城以后，我把收获写在本子上：勇气、耐心，还有一双愿意慢慢看的眼睛。","translation":"Last autumn I took two weeks off and joined a volunteer teaching programme. Before I left I assumed the hardest part would be the living conditions. Only after arriving did I find that what was really formidable was the classroom: three year groups in one room, with a huge gap between the children's foundations. On the first day, teaching geography, I was halfway through when a child fell asleep with his head on the desk. Later I changed my method, split the text into sections and had them check each other by reading aloud. Gradually more of them passed the exercises, and more hands went up. In my free time I visited families, a dozen or so households. Some children have parents working away and have to take on most of the housework themselves. As I came into more contact with them, I began to see that what we could bring was not only a few lessons. Before leaving we rehearsed a short performance on the playground. That afternoon the children danced, and although the movements may not have been neat, the applause was warm. Back in the city I wrote the gains of those two weeks in a notebook: courage, patience, and a pair of eyes willing to look slowly.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写了____。","options":["作者参加支教活动的经历和感受","村里学校校舍的修建过程","一次期末考试的结果","作者旅行时看到的风景"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage follows the whole two weeks — arrival, classroom problems, home visits, the performance — and ends with what the author gained."},{"q":"作者第一天讲地理课，____。","options":["有孩子趴在桌上睡着了","教室突然停电了","学生们没有课本","孩子问了很多问题"],"answer":0,"explain":"The text says 第一天讲地理，我讲到一半，就有孩子趴在桌上睡着了. Power cuts, missing textbooks and questions are not mentioned."},{"q":"作者把“一双愿意慢慢看的眼睛”写进收获里，是想说明____。","options":["支教让她学会了耐心观察","她打算以后去学医","村里的孩子视力不好","她准备换一份新工作"],"answer":0,"explain":"The phrase closes a list of gains (courage, patience) and echoes 随着接触的增多，我开始明白; it is about her own way of seeing, not about eyesight."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这次支教让我认识了很多可爱的孩子。","放学以后，老师去几户人家做家访。","他每天跟着录音练习朗读，进步很快。","孩子们排练了一个节目，家长都来鼓掌。","这次经历让我收获了勇气和耐心。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a short project or trip where you expected to help others but learned something yourself. Say what you planned and what actually happened. Use four of the words below.","required_words":["支教","收获","勇气","承担"],"min_chars":80,"model":"去年我参加了一次支教活动，只有两周。出发前，我准备了很详细的课件，以为自己能教很多。到了才发现，孩子们最需要的不是新知识，而是有人听他们说话。我陪他们朗读，一起排练节目，也去家里做过家访。那两周我承担的事情不多，收获却很大。回城以后，我多了面对陌生环境的勇气。","tips":"State the plan in one or two sentences, then describe what went differently, and close with the personal gain rather than a summary of the trip."}},{"n":25,"zh":"给自己加满水","en":"Adding up the load on yourself","book":2,"theme":"A ship's ballast becomes a working metaphor: the duties, rules and dependable people that keep a career steady are weight you add on purpose.","grammar":{"id":"g25","point":"鉴于 / 基于 / 出于","point_en":"in view of / on the basis of / out of (a motive)","structure":"鉴于 + 情况，…… ｜ 基于 + 依据，…… ｜ 出于 + 动机，……","explain_en":"These three prepositions all introduce a reason, but each one takes a different kind of reason, and that is exactly where learners slip. 鉴于 ('in view of, given') introduces a situation you have observed, usually a problem, a change or a risk, and the clause after it says what should be done about that situation. It is formal and common in reports, notices and minutes: 鉴于最近的情况，我们决定…… It nearly always opens the sentence, before the subject, with a comma after the phrase. 基于 ('on the basis of, based on') introduces the material or evidence that a judgement, plan or claim rests on: data, research, experience, a contract, a survey. The phrase can come before the subject, or after a noun as 基于……的 + noun, for example 基于数据的判断. 出于 ('out of, from') introduces the motive or feeling behind a person's action: 出于好奇, 出于礼貌, 出于责任, 出于同情. Its subject is a person or an organisation with intentions, and the phrase explains why they acted, not what the evidence was. A quick test: is the reason an observed situation (鉴于), a body of evidence (基于), or a motive inside someone's head (出于)? Keep the reason inside the phrase, then a comma, then a full clause with its own subject. Do not drop the comma and do not stack 因为 in the same slot.","common_mistake":"Learners mix the members up: 鉴于我很累 and 出于调查结果 both sound wrong to a native ear. Match the phrase to the kind of reason — observed situation, evidence, or personal motive.","examples":[{"zh":"鉴于天气恶劣，公司决定推迟今天的户外活动。","py":"jiàn yú tiān qì è liè gōng sī jué dìng tuī chí jīn tiān de hù wài huó dòng","en":"In view of the bad weather, the company decided to postpone today's outdoor event."},{"zh":"基于去年的数据，我们认为这个方案的风险可以承受。","py":"jī yú qù nián de shù jù wǒ men rèn wéi zhè ge fāng àn de fēng xiǎn kě yǐ chéng shòu","en":"On the basis of last year's figures, we think the risk of this plan is bearable."},{"zh":"他出于谨慎，把每一份合同都读了两遍。","py":"tā chū yú jǐn shèn bǎ měi yī fèn hé tóng dōu dú le liǎng biàn","en":"Out of caution, he read every contract twice."}],"drills":[{"q":"他____同情，把那位老人的车费免了。","options":["出于","鉴于","基于","至于"],"answer":0,"explain":"同情 is a feeling inside a person, so 出于 (out of a motive) is the only fit. 鉴于 needs an observed situation before a decision, 基于 needs evidence such as data, and 至于 means 'as for' and changes the topic."},{"q":"这份市场报告是____三年的销售数据写成的，所以结论比较可靠。","options":["出于","鉴于","基于","关于"],"answer":2,"explain":"基于 introduces the evidence that a piece of work rests on, here three years of sales data. 出于 would make the data a motive, 鉴于 introduces an observed situation for a decision rather than the basis of writing, and 关于 only marks a topic."}]},"reading":{"title":"船上的重量","text":"去年冬天，我跟一位老船长出海。船刚离开港口，风浪就大了起来，船身左右摇晃。我在舱里坐不住，心里有点慌张，只好抓住桌子。老船长却很镇定，他让人往船底的水箱里灌水，动作很谨慎。我不明白：船已经这么重了，为什么还要加水？他说，海上最大的风险不是浪，而是空船；加了重量，船才稳。那天风浪一直没停，我们却平平安安地返航了。\n\n鉴于那次经历，我慢慢懂得了一个道理：人不总是越轻越好。工作也一样，适当的责任、清楚的规则、几个靠得住的伙伴，都是我们的重量。它们让我们在恶劣的环境里保持平衡，不至于一有风吹草动就摔倒。彻底明白这一点，我用了好几年。","translation":"Last winter I went out to sea with an old captain. We had barely left the harbour when the wind and waves picked up and the hull began to roll from side to side. I could not sit still in the cabin, felt a little flustered and had to hold on to the table. The captain stayed calm. He had the crew pump water into the tanks at the bottom of the boat, working carefully. I did not understand: the boat was already so heavy, why add water? He said that at sea the biggest risk is not the waves but an empty hull; with the weight in, the boat steadies. The wind never dropped that day, yet we made it home safely. In view of that experience, I gradually learned something: a person is not always safer the lighter they are. Work is the same. Reasonable responsibility, clear rules and a few dependable colleagues are our weight. They hold us in balance in bad conditions, so that we do not fall over at the first gust of wind. It took me several years to understand this fully.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要想说明____。","options":["船越轻就越安全","人在工作中也需要一点重量","老船长其实不熟悉海上的情况","出海之前应该多准备一些水"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph turns the boat into a metaphor and states the point directly: work is the same, responsibilities and rules are our weight."},{"q":"老船长让人往水箱里灌水，是因为____。","options":["船舱里的水不够用","空船在风浪里更危险","他想让船开得更快","水箱需要经常清洗"],"answer":1,"explain":"The captain says '海上最大的风险不是浪，而是空船', and the fact that the boat stayed steady confirms the reason."},{"q":"从“彻底明白这一点，我用了好几年”可以看出作者____。","options":["一直不认同老船长的做法","后来再也不愿意出海","花了很长时间才理解这个道理","很快就当上了船长"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing sentence says the author needed several years to understand the idea fully, so the lesson came slowly rather than at once."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["那天的风浪很大，船上的人都有点慌张。","老船长很谨慎，他先检查了每个水箱。","空船在海上风险更大，必须增加重量。","我们终于平安返航，大家都松了一口气。","遇到恶劣的天气，保持平衡最重要。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a time when an extra responsibility or a strict rule turned out to help you stay steady at work. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["平衡","谨慎","重量","承受"],"min_chars":90,"model":"去年我接手了一个新项目，事情多得像石头，压得我喘不过气。起初我只想快点做完，结果越想快越乱。后来我给自己加了几条规则：每天只排三件最重要的事，每周五留半小时整理。这些规则看起来是重量，其实是一种平衡。我变得谨慎，不再一有问题就慌，也慢慢能承受更多的任务。","tips":"Open with the pressure you felt, name one concrete rule or extra duty you took on, then close with the specific change you noticed afterwards."}},{"n":26,"zh":"你属于哪一种“忙”","en":"Which kind of “busy” person are you","book":2,"theme":"Two kinds of busy — one driven by other people's messages, one driven by your own plan — and the weekly review that tells them apart.","grammar":{"id":"g26","point":"难免 / 不免 / 未免","point_en":"inevitably / cannot help but / rather too much","structure":"难免 + (会) + 动词/形容词 ｜ 不免 + 动词短语（情绪） ｜ 未免 + (太/过于) + 形容词/动词短语","explain_en":"All three concede that something undesirable is hard to dodge, but their force and their grammar differ. 难免 ('hard to avoid, inevitably') is the neutral, common one in writing. It follows a statement of a fact or a tendency and predicts the natural consequence: 忙起来难免会出错. It works for anybody, including yourself, and takes a verb phrase or an adjective, very often with 会 inserted. 不免 ('cannot help but') adds a personal, slightly emotional tone. It describes a feeling or reaction the speaker cannot suppress — 看到他这么努力，我不免有点感动 — and it normally has a person as subject, most often 我, 我们 or 人. 未免 ('rather too, a bit much') is different in kind: it evaluates and mildly criticises, meaning 'more than is reasonable'. It usually precedes 太, 过于 or 有点 plus an adjective, or a verb phrase describing excess: 这个要求未免太高了. So: 难免 predicts a natural result, 不免 reports an involuntary feeling, 未免 judges something excessive. Position is the same for all three — after the subject, before the predicate — but 未免 carries a complaint, so it cannot be used for a neutral prediction without sounding as if you are blaming someone.","common_mistake":"Learners use 未免 for plain unavoidable results, e.g. 时间紧，未免会加班, which sounds like a complaint that the overtime is excessive. For a neutral prediction, use 难免.","examples":[{"zh":"第一次上台讲话，难免会有点紧张。","py":"dì yī cì shàng tái jiǎng huà nán miǎn huì yǒu diǎn jǐn zhāng","en":"Speaking in public for the first time, you are bound to feel a little nervous."},{"zh":"看到那张旧照片，他不免想起小时候的事。","py":"kàn dào nà zhāng jiù zhào piàn tā bù miǎn xiǎng qǐ xiǎo shí hou de shì","en":"Seeing that old photo, he could not help thinking of his childhood."},{"zh":"这份报告的要求未免太高了，一天根本做不完。","py":"zhè fèn bào gào de yāo qiú wèi miǎn tài gāo le yī tiān gēn běn zuò bù wán","en":"The requirements for this report are rather too demanding; nobody could finish it in a day."}],"drills":[{"q":"一份炒饭卖八十块，____太贵了。","options":["未免","难免","不免","何尝"],"answer":0,"explain":"未免 marks the judgement that something is excessive and pairs naturally with 太. 难免 and 不免 report unavoidable results or involuntary feelings, not a value judgement, and 何尝 is a rhetorical 'when did I ever'."},{"q":"新员工不熟悉流程，____会出一点小错，这很正常。","options":["难免","未免","不免","难道"],"answer":0,"explain":"A general fact plus 会 plus the comment 这很正常 points to 难免. 未免 would judge the errors as excessive and contradicts 这很正常, 不免 describes the speaker's own involuntary feeling, and 难道 needs a rhetorical question with 吗."}]},"reading":{"title":"两种忙","text":"公司里最忙的人，往往也是效率最低的人。我观察过一位同事：他每天第一个到，最后一个走，桌上堆着两台电脑，一连几个月没有周末。可是到了年底，他负责的项目还是耽误了。\n\n问题不在勤奋，而在被动。他的时间表由别人的消息决定，谁找他，他就先做谁的事。忙了一整天，真正重要的步骤一步也没走。这种忙碌久了难免让人疲劳，也难免让人怀疑自己到底在做什么。\n\n与其等着被安排，不如每周留出一个小时安静地反省：这一周，哪些事是别人要我做的，哪些事是我自己觉得该做的？想清楚了，忙才有方向。","translation":"The busiest person in an office is often the least efficient one. I once watched a colleague: he was the first to arrive and the last to leave, had two laptops piled on his desk, and went months without a weekend. Yet by the end of the year the project he was in charge of was still behind schedule. The problem was not diligence but passivity. His timetable was set by other people's messages; whoever contacted him got served first. After a whole busy day, not one of the genuinely important steps had been taken. Sustained that way, being busy is bound to leave you tired, and bound to make you wonder what you are actually doing. Rather than waiting to be assigned work, it is better to set aside an hour each week to reflect quietly: which of these tasks did other people ask for, and which did I decide were worth doing? Once that is clear, being busy has a direction.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要谈的是____。","options":["怎样减少每天加班的时间","两种忙之间的区别","怎样和同事处好关系","项目为什么会延误"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage contrasts busy work driven by other people with busy work driven by your own priorities, and the title names the contrast directly."},{"q":"那位同事的项目到年底还是耽误了，主要是因为____。","options":["他不够勤奋努力","他的时间由别人的消息决定","公司的电脑太旧","他不愿意在周末加班"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph states it plainly: the problem lies in passivity, and his schedule is decided by other people's messages."},{"q":"作者建议每周反省，是为了____。","options":["让老板看到自己的努力","推掉别人安排的事情","分清哪些事真正重要","把时间表交给同事安排"],"answer":2,"explain":"The review asks which tasks were other people's requests and which were your own judgement, so its purpose is to find what actually matters."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["最近公司很忙碌，大家都在赶进度。","他被安排了很多杂事，工作变得很被动。","忙了一整天，重要的步骤一步也没走。","周末安静下来，我花了一个小时反省。","这样做效率不高，还容易让人疲劳。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a week when you were busy but not effective, and the one change you made to your schedule. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["忙碌","效率","被动","反省"],"min_chars":90,"model":"上个月我特别忙碌，每天回完所有消息天就黑了，真正想做的事一件也没完成。后来我发现，自己太被动了：谁找我，我就先处理谁的事。于是我改了一个习惯，早上先关掉提醒，用一小时做当天最重要的一件事，晚上再统一回复。一周下来，效率高了不少。每周五花十分钟反省，比多加班两个小时更有用。","tips":"Start with the honest state of that week, name one specific change in your daily schedule, and finish with the measurable difference it made."}},{"n":27,"zh":"下棋","en":"Playing chess","book":2,"theme":"A coach's one quiet question turns a lost chess game into a professional habit: stop, look again, and name the real reason you lost.","grammar":{"id":"g27","point":"反而 / 却 / 竟然 / 居然","point_en":"on the contrary / yet / unexpectedly / to one's surprise","structure":"反而 + 动词短语（与预期相反） ｜ 却 + 动词短语（转折） ｜ 竟然/居然 + 动词短语（出乎意料）","explain_en":"Four words, two jobs. 反而 and 却 both mark a turn. 反而 means 'on the contrary': the result is the opposite of what the situation predicts, and the expectation is usually already on the table — 吃了药，病反而更重了. It often follows 不但不 or 不仅没, and it pairs with 更: 越忙反而越乱. 却 is the plainest written 'yet, however'. It sets two clauses against each other without claiming the result is surprising: 他说了对不起，我却没有生气. 却 cannot open a sentence; it comes after the subject and before the verb. 竟然 and 居然 both mark real surprise — the speaker did not expect this at all. 竟然 is neutral and slightly formal; 居然 is more colloquial and often carries disbelief or disapproval, and it works well in rhetorical questions: 你居然不知道？ Both stand after the subject and before the verb. A practical test: if the result contradicts what you expected, use 反而; if you are simply setting two facts side by side in writing, use 却; if you are registering surprise at a fact, use 竟然 or 居然. Do not stack them in one slot, and remember that 反而 often needs a partner such as 不但不, 不仅没 or 越……越…… to sound complete.","common_mistake":"Learners put 却 or 竟然 at the head of a clause — 但是我却觉得, 却他没来. All four words sit after the subject and before the predicate.","examples":[{"zh":"他吃了两天药，病反而更重了。","py":"tā chī le liǎng tiān yào bìng fǎn ér gèng zhòng le","en":"He took the medicine for two days and the illness got worse instead."},{"zh":"我提醒过他三次，他却一句也没听进去。","py":"wǒ tí xǐng guò tā sān cì tā què yī jù yě méi tīng jìn qù","en":"I reminded him three times, yet he did not take in a single word."},{"zh":"这么简单的题，他居然算错了。","py":"zhè me jiǎn dān de tí tā jū rán suàn cuò le","en":"Such a simple question, and he actually got it wrong."}],"drills":[{"q":"我解释了半天，他不但没有消气，____。","options":["反而更生气了","却更生气了","竟然更生气","居然更生气"],"answer":0,"explain":"反而 is the fixed second half of 不但没有…… in this frame. 却 does not pair with 不但, and 竟然/居然 mark surprise at a new fact rather than the opposite of the expected result; both would also need 了 before the final particle."},{"q":"这张表我昨天才发给他，他____已经填完交上来了。","options":["居然","反而","难免","鉴于"],"answer":0,"explain":"居然 marks surprise at a fact that was not expected, here the speed. 反而 needs an opposite result, 难免 predicts a natural consequence and takes 会, and 鉴于 introduces an observed situation at the start of a sentence."}]},"reading":{"title":"那盘棋","text":"我学象棋的那一年，输得很惨。教练从不骂人，只是在旁边看着，等一局结束后才问我一句：刚才那一步，你为什么那么走？\n\n有一次，我明明看见对方的马已经跳到了危险的位置，却还是急着去吃一个小兵，结果输了。我很不服气，说运气不好。教练没有责备我，只是把棋盘摆回原来的样子，让我再走一遍，说是让我自己找教训。这一次我看清了：问题不在运气，在于我太想赢，反而忽略了眼前的危险。\n\n那盘棋我记了很多年。后来工作里遇到类似的情况，急着抢一个看起来不错的项目，我竟然会想起那句问话，于是停下来，多观察一会儿。承认自己会犯错并不丢人；真正丢人的是，输了却不知道为什么。","translation":"In the year I learned Chinese chess I lost badly. The coach never scolded anyone. He just watched from the side and, once a game was over, asked me one question: why did you play that move? Once I clearly saw that his knight had already landed in a dangerous square, yet I still rushed to capture a small pawn, and lost. I was not convinced; I said it was bad luck. He did not blame me. He only set the board back the way it was and told me to play it again, saying I should find the lesson myself. This time I saw it: the problem was not luck but that I wanted to win so badly that I ignored the danger in front of me. That game stayed with me for years. Later at work, when I was in a hurry to grab a project that looked good, I would unexpectedly hear that question again, so I stopped and watched a little longer. Admitting you can make a mistake costs you nothing; what really costs you is losing and not knowing why.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["一场正式的象棋比赛","一盘输掉的棋带来的改变","教练怎样教孩子学棋","怎样才能提高象棋水平"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage moves from the lost game and the coach's question to the same habit showing up later at work, so the game's effect on the author is the subject."},{"q":"作者认为那盘棋输掉的主要原因是____。","options":["当天的运气不好","太想赢而忽略了危险","教练事先没有提醒","对手的水平太高"],"answer":1,"explain":"The author says '问题不在运气，在于我太想赢，反而忽略了眼前的危险', which rejects luck and names the real cause."},{"q":"从最后一段可以看出，作者后来对“输”的态度是____。","options":["尽量想办法避免再输","认为输赢一点也不重要","输了也要弄清楚原因","不再参加任何比赛和项目"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing line says the real loss is losing without knowing why, which shows the author wants the reason, not simply the avoidance of defeat."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["那盘象棋我输得很不服气。","教练没有责备我，只让我再走一遍。","我太想赢，反而忽略了眼前的危险。","他一直在旁边观察，一句话也没说。","那次教训让我改掉了急着下结论的习惯。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a mistake you made at work and what you learned by going back over it. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["教训","观察","服气","责备"],"min_chars":90,"model":"刚工作时，我把一份报价单发错了客户，被经理叫去谈话。一开始我不太服气，觉得那只是小错。后来我们把整个过程重新走了一遍，我才发现自己在发送之前从没有观察过附件。那次的教训很简单：发出去以前停三秒，检查收件人和附件。经理没有责备我，只让我把步骤写下来贴在电脑旁边。那张纸我留了三年。","tips":"Set the scene in one sentence, show the moment you looked again instead of defending yourself, and end with the concrete rule you kept."}},{"n":28,"zh":"最受欢迎的毕业生","en":"The most popular graduate","book":2,"theme":"A recruiter looks at only three lines of a CV, and the answer to campus anxiety turns out to be attitude rather than credentials.","grammar":{"id":"g28","point":"简直 / 究竟 / 到底","point_en":"simply, virtually / exactly (what), after all","structure":"简直 + 像/是/不敢/无法 + …… ｜ 究竟/到底 + 疑问词（问句） ｜ 到底 + 毕竟/终于（陈述句）","explain_en":"简直 is an intensifier of comparison, not a question word. It tells the listener that what follows is an extreme way of putting something: 房间里简直像冰库. It almost always needs a partner — 像, 是, 等于, 成了, or a negative verb such as 不敢, 无法, 不敢相信. Without that partner the sentence feels unfinished, which is why a bare 我简直很高兴 sounds wrong. 究竟 and 到底 share one job: pressing a question, 'what exactly, after all'. Both stand before the verb or before the question word: 他究竟为什么辞职？/ 你到底想说什么？ 究竟 is the more written, slightly formal choice and often ends with 呢; 到底 is the everyday spoken one. Only 到底 has a second life outside questions, meaning 'after all, in the end': 他到底还是答应了, or 他到底是个新人，别要求太高. 究竟 has no such use. Position is the same for both — after the subject, before the predicate, never at the very start of a sentence. If your sentence already ends in 吗, do not add 究竟 or 到底: they want a question word such as 为什么, 怎么, 谁, 哪, or a choice between two alternatives, not a yes-or-no question.","common_mistake":"Learners write 简直 with no comparison (我简直很高兴) and use 究竟 in statements to mean 'in the end'. Pair 简直 with 像/是/不敢, and keep 究竟 for questions.","examples":[{"zh":"这间办公室安静得简直像图书馆。","py":"zhè jiān bàn gōng shì ān jìng de jiǎn zhí xiàng tú shū guǎn","en":"This office is so quiet it is simply like a library."},{"zh":"你究竟想让我先做哪一件事？","py":"nǐ jiū jìng xiǎng ràng wǒ xiān zuò nǎ yī jiàn shì","en":"Which task exactly do you want me to do first?"},{"zh":"他到底还是个新人，别对他要求太高。","py":"tā dào dǐ hái shì gè xīn rén bié duì tā yāo qiú tài gāo","en":"He is still a newcomer after all; don't expect too much of him."}],"drills":[{"q":"这份计划改了六遍，我____不敢相信自己看错了日期。","options":["究竟","到底","简直","索性"],"answer":2,"explain":"简直 pairs with 不敢相信 to exaggerate, and that partner is exactly what it needs. 究竟 and 到底 only press questions, and 索性 means 'decided to just', which does not fit here."},{"q":"别急，他____比你早入行五年，经验多一些。","options":["简直","究竟","到底","难道"],"answer":2,"explain":"Here 到底 means 'after all' in a statement, which is its second use. 究竟 has no such use in statements, 简直 would need 像/是/不敢相信, and 难道 needs a rhetorical question."}]},"reading":{"title":"三行简历","text":"上个月的招聘会，我在现场待了一整天。最挤的展位不是工资最高的那家，而是一家做节水设备的小公司。老板亲自坐在桌后，一上午没有停过。\n\n那一届毕业生的就业情况本来就不太好，来的人特别多。老板后来告诉我，收简历时他只看三行：你做过什么，做出过什么结果，你还想学什么。至于学校，他不太在意。他说，很多年轻人把简历写得很漂亮，却说不清自己究竟能解决什么问题；也有些人学校很普通，优势却正好在具体做事上。\n\n我问他：什么样的人你愿意留下？他想了一会儿说：面对问题不逃跑的人。经验缺乏不要紧，技能可以培养，态度培养不了。\n\n回去的路上我一直在想这句话。工作到底需要什么样的人？答案也许比我们想的简单：不是最聪明的，而是能把一件小事真正做完的人。","translation":"At last month's job fair I spent a whole day on site. The busiest stand was not the one paying the most but a small company that makes water-saving equipment. The owner sat behind the table himself and did not stop once all morning. That year's graduates were having a hard time finding work, so the crowd was especially large. The owner later told me that he reads only three lines of a CV: what you have done, what result you produced, and what you still want to learn. As for your school, he does not care much. He said many young people write a beautiful CV but cannot say what problem they can actually solve, while others come from very ordinary schools yet their strength happens to be in getting concrete things done. I asked him what kind of person he wanted to keep. He thought for a moment and said: someone who does not run away when a problem appears. A lack of experience is not a problem; skills can be taught, attitude cannot. On the way home I kept thinking about that sentence. What kind of person does work really need? The answer may be simpler than we think: not the cleverest one, but the one who can actually finish a small job properly.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要说明的是____。","options":["招聘会上哪个展位最挤","小公司怎样提高工资待遇","老板最看重毕业生的什么","一份简历应该写多长"],"answer":2,"explain":"The whole passage is built around the owner's three-line test and his closing comment about attitude, so what he values is the main point."},{"q":"老板看简历时最先看的三行不包括____。","options":["你做过什么","你做出过什么结果","你还想学什么","你毕业于哪所学校"],"answer":3,"explain":"The passage lists the three lines and then says '至于学校，他并不太在意', so the school is explicitly not one of them."},{"q":"从“遇到问题不逃跑的人”这句话可以看出来，老板最看重____。","options":["学历和成绩","经验和人脉","面对问题的态度","说话的能力"],"answer":2,"explain":"He follows the sentence with '态度培养不了', so not running away is a matter of attitude rather than of qualifications."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["那一届毕业生的就业情况比往年难。","我的简历只有一页，写了三行重点。","老板问得很具体，我一时不知道怎么回答。","他最大的优势是遇到问题不逃避。","这份工作有没有前途，要看行业的发展。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write the three lines you would put at the top of your CV and explain why they matter for the job you want. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["简历","优势","具体","前途"],"min_chars":90,"model":"我的简历开头只有三行。第一行写我做过什么：在一家小公司负责过三年的客户维护。第二行写结果：把老客户的流失从每月五家降到一家。第三行写我还想学什么：数据分析。我的优势不是名校，而是能把具体的事情做完。这份工作我看重的是前途，所以愿意从最基础的部分学起。","tips":"Give three short lines rather than a paragraph, put a number in at least one of them, and close with why this role fits your longer plan."}},{"n":29,"zh":"培养对手","en":"Training your rivals","book":2,"theme":"A new stationery shop next door does not finish off the old one: a livelier street brings more customers, and a rival keeps you from getting lazy.","grammar":{"id":"g29","point":"索性 / 干脆 / 不妨","point_en":"simply decided to / just went ahead and / might as well","structure":"索性 + 动词短语（经过犹豫） ｜ 干脆 + 动词短语 / 形容词 ｜ 不妨 + 动词短语（建议）","explain_en":"All three mean something like 'just do it', but they come out of different situations. 索性 marks a decisive move after hesitation, or after other attempts have failed: 等了两个小时也没来车，我们索性走回去. It reports what was actually done, so it belongs with completed actions. 干脆 is close but adds briskness — cutting out the middle steps: 他干脆把整段删了. It is also a plain adjective meaning 'straightforward, no-nonsense' as in 说话很干脆, which 索性 can never be, so 干脆 covers both an adverb and a description of manner. Use 干脆 for a clean, resolute action, and 索性 when you gave up on the reasonable option and did the more drastic thing instead. 不妨 is a different animal: a soft suggestion, 'you might as well, there is no harm in it'. It appears in advice to another person or in 我们 suggestions — 你不妨先打个电话问问 — and it never narrates a finished action. To sum up: 索性 and 干脆 both report what someone did, with 索性 signalling resignation or a last resort and 干脆 signalling a clean decision; 不妨 only proposes something someone could try. All three sit after the subject and before the verb, and none of them takes 了 right after it.","common_mistake":"Learners use 不妨 to report the past (昨天我不妨去了) and 索性 for polite advice. 不妨 only makes suggestions; 索性 reports a decisive action that has already been taken.","examples":[{"zh":"等了半个小时公交车也没来，我们索性走路回家。","py":"děng le bàn gè xiǎo shí gōng jiāo chē yě méi lái wǒ men suǒ xìng zǒu lù huí jiā","en":"We waited half an hour and no bus came, so we simply walked home."},{"zh":"这张表太复杂，他干脆重新做了一份。","py":"zhè zhāng biǎo tài fù zá tā gān cuì chóng xīn zuò le yī fèn","en":"The form was too complicated, so he just made a new one."},{"zh":"你要是拿不定主意，不妨先问问同事。","py":"nǐ yào shì ná bù dìng zhǔ yì bù fáng xiān wèn wèn tóng shì","en":"If you can't decide, you might as well ask a colleague first."}],"drills":[{"q":"在门口等了一个小时也没等到人，我们____打车过去了。","options":["索性","不妨","鉴于","难免"],"answer":0,"explain":"After a failed attempt the speaker reports a decisive action, which is 索性. 不妨 can only offer advice about the future, 鉴于 needs an observed situation at the head of the clause, and 难免 needs a verb phrase predicting a natural result."},{"q":"这个方案还不成熟，你____先找两位老客户试一试。","options":["不妨","索性","到底","竟然"],"answer":0,"explain":"The sentence gives soft advice, which is exactly the job of 不妨. 索性 would report a decisive action already taken and implies earlier hesitation, while 到底 and 竟然 do not fit this slot at all."}]},"reading":{"title":"隔壁的文具店","text":"我家楼下有两家文具店，隔着一条小路，老板都是中年人。左边那家开了十几年，右边的去年才开张。\n\n开张那阵子，邻居们都说，老店这下麻烦了。可奇怪的是，老店的生意并没有垮。有一次我去买电池，正好碰上右边的小老板来问事，老店的老板干脆把进货单拿出来给他看，还告诉他哪家批发商的日用品便宜。\n\n我有点不理解，问他为什么帮对手。他说，这条街以前只有我一家，安静得很，天黑以后没人愿意走过来；现在好了，两家都在，家长会带着孩子一起逛。\n\n原来生意不是一个人吃完的。他说，一条街的利润不能只算自己那一份，两家适当拉开价格，谁也不挤谁。把对手培养起来，街道才有人气，自己也不至于越来越懒。这个道理，他比我们想得远。","translation":"Downstairs from my home there are two stationery shops separated by a narrow path, both run by middle-aged owners. The one on the left has been open for over ten years; the one on the right opened only last year. When it opened, the neighbours all said the old shop was in trouble now. Strangely, the old shop did not collapse. Once, when I went to buy batteries, the young owner from next door happened to come over with a question, and the old owner simply took out his purchase invoices and showed them to him, even telling him which wholesaler sells cheap household goods. I did not quite understand and asked why he helped a rival. He said that for years this street had only his shop, quiet as anything, and after dark nobody wanted to walk down it; now it was better, with both shops there, parents would bring their children to stroll along. So business is not something one person can eat all of. He said the profit on a street cannot be counted as just your own share; if the two shops keep their prices reasonably apart, neither crowds the other out. Train your rival and the street comes alive, and you yourself do not get lazier and lazier. On this point, he saw further than the rest of us.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要说明____。","options":["老店怎样把新店挤走","两家店为什么卖一样的东西","有对手有时反而是好事","邻居之间应该少来往"],"answer":2,"explain":"The old owner's explanation and the closing line about training a rival both make the case that a competitor can help, which is the main idea."},{"q":"老店老板给新店看进货单，是因为他____。","options":["想让新店早点关门","希望整条街热闹起来","以前欠了对方的人情","担心自己的货卖不出去"],"answer":1,"explain":"He explains that a single quiet shop kept people away, while two shops bring families to the street, so a livelier street is his reason."},{"q":"从“自己也不至于越来越懒”可以推出来____。","options":["两家店早晚会合并","有竞争人才不会停下来","老店老板准备退休了","新店很快会搬到别处去"],"answer":1,"explain":"The sentence implies that without a rival the owner would slack off, so competition keeps people working rather than complacent."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["隔壁新开了一家文具店，老板很热心。","老店没有垮，生意反而更好了。","两家店一竞争，整条街都热闹起来。","他干脆把进货的价格告诉了我。","把对手培养起来，对自己也有好处。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a competitor, classmate or colleague who made you better, and what you learned from having them around. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["对手","培养","合理","利益"],"min_chars":90,"model":"刚进公司时，我很怕隔壁组的那位同事，觉得他处处比我快。后来我们一起做一个项目，他做事很干脆，从不拖到最后一刻。我学着他的样子，把每天的任务分成三块。项目结束后我发现，我们的利益其实在一起：客户留住了，两个组都有活干。现在我愿意身边多一些这样的对手，因为合理的关系不是互相消耗，而是互相培养。","tips":"Name the person and the one thing they did better, skip the revenge angle, and end with the habit you copied from them."}},{"n":30,"zh":"竞争让市场更高效","en":"Competition makes the market more efficient","book":2,"theme":"Two delivery teams running the same route show how clear rules turn rivalry into better equipment, cheaper prices and livelier staff.","grammar":{"id":"g30","point":"何必 / 何尝 / 难道 / 岂","point_en":"why bother / have I ever not / surely not / how could it be","structure":"何必 + 动词短语（+ 呢）？ ｜ 何尝 + 不/没有……？ ｜ 难道 + 主语 + 谓语……吗？ ｜ 岂 + 不/能/敢……？","explain_en":"These four are all rhetorical, which means the speaker does not want an answer — they want agreement. 何必 ('why bother') says that an action is unnecessary or not worth the trouble: 只是小问题，何必这么紧张？ It comes before the verb, often with 呢, and it rejects doing something. 何尝 ('have I ever not…') is the subtle one: it uses a negative form to insist that the opposite is true. 我何尝不想去？ means 'of course I want to go'; the surface is a question, the meaning is an assertion. It almost always appears with 不 or 没有 and a question mark, and it is literary in tone. 难道 starts a challenge and expects 'no' as the answer, and it nearly always ends the sentence with 吗 or 不成: 难道你忘了我们的约定吗？ It can front the subject or follow it. 岂 is the most formal and the most compressed: 岂不更好？ 'wouldn't that be even better?', 岂能随便改？ 'how could it be changed just like that?'. It pairs with 不, 能, 敢 or 是 and reads like written argument. All four turn a statement into a challenge or an insistence, and none of them reports a plain fact. Tone is the real difference: 何必 rejects an action, 何尝 reveals a hidden truth, 难道 challenges the listener, 岂 asserts with formal force.","common_mistake":"Learners write 难道 in ordinary statements without 吗, and they read 何必 as 'why not'. 何必 always means the action is unnecessary, and 难道 needs the question frame.","examples":[{"zh":"只是一个小误会，何必说得这么严重？","py":"zhǐ shì yī gè xiǎo wù huì hé bì shuō de zhè me yán zhòng","en":"It was only a small misunderstanding; why make it sound so serious?"},{"zh":"我何尝不想休息，只是这个月实在太忙。","py":"wǒ hé cháng bù xiǎng xiū xi zhǐ shì zhè ge yuè shí zài tài máng","en":"It is not that I don't want a break; this month is simply too busy."},{"zh":"难道你没有收到我昨天发的邮件吗？","py":"nán dào nǐ méi yǒu shōu dào wǒ zuó tiān fā de yóu jiàn ma","en":"Surely you received the email I sent yesterday?"}],"drills":[{"q":"只是晚了十分钟，你____发这么大的火？","options":["何必","何尝","岂","到底"],"answer":0,"explain":"何必 says the reaction is unnecessary and pairs with a bare verb phrase. 何尝 needs 不 or 没有 to insist on a hidden truth, 岂 needs 不/能/敢, and 到底 only presses a question."},{"q":"____你忘了今天下午要交报告吗？","options":["何必","难道","何尝","岂"],"answer":1,"explain":"难道 opens a rhetorical challenge and is completed by 吗 at the end. 何必 needs a verb phrase about an unnecessary action, 何尝 would need 不 or 没有, and 岂 cannot sit before a subject."}]},"reading":{"title":"两条路线","text":"我们公司做生鲜运输，主要把海边的鱼送到城里的饭店。前几年只有一条路线，车队由一位老负责人管，大家早上装货，下午到达，日子过得很和平。\n\n问题也慢慢出来了：设备越来越旧，没有人提；送到的鱼死了一半，也没有人急。因为没有别的车队，饭店只能接受。\n\n去年，老板做了一个让所有人意外的决定：同样的路线，再成立一个小组，两组分别报出每周的成本。消息一出来，两个组的员工都坐不住了。老组第一次主动换了设备，新组把装车的时间缩短了半小时。几个月后，鱼存活的比例提高了很多，价格也降了下来，服务也改善了不少。\n\n难道竞争一定伤感情吗？我看未必。只要规则清楚，它更像一条鲇鱼，让本来安静的沙丁鱼不得不游起来。","translation":"Our company delivers fresh food, mainly carrying fish from the coast to restaurants in the city. For years there was only one route, run by an old manager: everyone loaded in the morning, arrived in the afternoon, and life was peaceful. Then the problems surfaced one by one. The equipment was getting old and nobody raised it; half the fish arrived dead and nobody panicked. With no other fleet around, the restaurants could only accept it. Last year the boss made a decision that surprised everyone: on the same route, set up a second team, and have the two teams each report their weekly cost. The moment the news came out, staff in both teams could not sit still. The old team changed the equipment on its own initiative for the first time, and the new team cut loading time by half an hour. A few months later the share of fish surviving the trip had risen a lot, prices had come down, and the service had improved noticeably. Must competition always hurt feelings? I doubt it. As long as the rules are clear, it works more like a catfish, making the once-quiet sardines swim.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要讲的是____。","options":["怎样把鱼运得更快一些","适度竞争带来的变化","老板为什么要换新设备","饭店怎样降低采购成本"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage describes the quiet monopoly, the boss's decision and the concrete improvements that followed, so the changes brought by competition are the main point."},{"q":"老板做的决定是____。","options":["取消原来的那个车队","把两条路线合并成一条","再成立一个小组跑同样的路线","把鱼的价格提高一半"],"answer":2,"explain":"The third paragraph says the two teams cover the same route and report their weekly costs separately, which is exactly the decision."},{"q":"“它更像一条鲇鱼”这个比喻想说的是____。","options":["竞争会伤害同事之间的感情","竞争能让人保持活力","鱼比人更需要活动空间","新组一定比老组更能干"],"answer":1,"explain":"The catfish makes the sardines swim, and the author says competition does not have to hurt feelings, so the image stands for the energy rivalry creates."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["我们公司负责把海边的鱼运输到城里。","两个组的员工都开始想办法降低成本。","设备换了以后，鱼存活的比例高了很多。","难道竞争一定会伤害感情吗？","只要规则清楚，竞争对大家都有利。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Think of a place where competition made things better for customers — a market, a street of shops, a team. Explain what changed. Use at least three of the words below.","required_words":["商品","改善","活力","有利"],"min_chars":90,"model":"我家附近有一条卖早餐的小街，以前只有一家店，包子常常是凉的，价格也不便宜。后来街口又开了两家，同样的商品，质量差一点就没人买。第一家店很快换了设备，还改善了几种点心的做法。现在整条街都很有活力，早上七点就排起了队。竞争对顾客是有利的，对认真做事的店主也未必是坏事。","tips":"Describe the situation before, the moment a competitor appeared, and one concrete change a customer can see or taste."}},{"n":31,"zh":"登门槛效应","en":"Foot-in-the-door effect","book":2,"theme":"Why a very small first request is often the easiest way to get a larger one accepted, told through a new hire's first month at a newspaper office.","grammar":{"id":"g31","point":"难怪 / 怪不得","point_en":"no wonder; that explains why","structure":"原因 + 难怪/怪不得 + 结果（先知道原因，再说“原来如此”）","explain_en":"Use 难怪 or 怪不得 when you have just learned a reason and it suddenly explains something you had already noticed. The cause comes first — either earlier in the same sentence or in the previous sentence — and what follows the adverb is the fact that is now explained: 难怪你今天这么精神，原来昨晚早睡了。 Both words go immediately before the subject of the clause, never at the end of it, and both can stand alone as a one-word reaction: 难怪！/ 怪不得！ 难怪 is neutral and slightly more written. 怪不得 is the everyday spoken form and often takes 了 or 啊 after it: 怪不得他这么高兴。 难怪 can also be followed by 原来 to spell the cause out. Neither word asks a question and neither means 'strange' — for that, use 奇怪. Compare 难怪 with 原来: 原来 simply reports the newly found fact, while 难怪 adds the speaker's reaction, 'that explains it'. If the clause after the adverb is only a guess rather than something you now understand, use 大概 or 也许 instead.","common_mistake":"Learners often put 难怪 in front of the cause, as in 难怪下雨，他没带伞, when the cause must come first: 他没带伞，难怪淋湿了。 A second slip is using 难怪 to translate 'strange'; 奇怪 is the word for that.","examples":[{"zh":"难怪你今天这么精神，原来昨晚早睡了。","py":"nán guài nǐ jīn tiān zhè me jīng shén yuán lái zuó wǎn zǎo shuì le","en":"No wonder you are so energetic today — you went to bed early last night."},{"zh":"怪不得大家都赞成这个方案，它确实省时间。","py":"guài bu de dà jiā dōu zàn chéng zhè ge fāng àn tā què shí shěng shí jiān","en":"No wonder everyone approves of this plan; it really does save time."},{"zh":"他报告写得那么清楚，难怪经理总让他处理急事。","py":"tā bào gào xiě de nà me qīng chu nán guài jīng lǐ zǒng ràng tā chǔ lǐ jí shì","en":"His reports are so clear that it is no wonder the manager always asks him to handle urgent matters."}],"drills":[{"q":"他连着值了三天班，____今天开会时一直打哈欠。","options":["难怪","难道","反而","简直"],"answer":0,"explain":"难怪 introduces the explanation after a known cause: he worked three night shifts, so the yawning is no surprise. 难道 only appears in rhetorical questions, 反而 marks a contrast with expectation, and 简直 exaggerates a description; none of them means 'no wonder'."},{"q":"____他这么熟悉这条街，原来他在这里住了十年。","options":["不得不","了不起","怪不得","由不得"],"answer":2,"explain":"怪不得 fits the pattern reaction-first, reason-after: the 原来 clause supplies the cause. 不得不 means 'have to', 了不起 is an adjective meaning 'amazing', and 由不得 means 'not up to someone' — all are wrong parts of speech here."}]},"reading":{"title":"第一件小事","text":"刚进报社那年，我被安排给一位老编辑当助手。第一天轮到我值班，他只让我把一段三百字的消息看一遍，回来告诉他有没有错字。事情太小，我没有犹豫就答应了。\n第三天，他让我帮忙处理一封读者来信；一个星期以后，我已经在替他整理短评了。月底总结会上，我看见自己的名字第一次出现在报纸上。同事笑着说，这位编辑最会用这种办法带新人。先给一个很低的门槛，你点了头，后面的事就不觉得难。\n我这才明白，怪不得他从来不催人，也从不勉强谁。那种被信任的感觉，比任何报告都更让人迫切地想把下一步做好。","translation":"The year I joined the newspaper office, I was assigned as an assistant to a senior editor. On my first day on duty, he asked me only to read a three-hundred-character news item and tell him whether there were any typos. The task was so small that I agreed without hesitating.\nOn the third day he asked me to help handle a reader's letter; a week later I was already sorting his short commentaries. At the month-end review meeting I saw my own name in the paper for the first time. A colleague laughed and said this editor was a master at bringing new people along: give them a very low threshold first, and once they nod, the rest no longer feels difficult.\nOnly then did I understand — no wonder he never rushed anyone and never forced anyone. That feeling of being trusted made me more eager to do the next step well than any written report could.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要讲的是____。","options":["一位编辑怎样一步步带新人","报社里如何检查错字","新人怎样写出一篇短评","总结会上如何汇报工作"],"answer":0,"explain":"The passage follows the assistant's tasks from reading a short news item to sorting short commentaries, all arranged by the senior editor, so the focus is his step-by-step way of training a newcomer."},{"q":"作者第一天值班时，被安排做的是____。","options":["替编辑写一篇短评","在总结会上发言","把一段消息看一遍","处理一封读者来信"],"answer":2,"explain":"The first paragraph says that on his first day on duty he was asked to read a three-hundred-character news item and report whether there were any typos."},{"q":"从文章最后一段看，作者对老编辑的做法____。","options":["有些反感","十分赞成","保持怀疑","不太理解"],"answer":1,"explain":"The closing sentence says the trust made him eager to do the next step well, and he uses 怪不得 to show he now understands the method — clear approval rather than doubt."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["他值班的时候从来不接私人电话。","社区请我帮忙处理一份报告。","我没有犹豫就答应了这件事。","他劝我先实践一个月再作决定。","那位编辑说话很谦虚，也不轻易批评人。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe a small first step at work that later led to something bigger. What did you hesitate about, what did you agree to, and what changed afterwards? Use the words below.","required_words":["犹豫","处理","报告","实践"],"min_chars":80,"model":"上个月主管让我试着处理客户来信。我有些犹豫，怕自己写不好。第一封只有两百字，我改了三遍才发出去；两周后我独立写了一份报告，才发现最难的是开头那一步。这件事让我更愿意在实践中学习，也让我明白：把小事做好，后面的路自然会宽一点。","tips":"Start with the request and your hesitation, add one concrete detail about the first small task, then close with what that first step changed in your attitude."}},{"n":32,"zh":"身边的环保","en":"Protecting the environment around us","book":2,"theme":"How one office recycling box turned sceptical colleagues into careful users, and why local habits matter more than grand slogans.","grammar":{"id":"g32","point":"甚至 / 乃至 / 以至于","point_en":"even; and even; so much so that","structure":"甚至 + 极端例子；乃至 + 书面并列项；……，以至于 + 结果","explain_en":"All three push an idea to an extreme, but they work at different levels. 甚至 means 'even' and adds a surprisingly extreme example to what has just been said. It stands before the example, often with 都 or 也 later in the clause: 他甚至周末也来加班。 It can link words, phrases or whole clauses, in speech and in writing.\n乃至 is the written, formal cousin of 甚至. It normally joins items inside one phrase or list, and it sounds odd introducing a full result clause: 工厂乃至每一个家庭都受到影响。\n以至于 means 'to such an extent that' and introduces a consequence. Before it you need a stated degree or a repeated action; after it comes the result, usually something unintended: 他连着熬了一个月，以至于把开会的时间都记错了。 Do not use 以至于 for a simple cause — that is 因为 — and unlike 甚至 it cannot join two nouns.\nSo: 甚至 adds an extreme case, 乃至 lists extreme cases in formal prose, and 以至于 reports where an extreme situation led.","common_mistake":"A common error is using 以至于 without any stated extent, as in 我很累，以至于想睡觉, and using 甚至 where the second part is a consequence rather than an added example.","examples":[{"zh":"这条河里连小鱼都看不见，甚至水草也很少了。","py":"zhè tiáo hé lǐ lián xiǎo yú dōu kàn bu jiàn shèn zhì shuǐ cǎo yě hěn shǎo le","en":"In this river you cannot even see small fish, and even the water weeds have become scarce."},{"zh":"一座城市的能源供应，会影响到工厂乃至每一个家庭。","py":"yí zuò chéng shì de néng yuán gōng yìng huì yǐng xiǎng dào gōng chǎng nǎi zhì měi yí ge jiā tíng","en":"A city's energy supply affects everything from factories down to every single household."},{"zh":"他连续加班一个月，以至于连周末是哪一天都忘了。","py":"tā lián xù jiā bān yí ge yuè yǐ zhì yú lián zhōu mò shì nǎ yì tiān dōu wàng le","en":"He worked overtime for a month straight, to the point that he forgot which day the weekend was."}],"drills":[{"q":"这道题连老师都想了很久，____用了三种方法才算出来。","options":["甚至","至于","关于","由于"],"answer":0,"explain":"甚至 adds the extreme case: even the teacher needed three methods. 至于 changes the topic, 关于 means 'about', and 由于 gives a cause; none of them can add an extreme example here."},{"q":"他连着一个月熬夜赶方案，____把开会的时间记错了。","options":["因为","虽然","以至于","不但"],"answer":2,"explain":"The clause before the blank states the extent (a whole month of late nights) and what follows is its unintended result, which is exactly what 以至于 introduces. 因为 and 虽然 need paired clauses, and 不但 must be followed by 而且 or 还."}]},"reading":{"title":"楼里的分类箱","text":"去年春天，公司在一楼放了一台分类回收箱。开始没人当真，有人把没喝完的咖啡连杯子一起扔进去，墙上的说明也很少有人看。我也觉得这种事离自己太远，甚至有点麻烦。忙起来连说明都懒得看，以至于箱子放了半年，还有同事不知道它在那儿。\n三个月后，行政部公布了一组数据：整栋楼的用电量比前一年少了百分之九，废纸回收量多了一倍。数字不算大，却足够真实。大家开始自觉关灯，打印前也会多想一下；行政部还逐步把走廊的旧灯换成了节能的设施。\n最让我意外的是保洁阿姨。她每天把纸箱压平捆好，说这些资源扔了太可惜。现在出差住酒店，我也会先找一找回收箱。宏大的事离我们很远，可身边的小选择都在悄悄影响以后。每个人做一点贡献，加起来就不一样。","translation":"Last spring the company put a sorting and recycling bin on the ground floor. At first nobody took it seriously. Some people threw their half-finished coffee in, cup and all, and few bothered to read the notice on the wall. I also felt this kind of thing was far away from me, even a bit of a nuisance; when work got busy I could not be bothered to read the notice either, so much so that after six months some colleagues still did not know the bin was there.\nThree months later, the admin department published a set of figures: the whole building used nine percent less electricity than the year before, and paper recycling had doubled. The numbers were not large, but they were real enough. People began switching off lights without being asked and thinking twice before printing; the admin department also gradually replaced the old corridor lights with energy-saving fixtures.\nWhat surprised me most was the cleaning lady. Every day she flattened the cardboard boxes and tied them up, saying it would be a shame to throw such resources away. Now when I stay in a hotel on a business trip, I look for the recycling bin first. Grand events are far away from us, but the small choices around us quietly shape what comes next. Everyone making a small contribution adds up.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["公司如何减少员工的加班时间","酒店怎样处理用过的旧纸箱","办公室里一项环保习惯慢慢形成","行政部更换走廊灯的全过程"],"answer":2,"explain":"The passage moves from the new bin and people's indifference to the published figures and the changed daily habits, so the main thread is how one environmental habit gradually took hold."},{"q":"行政部公布的数据显示，整栋楼的用电量比前一年____。","options":["增加了一倍","减少了百分之九","基本没有变化","减少了大约一半"],"answer":1,"explain":"The second paragraph says the building used nine percent less electricity than the previous year (少了百分之九), while the amount of recycled waste paper doubled."},{"q":"从保洁阿姨的做法可以看出，她____。","options":["真心爱惜这些资源","只是应付上级检查","觉得分类箱很麻烦","对回收并不了解"],"answer":0,"explain":"She flattens and ties the boxes every day and says it would be a shame to waste such resources, which shows genuine care rather than reluctance or ignorance."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["公司上个月公布了新的用电数据。","大家逐步养成了自觉关灯的习惯。","节约能源其实可以从关空调做起。","这些旧的办公设施还能继续使用。","下雨天尽量少开车，尾气会少一些。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe one small environmental habit your workplace could adopt. Say what it is, what resistance it met at first, and what changed. Use the words below.","required_words":["数据","自觉","资源","公布"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我们部门从三月开始做垃圾分类。起初没人愿意，连我自己也觉得麻烦。行政部把每个月的用电数据公布在门口，大家看见曲线往下走，态度慢慢变了。现在关灯、双面打印都成了习惯，纸箱也会自觉压平。资源省下来了，办公室反而更整洁。","tips":"Open with the habit and the initial resistance, add one concrete detail such as the printed figures, then close with the change you can see today."}},{"n":33,"zh":"以堵治堵—缓解交通有妙招","en":"Treating congestion with congestion: A smart way to relieve traffic burden","book":2,"theme":"Why removing a convenient left turn made a busy junction faster, and what that teaches about solving problems by subtraction.","grammar":{"id":"g33","point":"并非 / 并不是","point_en":"is not (in fact); not A but B","structure":"并非/并不是 + A + （而是/只是）+ B","explain_en":"并非 and 并不是 both deny something in a firm, slightly corrective way: 'it is not in fact the case that...'. The 并 adds the sense of 'contrary to what you might assume'. They come before the thing being denied, and they are very often followed by 而是, 只是 or 不过是, which supplies the real explanation: 这次问题的原因并非车太多，而是路口设计不合理。 / 他并不是不想帮忙，只是手上还有别的事。\n并不是 is the everyday form and can deny almost anything in speech. 并非 is shorter, more formal and more written; it also appears alone in the fixed phrase 并非如此. Both can deny a noun, a verb phrase or a whole clause. Do not confuse 并非 with 并不: 并不 is an adverb that negates verbs and adjectives (并不容易, 并不想), while 并非 negates the verb 是 or stands before a noun phrase. 并非 is not simply a louder 不是 — the extra meaning is the correction of an assumption, so the sentence usually expects a follow-up that says what is actually true.","common_mistake":"Learners write 并非 directly before an adjective or a plain verb, as in 并非容易 or 并非知道; use 并不容易 and 并不知道 instead. They also forget that the 而是 or 只是 clause is usually the real point of the sentence.","examples":[{"zh":"这次拥堵的原因并非车太多，而是路口的安排不合理。","py":"zhè cì yōng dǔ de yuán yīn bìng fēi chē tài duō ér shì lù kǒu de ān pái bù hé lǐ","en":"The cause of this congestion is not too many cars but poor planning at the junction."},{"zh":"他取消会议并不是因为不重视，而是时间实在排不开。","py":"tā qǔ xiāo huì yì bìng bú shì yīn wèi bù zhòng shì ér shì shí jiān shí zài pái bu kāi","en":"He cancelled the meeting not because he does not care, but because his schedule truly could not be rearranged."},{"zh":"问题并非无法解决，只是需要多花一点时间。","py":"wèn tí bìng fēi wú fǎ jiě jué zhǐ shì xū yào duō huā yì diǎn shí jiān","en":"The problem is not unsolvable; it simply needs a little more time."}],"drills":[{"q":"这次事故的原因____司机不小心，而是路面太滑。","options":["并非","并不","并没","并非不"],"answer":0,"explain":"The frame 并非……而是…… denies a noun phrase and then gives the real cause. 并不 and 并没 can only negate verbs or adjectives, and 并非不 is a double negative that reverses the meaning."},{"q":"新规定____要限制大家，只是想让流程更清楚。","options":["并非不","并不是","并不曾","不是不"],"answer":1,"explain":"并不是要……只是…… corrects an assumption and then explains the real purpose. 并非不 and 不是不 are double negatives, and 并不曾 means 'never did', which clashes with a present purpose."}]},"reading":{"title":"路口的那条左转线","text":"我们公司门口那条路，早晚高峰总是堵得厉害。路口只有两条车道，左转的车一多，直行的队伍就排到广场边上。大家都说，路太窄，唯一的办法是把面积扩大。交通部门来社区咨询时，一位工程师却提出了相反的想法：取消左转，让车多绕几百米。\n方案公布以后，同事们纷纷摇头，觉得这个主意太主观。第一个月，抱怨不少，甚至有人打电话去投诉。可到了第二个月，数据变了：直行的通行时间缩短了近四成，拥挤明显缓解，行人也敢过马路了。\n工程师解释说，挡住整条路的其实是那几辆左转车。把左转线去掉，看起来更堵，实际上是把路面留给了大多数人。这个道理并非人人都能想到，只是需要一点勇气去试。现在那条路照常繁忙，只是队伍短了很多。","translation":"The road outside our company gate is always badly jammed at rush hour. The junction has only two lanes, and as soon as a few cars turn left, the queue going straight backs up to the edge of the square. Everyone said the road was too narrow and the only answer was to enlarge the area. When the traffic department came to consult the community, a young engineer proposed the opposite idea: ban the left turn and make cars drive a few hundred metres further.\nAfter the plan was announced, colleagues shook their heads, feeling the idea was too subjective. In the first month there were plenty of complaints, and some people even phoned in to object. But by the second month the figures had changed: the time needed to go straight was cut by nearly forty percent, the crowding eased noticeably, and pedestrians dared to cross again.\nThe engineer explained that the real blockage was those few left-turning cars. Removing the left-turn lane looks like making things more congested, but actually it gives the road back to the majority. This idea is not something everyone thinks of — it just takes a little courage to try. The road is as busy as ever now, but the queue is much shorter.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要介绍的是____。","options":["一条马路扩宽工程的全过程","一个用限制来缓解拥堵的办法","交通部门如何招聘工程师","公司班车路线的调整方案"],"answer":1,"explain":"The whole passage is built around the engineer's counter-intuitive proposal, the objections it met, and the improvement in travel time — a way of relieving congestion by restricting one movement."},{"q":"工程师提出的办法是____。","options":["把路口面积扩大一倍","禁止行人过马路","增加一条公交车道","取消路口的左转"],"answer":3,"explain":"The first paragraph quotes the engineer's proposal directly: cancel the left turn and let cars drive a few hundred metres more."},{"q":"从同事们第一个月的反应看，他们____。","options":["早就期待这次改变","完全赞成工程师","对新方案抱有怀疑","认为数据不够真实"],"answer":2,"explain":"They shook their heads, complained, and some even called to object, which shows doubt about the proposal rather than support."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这条路一到早上就特别拥挤。","取消左转以后，拥堵明显缓解了。","行人和骑车的人共用一条通道。","广场旁边的停车场周末照常开放。","新方案要经过批准才能开始实施。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write a short proposal for one small change at work or in your neighbourhood. Name the usual assumption, then offer a different solution and its likely effect. Use the words below.","required_words":["拥挤","缓解","取消","期待"],"min_chars":80,"model":"楼下的早餐店每天都很拥挤，排队的人一直站到门口。店长原想扩大店面，可他算过数据才发现，真正慢的是结账。上个月他取消了两种现做的点心，队伍短了一半，拥挤的情况缓解了不少。现在老顾客都很期待他再改一改。","tips":"State the familiar assumption in one sentence, then present your different solution, add a concrete detail such as a figure or a time saved, and close with the result."}},{"n":34,"zh":"鸟儿的护肤术","en":"How birds take care of their feathers","book":2,"theme":"A balcony sparrow's grooming routine, read as a lesson in small daily maintenance rather than mere instinct.","grammar":{"id":"g34","point":"再……不过 / 没有比……更……","point_en":"couldn't be more; nothing is more ... than ...","structure":"再 + 形容词 + 不过（+ 了）；没有比 + A + 更 + 形容词 + 的（+ 了）","explain_en":"Both patterns push a quality to its maximum, but they are built differently. 再……不过 is a fixed frame: 再 + adjective + 不过, optionally with 了. It works like a strong 'extremely' and usually evaluates a situation rather than comparing two things: 这个时间再合适不过了。 Only a small set of evaluative adjectives fit comfortably (好, 合适, 简单, 清楚, 方便); you do not put 很 or 非常 inside the frame.\n没有比……更…… is a real comparison. It names the thing you are comparing with after 比, then the quality after 更, and the phrase usually ends with 的 or 了: 没有比这个更清楚的办法了。 The 更 is obligatory — without it the sentence is incomplete. The item after 比 can be a person, a time, a place or an action.\nUse 再……不过 for a quick verdict on a plan or an occasion, and 没有比……更…… when you want the comparison to be visible. Neither pattern is used to ask a question, and neither takes 是 before the adjective.","common_mistake":"The usual errors are dropping 更 from 没有比……更…… (as in 没有比这个好), keeping 很 or 非常 inside 再……不过 (as in 再好很不过), and reading 不过 as the conjunction 'but' rather than as part of the frame.","examples":[{"zh":"这件事交给你再合适不过了。","py":"zhè jiàn shì jiāo gěi nǐ zài hé shì bú guò le","en":"This task could not be in better hands than yours."},{"zh":"对刚学打字的人来说，这个输入法再简单不过。","py":"duì gāng xué dǎ zì de rén lái shuō zhè ge shū rù fǎ zài jiǎn dān bú guò","en":"For someone just learning to type, this input method could not be simpler."},{"zh":"对我们来说，没有比按时下班更让人高兴的事了。","py":"duì wǒ men lái shuō méi yǒu bǐ àn shí xià bān gèng ràng rén gāo xìng de shì le","en":"For us there is nothing more pleasing than leaving work on time."}],"drills":[{"q":"周末去公园看鸟____了，天气预报说这两天都是晴天。","options":["再好很过","比再好","再好不过","更不过好"],"answer":2,"explain":"The fixed frame is 再 + adjective + 不过, so 再好不过了 is the only grammatical option. The others either insert 很 inside the frame or reorder 比 and 更, which the pattern does not allow."},{"q":"对一个刚入职的新人来说，没有比遇到耐心的师傅____的事了。","options":["更幸运","很幸运","最幸运","太幸运"],"answer":0,"explain":"The frame 没有比……更…… requires 更 before the adjective. 很, 最 and 太 cannot fill that slot after 比, so only 更幸运 completes the comparison."}]},"reading":{"title":"羽毛的日常","text":"阳台上一直放着一个浅盘子，我常往里倒一点水。夏天最热的时候，麻雀会跳进去，把翅膀张开，反复拍打，水花溅得到处都是。洗完了，它站在栏杆上，用嘴一下一下地整理羽毛，动作很像人用梳子梳头。\n鸟爱惜羽毛的程度，超出很多人的想象。羽毛光滑，既能保暖，又能挡水；没有它，鸟既飞不上天空，也熬不过干燥的季节。所以它们一有空就整理，发现寄生虫就马上处理。有的鸟还会把蚂蚁放在翅膀下面，借蚂蚁的气味赶走小虫。\n我原以为这只是本能，后来才明白，这更像一种保养：每天花几分钟，把最重要的东西照顾好。对一只鸟来说，没有比羽毛更值得花时间的东西了。人其实也一样。","translation":"A shallow dish has always sat on my balcony, and I often pour a little water into it. On the hottest summer days a sparrow will hop in, spread its wings, and beat them again and again until water splashes everywhere. When it has finished, it stands on the railing and tidies its feathers with its beak, one stroke at a time, much as a person combs their hair.\nBirds treasure their feathers far more than most people imagine. Feathers are smooth and keep the bird both warm and dry; without them a bird could neither fly up into the sky nor survive the dry season. So whenever they have a moment, they groom, and they deal with parasites at once. Some birds even tuck ants under their wings and use the ants' smell to drive away tiny insects.\nI used to think this was pure instinct, but later I understood it is closer to maintenance: a few minutes a day spent looking after the thing that matters most. For a bird there is nothing more worth the time than its feathers. People are much the same.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["阳台上的盘子该怎么摆放","鸟怎样照顾自己的羽毛","麻雀和蚂蚁之间的合作","人应该怎样在家里养鸟"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage describes the sparrow bathing, tidying its feathers, and dealing with parasites, then draws the parallel with human maintenance — the focus is feather care."},{"q":"鸟洗完澡以后会____。","options":["把盘子里的水喝光","用肥皂清洗翅膀","站在栏杆上整理羽毛","飞到树上睡一觉"],"answer":2,"explain":"The first paragraph says that after washing, the bird stands on the railing and tidies its feathers with its beak."},{"q":"作者写这篇文章，主要想____。","options":["借鸟的习性谈日常保养","介绍一种少见的鸟类","说明阳台应该怎样布置","提醒大家不要养鸟"],"answer":0,"explain":"The last paragraph explicitly turns the bird's routine into a point about people: daily maintenance of what matters most, which is the author's real purpose."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["小鸟站在栏杆上反复整理翅膀。","它的羽毛又光滑又干净。","每天花几分钟保养自己很重要。","洗完澡以后，它看起来痛快多了。","这个秘密他一直没有告诉别人。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Describe an object or a daily habit you maintain carefully. Say what you do, why others find it excessive, and what it gives you back. Use the words below.","required_words":["保养","反复","爱惜","秘密"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我有一把用了六年的剪刀，每次用完都擦干净，放回抽屉。朋友笑我太爱惜，我却觉得这是最简单的保养。工具反复使用，总会有磨损；花两分钟照顾它，它就能多陪你几年。这个秘密其实不新鲜，只是很少人愿意坚持。","tips":"Name the object or habit, describe the small routine in detail, mention the mild teasing you get, then close with what the habit actually gives you."}},{"n":35,"zh":"植物会出汗","en":"Plants also sweat","book":2,"theme":"How leaves quietly release water all afternoon, and what that small system teaches about cooling down and keeping balance.","grammar":{"id":"g35","point":"差点儿 / 好不容易","point_en":"almost; barely; with great difficulty","structure":"差点儿 + 动词/形容词（+ 了）；好不容易（才）+ 动词","explain_en":"差点儿 marks a situation that came very close to happening. With something unwanted, it means the event did not happen: 路上很滑，他差点儿摔倒 (he nearly fell but stayed on his feet). With something wanted, it usually means the chance was missed: 我差点儿赶上那班车 often implies I did not catch it. Adding 没 flips the reading for wanted events — 差点儿没赶上 means I did catch it — which is why clear context matters.\n好不容易 means 'with great difficulty' and praises the effort behind a result. It sits before the verb, very often with 才: 我好不容易才找到停车位。 The 才 is not compulsory, but it makes the struggle explicit. 好容易 means exactly the same thing despite looking opposite; 很容易 is the real opposite.\n差点儿 describes what almost happened and usually refers to a single event. 好不容易 describes how a completed action was finally achieved. Do not mix them: 差点儿买到票 suggests you probably did not get the ticket, while 好不容易买到票 means you did get it and it was hard work.","common_mistake":"Learners over-correct 差点儿 for bad events: 差点儿没摔倒 does not mean 'did not nearly fall' — it still says the fall almost happened. They also use 好不容易 as an adjective meaning 'difficult' (这件事好不容易), where 不容易 is the right form.","examples":[{"zh":"路面很滑，他差点儿摔倒。","py":"lù miàn hěn huá tā chà diǎnr shuāi dǎo","en":"The road was slippery and he nearly fell."},{"zh":"我好不容易才在附近找到一个停车位。","py":"wǒ hǎo bù róng yì cái zài fù jìn zhǎo dào yí ge tíng chē wèi","en":"I had a hard time finding a parking space nearby."},{"zh":"这次测验他差点儿就及格了，只差两分。","py":"zhè cì cè yàn tā chà diǎnr jiù jí gé le zhǐ chà liǎng fēn","en":"He almost passed this test, missing it by only two points."}],"drills":[{"q":"路上堵得厉害，我____才赶上九点的会议。","options":["好不容易","好容易不","很容易","不容易地"],"answer":0,"explain":"好不容易（才）…… describes a result achieved with difficulty, which matches the heavy traffic. 很容易 means the opposite, and the other two are not valid forms."},{"q":"他下楼时脚下一滑，____摔倒。","options":["差不多","一点儿","差点","差点儿"],"answer":3,"explain":"差点儿 + a verb marks something that very nearly happened. 差不多 means 'about' or 'almost' in quantity, 一点儿 is a quantity expression, and 差点 cannot stand alone as an adverb."}]},"reading":{"title":"叶子的汗","text":"夏天的午后，你从树荫下走过，会不会觉得那里比马路上凉快？这不只是因为太阳被挡住了。树叶一直在悄悄工作：它们从根部吸收水分，再把水送到枝干和叶梢。\n水最后从叶子上的小孔跑出去，这个过程叫蒸腾。它有点像人的汗腺。天热的时候，水分从毛孔冒出来，带走一部分热量，身体就能慢慢恢复舒服的状态。植物没有肌肉，不会自己走到荫凉的地方歇一歇，但它有一套系统，能自动控制水分的释放。\n有人做过测验：一片成熟的叶子，一天蒸腾掉的水比它自己的重量还多。所以树林里的空气总是湿润的。那天下班晚，我差点儿错过观察的时间；好不容易等到一片云飘过，才看清叶面上细细的水痕。下次你觉得热，不妨看看身边的树，它们正用你看不见的方式给自己降温。","translation":"On a summer afternoon, when you walk through the shade of a tree, does it feel cooler than the road? That is not only because the sun is blocked. The leaves have been working quietly all along: they absorb water through the roots and send it up to the branches and the tips of the twigs.\nThe water finally escapes through tiny holes in the leaf, and this process is called transpiration. It works a little like human sweat glands. On a hot day water comes out through the pores, carries some of the heat away, and the body gradually returns to a comfortable state. Plants have no muscles and cannot walk over to a shady spot to rest, but they have a system that automatically controls how much water they release.\nSomeone once ran a test: a single mature leaf can give off more water in a day than its own weight. That is why the air in a wood is always moist. I finished work late that day and almost missed the best time to watch; it took me a long while to wait for a cloud to pass so that I could see the fine streaks of water on the leaf surface. Next time you feel hot, take a look at the tree beside you — it is cooling itself in a way you cannot see.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要说明的是____。","options":["夏天为什么应该多喝凉开水","植物怎样通过蒸腾给自己降温","树荫和马路的温度差别有多大","叶子上的小孔是怎样形成的"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage explains how roots take up water, how it leaves through the leaf, and why that cools the plant — transpiration is the central idea."},{"q":"水从叶子跑出去的过程叫____。","options":["吸收","循环","蒸腾","呼吸"],"answer":2,"explain":"The second paragraph names the process directly: water leaves through small holes in the leaf and this is called 蒸腾."},{"q":"作者提到人的汗腺，是为了____。","options":["帮助读者理解植物的蒸腾","说明人比植物更怕热","证明夏天应该多喝水","比较人和植物的体温"],"answer":0,"explain":"The sweat gland comparison is introduced with 有点像 and is used to make the unfamiliar process of transpiration easier to picture, not to compare the two bodies' temperatures."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["植物的根一直在吸收水分。","天热的时候，叶子会释放水分。","树荫下的空气往往比较湿润。","这个系统能自动控制水的多少。","我差点儿忘了今天下午的测验。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Explain one simple everyday science idea to a colleague who has never thought about it. Keep the tone practical, and give one concrete example. Use the words below.","required_words":["吸收","控制","恢复","常识"],"min_chars":80,"model":"夏天办公室的空调总开得太低，很多人下午反而没有精神。身体需要一点时间恢复，温度变化太快并不好。我在茶水间贴了一张小纸条：小口喝温水，身体吸收得更好，也能控制住忽冷忽热。这些只是常识，可真正做到的人不多。","tips":"Start with the everyday observation your colleague will recognise, explain the simple mechanism in two or three short sentences, then end with one practical suggestion."}},{"n":36,"zh":"老舍与养花","en":"Lao She and his flowers","book":2,"theme":"What a few pots of chrysanthemums on a balcony teach about patience, small daily care and the pleasure of sharing.","grammar":{"id":"g36","point":"值得 / 便于 / 善于 / 勇于","point_en":"be worth; make it easy to; be good at; be brave enough to","structure":"值得/便于/善于/勇于 + 动词短语","explain_en":"These four are verb-like words that take another verb phrase after them, and each adds a different judgement. 值得 means 'be worth it': 值得花时间, 值得一试. The thing after it is an action whose value you are endorsing. It also works with verbs of deserving when the subject is a person or thing — 值得信赖, 值得尊敬 — but it never takes a bare adjective: say 很值得, not 值得很.\n便于 means 'make it convenient to' and usually follows a measure or an arrangement, explaining what that arrangement makes easier: 把常用文件放在桌边，便于随时查找。 It describes the purpose of a set-up, not a personal skill.\n善于 means 'be good at' and points to a method or a way of handling people and situations: 善于安排时间, 善于沟通。 擅长 is close, but it is used more for trained skills and often takes a noun (擅长画画).\n勇于 means 'have the courage to' and is formal and approving. It introduces something risky but admirable: 勇于承认错误, 勇于尝试。 敢于 is stronger and more neutral; 勇于 sounds like praise.\nAll four normally take a verb phrase rather than a bare noun; 便于 in particular describes an arrangement, not a personal skill.","common_mistake":"Learners say 值得很 for 'very worth it', or put a bare noun after 善于 without a verb (善于英语). They also use 勇于 for trivial actions, where 敢于 or 愿意 sounds more natural.","examples":[{"zh":"这份报告值得再花半天时间修改。","py":"zhè fèn bào gào zhí dé zài huā bàn tiān shí jiān xiū gǎi","en":"This report is worth another half day of revision."},{"zh":"常用文件放在桌边，便于随时查找。","py":"cháng yòng wén jiàn fàng zài zhuō biān biàn yú suí shí chá zhǎo","en":"Keeping frequently used files at the edge of the desk makes them easy to find at any time."},{"zh":"他善于安排时间，也勇于承认自己的错误。","py":"tā shàn yú ān pái shí jiān yě yǒng yú chéng rèn zì jǐ de cuò wù","en":"He is good at managing his time and brave enough to admit his own mistakes."}],"drills":[{"q":"这套工具放在门口，____取用。","options":["便于","值得","善于","勇于"],"answer":0,"explain":"便于 links a placement to the convenience it creates, here 'easy to take and use'. 值得 judges value, while 善于 and 勇于 describe people's abilities, not where tools are kept."},{"q":"这个习惯要坚持下去，很____。","options":["便于","善于","值得","勇于"],"answer":2,"explain":"值得 can end a short evaluative sentence meaning 'worth doing'. The other three all need a following verb phrase and cannot sit at the end of the sentence like this."}]},"reading":{"title":"阳台上的菊花","text":"搬进这套房子时，阳台是空的。我从菜市场捡回两个旧花盆，又买了三盆菊花，摆在窗边。起初只是想让屋里多一点颜色，没想到一年以后，我成了这栋楼里最会浇水的人。\n养花没有想象中轻松。夏天暴雨来得急，盆里的土总是潮湿的，根就会烂；冬天屋里干燥，该浇的时候不能拖，不然叶子容易发黄。我慢慢熟练了，也学会了看天气：天热时早晚各浇一次，天冷了就少浇。施肥也有讲究，多了烧根，少了不开花；花盆垫高一点，便于排水。这些经验，都是在一个个失败的周末里攒下来的。\n去年秋天，第一朵菊花开的那个早上，我在阳台上站了很久。那种开心很难跟别人解释，反正就是觉得日子有了回报。养花值得花时间，也让我学会了等待。现在邻居路过，总问我能不能分几枝，我总是很乐意分享。","translation":"When I moved into this flat, the balcony was empty. I picked up two old flowerpots from the market, bought three pots of chrysanthemums and set them by the window. At first I only wanted a little more colour in the room; a year later I had become the best waterer in the building.\nGrowing flowers is less easy than it looks. Summer rainstorms come fast and the soil in the pots stays damp, so the roots rot; indoors in winter the air is dry, and watering cannot be put off, otherwise the leaves soon turn yellow. I gradually learned to read the weather: water morning and evening on hot days, less when it turns cold. Fertilising has its rules too — too much burns the roots, too little means no flowers; I raised the pots on bricks so the water drains away easily. All of this I gathered over a series of failed weekends.\nLast autumn, on the morning the first chrysanthemum opened, I stood on the balcony for a long time. That kind of happiness is hard to explain to anyone else; it simply felt as though the days had paid me back. Growing flowers is worth the time, and it has taught me to wait. Now when neighbours pass by they ask whether they can have a few stems, and I am always happy to share.","questions":[{"q":"这篇文章主要写的是____。","options":["菜市场里的花应该怎样挑选","作者养菊花的过程和感受","邻居之间如何互相帮助","阳台装修需要注意什么"],"answer":1,"explain":"The passage follows the balcony from empty pots to the first flower and ends with sharing stems, so it is about the process of growing chrysanthemums and how it felt."},{"q":"作者说夏天暴雨过后，盆里的土总是潮湿的，这样会让____。","options":["花开得更早","叶子变红","土变得很干","根烂掉"],"answer":3,"explain":"The second paragraph states that after a summer rainstorm the soil in the pots stays damp, and the roots rot (根就会烂)."},{"q":"从最后一段看，作者认为养花最大的收获是____。","options":["省下了买花的钱","认识了整栋楼的邻居","学会了耐心和分享","把阳台装饰得更漂亮"],"answer":2,"explain":"The closing lines say growing flowers made the author good at waiting and happy to give stems to neighbours, which points to patience and sharing rather than money or decoration."}]},"listening":{"dictation":["这盆菊花需要每天浇水。","暴雨过后，花盆里积了很多水。","施肥不能太多，不然叶子会发黄。","她把多出来的花分享给邻居。","养花让我的生活多了不少乐趣。"]},"writing":{"prompt":"Write about a hobby or routine that rewards patience. Describe how you started, one difficulty you hit, and what you get from it now. Use the words below.","required_words":["养","乐趣","熟练","分享"],"min_chars":80,"model":"我在阳台上养了几盆菊花，开始连浇水都不熟练，不是太多就是太少。后来我每天记下天气和土的干湿，慢慢摸出了规律。花开的时候，我把照片分享给同事，大家都说好看。养花最大的乐趣，是看着一件小事一天天变好。","tips":"Open with how the hobby started, describe one concrete difficulty and how you fixed it, then close with the pleasure it gives you now."}}];
